{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1477124-clan-tzimisce-is-the-least-interesting-clan","id":1477124,"title":"Clan tzimisce is the least interesting clan","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2022-03-23T15:36:54-07:00","id":1477124,"title":"Clan tzimisce is the least interesting clan","content":"In my opinion the least interesting clan has to be clan tzimisce, other than vicissitude there's not much going for them. Without vicissitude they're a discount, venture. Sure they have koldunic sorcery, but at this point everyone and their mother knows blood sorcery. And honestly vicissitude in itself isn't that interesting either, sure you can manipulate flesh and bone, but that's it. First dot is insanely useful though.<br /> <br /> I will admit that Kupala is pretty interesting, but that's about it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"https://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://www.nodiatis.com/pub/18.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27313-hello","name":"Hello","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27313_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-23T17:02:34-07:00","id":1477134,"title":"","content":"Tzimisce are a clan of largely unrealized potential. Sadly, this is due to both a lack of vision on the part of the writers and many gamers.<br /> <br /> Their clan weakness anchors them to an area mechanically rather than just having fluff state that vampires dwell in cities or near civilization. There seems to be very little fluff focus on managing societies of mortals.<br /> <br /> Their ability to craft flesh by discipline or kuldonic sorcery means they can be played as horde faction, but that isn't allowed post Masquerade era. I bet very few STs have run games where Tzimisce and Nosferatu go full out minion army warfare, an army of vozhd verses limitless masses of mutant vermin wiping out whole cities as collateral damage. If vampiric kaiju battles are uninteresting.... I don't know what to suggest.<br /> <br /> Kuldonic sorcery is better magic than several Thaumaturgy paths and allow for the whole Element Bender flavor, but the fluff says only the rarest elders of the clan are well versed in such things.<br /> <br /> I find that when a clan/bloodline is uninteresting, it usually means it lends itself to a game style or play style the person doesn't favor or perhaps doesn't even think of.<br /> <br /> Don't get me wrong though, I have had my fill of players who make a Tzimisce character just to recreate a hentai body horror scene because they are trying to be edgy or are just trying to see what shade of green they can make the other players turn.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/727-thoth","name":"Thoth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar727_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1689"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-23T17:13:10-07:00","id":1477137,"title":"","content":"I like the Tzims. They are fun to play when you want to be either a classic old school vampire, or Necroscope wamphyri.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3598-cajunkhan","name":"CajunKhan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3598_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1700"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-23T18:57:20-07:00","id":1477145,"title":"","content":"I find Tzimisce to be one of the more multi-faceted and versatile clans. Almost every other clan stereotype fits nicely as a Tzimisce concept: bestial, monstrous, mystic, aristocratic, madman, scientist, soldier, artist, freak show, silent killer, flamboyant performer, etc, etc.<br /> <br /> Most complaints I hear are when players focus on Vicissitude stuff. I feel this has been made even worse with their recent loss of Auspex. Without the possible pursuit of transcendence, and higher understanding and insight, Vicissitude just becomes a low-brow gross out contest; the Tzimisce equivalent of \u201cfishmalk.\u201d","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24351-garygeneric","name":"Garygeneric","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24351_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"108"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-23T19:16:04-07:00","id":1477148,"title":"","content":"So, you have chosen death? Interesting. I'll make note of that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><div align=\"left\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/7.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26764-vilenecromancer","name":"Vilenecromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26764_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"247"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-23T19:43:05-07:00","id":1477149,"title":"","content":"I find the Tzimisce to be really interesting. In many ways more interesting than the Ventrue as they can encompass the concepts of the Ventrue but with greater flavor in addition to numerous other concepts.<br /> <br /> Below are some things that I find interesting about the Tzimisce. There are less interesting interpretations and aspects of the Tzimisce which I won\u2019t bother touching on.<br /> <br /> They are aristocrats who are at once evil but also honorable. They hold to their traditions and how hospitality to welcomed visitors and respect to the lord of the land. They are a more traditional and even rural sort of nobility than the Ventrue or Lasombra, having a connection to the land as well as dominance over animals and perhaps the land itself. In some ways, this aspect of them gives the Tzimisce the most vampiric flavor of any Clan.<br /> <br /> They are the most ghoul focused Clan, befitting their flavor of tradition bound medieval lords, they have special servants including the Revenants who have served them over the generations. There are the Revenant families which are particularly unique and interesting within the setting, aristocrats in their own rights, but also twisted and dark like their masters, human and yet something else. There are standard ghouls and well as animal ghouls who they can control with greater effect because of animalistic. Then there are those monstrous ghouls altered by Vicissitude. The Tzimisce Clan aren\u2019t just the vampires, but a diverse assortment of their servants that form a part of the Tzimisce culture.<br /> <br /> The Tzimisce are spiritual. They have this connection to their ancestral lands, sometimes that they can draw upon with Koldunic Sorcery. They sometimes aspire to rise above their vampiric state, altering themselves or learning about the vampiric form. This can be interpreted in a mystical way, a religious one, or even as a science.<br /> <br /> A Tzimisce character can be a noble lord, an inquisitive scientist, a spiritual mystic, or a sadistic villain. A Tzimisce can take on the place of several other Clans and yet still have their own unique flavor. Then you can add in the Revenant families, and your Tzimisce character could be a former Revenant and then you have that flavor in addition. Vicissitude can be cool, but I really don\u2019t even think that you need it for the Tzimisce Clan to be awesome.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1129,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1129-sergeant-brother","user":"Sergeant Brother","date":". 03-23-2022, 10:46 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1129-sergeant-brother","name":"Sergeant Brother","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1129_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-23T19:43:18-07:00","id":1477150,"title":"","content":"The Tzimisce are fascinating and one of my all time favorite clans. However, Vicissitude is the least interesting thing about them. There's a reason the Old Clan Tzimisce and Dark Ages Tzimisce are the best Tzimisce.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-23T19:59:01-07:00","id":1477152,"title":"","content":"Vampire: the Dark Ages was my first WoD game. From the perspective the idea of the Tzim being the least interesting is baffling. The modern nights Tzim are a different matter though, because the Tzim's creative origins and being part of the Sabbat made it very hard to bring up their cooler aspects without going back in time.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-23T19:59:17-07:00","id":1477153,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vilenecromancer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1477124-clan-tzimisce-is-the-least-interesting-clan?p=1477148#post1477148\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, you have chosen death? Interesting. I'll make note of that.</div> </div> </div> </div>I didn't choose death, death chose me. #Giovanni #Cappodocian","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"https://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://www.nodiatis.com/pub/18.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27313-hello","name":"Hello","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27313_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-23T20:03:15-07:00","id":1477155,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1477124-clan-tzimisce-is-the-least-interesting-clan?p=1477152#post1477152\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Vampire: the Dark Ages was my first WoD game. From the perspective the idea of the Tzim being the least interesting is baffling. The modern nights Tzim are a different matter though, because the Tzim's creative origins and being part of the Sabbat made it very hard to bring up their cooler aspects without going back in time.</div> </div> </div> </div>That is one of my big issues with the Clan. I like the dark lord aspect of the Tzimisce and in the Sabbath, that angle is subverted.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1129-sergeant-brother","name":"Sergeant Brother","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1129_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-23T21:38:18-07:00","id":1477166,"title":"","content":"I simply love them. I think Vicissitude is really interesting and fun, but the Tzimisce are oh so much beyond just that. It is not about their stats, but about the stories those stats tell, of those old Carpathian lords and their relationship to their land, their lineages, their subjects, their duties and their privileges. And the myriad unique ways a given Tzimisce can relate to this weight of history and tradition.<br /> <br /> Also, you simply have no better clan to play old school vampires. Sure, you can get Orlok's look with a Nosferatu, but outside that it is the Tzimisce the clan that deals the most with the themes and inspirations from before Anne Rice.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-23T21:56:46-07:00","id":1477167,"title":"","content":"One of the cool things about the Tzimisce is that they are more than just a vampiric archetype. They aren\u2019t just lordly vampires or mystical vampires, they have a complex Clan culture and history that blends those various archetypes in a really interesting way. Drawing inspiration from some of the oldest popular vampire myths while also incorporating original ideas as well. In my opinion, they are one of the more interesting Clans. <br /> <br /> I guess my questions for Hello are: what do you think that the Tzimisce need to be interesting? What Clans do you think are the most interesting and why?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1129-sergeant-brother","name":"Sergeant Brother","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1129_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-23T22:30:00-07:00","id":1477170,"title":"","content":"*aHEM* I'm going to have to +11 the &quot;The Tzimisce are one of the most interesting and flexible out of all the Clans.&quot; But I can agree that you have to dip into the Dark Ages depiction to get a lot of that. And that I can't necessarily speak much for what they have become in V5. Definitely among those saddened by the loss of Auspex. But one of the coolest things about the Tzimisce is that they are one of the easiest Clans to just shrug and go &quot;yeah, they made a Bloodline for that.&quot; It probably requires more fudging in V5, dunno what kind of alterations and retcons may have been put in place, but they are among the masters of manipulating the Kindred condition, through the manipulation of Revenant bloodlines and then Embracing the results, among other things.<br /> <br /> There are too many examples to draw on if you would like mystics or mad scientists.<br /> <br /> Want a warrior Tzimisce? <a href=\"https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Vladimir_Rustovich\" target=\"_blank\">Say hello to Vladimir.</a><br /> <br /> What about a socialite Tzimisce, a diplomat? <a href=\"https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Radu_Bistri\" target=\"_blank\">Radu has you covered.</a><br /> <br /> Pretty boy hedonist? <a href=\"https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Ilias_cel_Frumos\" target=\"_blank\">Ilias throws a great party.</a><br /> <br /> Drag queen? <a href=\"https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Zachary_Sikorsky\" target=\"_blank\"> Meet my friend Zachary.</a> Until he got himself into a little bit of trouble, that is, poor fellow.<br /> <br /> To go back to your original comments a bit, Tzimisce are not bargain-bin Ventrue, though I do find the parallels between the two to be interesting, especially when you consider their history as rivals in Central Europe. Even accepting V5's alterations to the Clan, having Animalism and PROTEAN combined with Dominate is a delightfully terrifying combination. If that Discipline spread is not kicking all kinds of ass, I'd suspect that has more to do with the limits the V5 system places on Disciplines than a flaw with the Tzimisce Discipline spread itself. I'm not quite with <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar12002_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"12002\" data-vbnamecard=\"12002\">CTPhipps</a> on the idea that Vicissitude is the least-interesting thing about the Tzimisce, but saying they can't be interesting *without* it is completely insane to me.<br /> <br /> \u200bI think <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1129-sergeant-brother\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar1129_3.jpg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1129\" data-vbnamecard=\"1129\">Sergeant Brother</a> is probably right that we'd need a bit more clarification on what you think makes the Tzimisce uninteresting, or other Clans more interesting, to respond better. But I rarely miss an opportunity to stan for the Tzimisce, thanks for giving me an excuse :P","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25886-kharnov","name":"Kharnov","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"683"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-23T23:22:11-07:00","id":1477172,"title":"","content":"I was originally perplexed by what to do with the Tzimisce. I absolutely hated Vicissitude when it was first introduced (and still do, when I ST I eliminate the Discipline). I had no idea why this abomination of an idea was stinking up Vampire. It was well over a decade before I finally discovered this was based on Necroscope style vampires and finally understood why it was in the game. So while I finally understood it, I still hated it. Necroscope was crap. (Well before V5, I nuked Vicissitude and replaced it with Protean for their in-clan Discipline.)<br /> <br /> But at the same time, &quot;Dracula was a Tzimisce&quot; always sounded cool. Dracula, of course, is awesome. But White Wolf's Dracula introduced a lot of odd things that had nothing to do with the book so it wasn't really clear what justified making Dracula a Tzimisce other than the clan weakness of needing to dwell in one's grave soil. That seemed to be it.<br /> <br /> So the identity of Tzimisce seemed bound to be a combination of being tied to the soil, and being &quot;fiends&quot; (meaning cruel). I guess that's OK. Being Vlad the Impaler is interesting. But it means that the most interesting thing about the Tzimisce isn't the stuff created by VtM, it's about rediscovering the things you like about Dracula - his ancient lineage, his ties to the Scholomance, his brides, his callous nature, and so on. You need to abandon the unique stuff VtM did with it.<br /> <br /> I know lots of people now love these faux-Necroscope vampires so I'm not here to convert anyone. I just never liked them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-23T23:36:06-07:00","id":1477174,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1477124-clan-tzimisce-is-the-least-interesting-clan?p=1477172#post1477172\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But it means that the most interesting thing about the Tzimisce isn't the stuff created by VtM, it's about rediscovering the things you like about Dracula - his ancient lineage, his ties to the Scholomance, his brides, his callous nature, and so on. You need to abandon the unique stuff VtM did with it.</div> </div> </div> </div>It <b>is</b> mostly this. The thing is that the authors decided to embrace it instead of avoiding it, so here and there they confirmed all those things about the Tzimisce that are originally from outside the game.<br /> <br /> The end result, though, was reasonably well put together and we got a clan that is complex and nuanced as all clans should be, but outside it most of their descriptions are very <i>Planet of Hats</i> style. Not that the Tzimisce always avoid this, but they do so more consistently and frequently.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-24T00:06:44-07:00","id":1477175,"title":"","content":"I have had a House Rule version of the Tzimsice that have <b>Animalism</b>,<b> Blood Sorcery</b>, and <b>Protean</b>.<br /> <br /> This version of the Tzimisce has most of the STORY elements of Vicissitude but very little of the game mechanics. In this version of the Tzimsice, they can shapeshift into bats and wolves as well as control them like the Gangrel. However, they have their Koldunic magic as rituals.They can communicate with the spirits of the land (either corrupted or by using magic to bind them) and they swiftly establish domination over their homelands through the use of shamanistic bindings.<br /> <br /> But in addition to this, the Tzimisce are also the people who discovered/possess the rituals for <b>Biothaumaturgical Experimentation</b> which effectively replaces Vicissitude in my games alongside Protean.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Biothaumaturgic_Experimentation\" target=\"_blank\">https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Bi...xperimentation</a><br /> <br /> Basicially, &quot;True Tzimisce&quot; as I call my House Ruled ones are ones that can't manipulate flesh by hand. They have to have a laboratory, dungeon, torture cellar, and workshop to do all their horrifying experiments to ghouls/humans/vampires and whatnot. It's not a fast process but one that takes time as well as money/resources. I think it makes Vicisstiude less OP and more interesting as a result. Combine Animalism, Blood Sorcery, and Protean with a Out of Clan Discipline for Dominate and you can understand why Dracula would be a Tzimisce better than in canon.<br /> <br /> Dracula doesn't much fit as a flesh-crafted monster but as a Sorcerer-Noble with lots of animal powers? Yes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-24T00:29:11-07:00","id":1477178,"title":"","content":"Tzmisce without Vicissitude are just lesser Ventrue who build domains on the fringes of society. That's... workable, but it's not any good. <br /> <br /> Vicissitude however is interesting not only from a -what you can do with it- perspective but also from a society/theological point of view; is it right to change your unchanging body granted by the curse of caine? Wouldn't society become unstable if anyone could just change their face permanently after committing a crime? What kind of impact would all of your &quot;practice&quot; have on your humanity? There's some pretty solid reasons to condemn Vicissitude and there's some pretty solid reasons to champion it; it makes for an interesting debate. Thus, I can't agree with any notion that the game would be better off without it. That said, I don't think Tzmisce ever aught to be common.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-24T00:30:46-07:00","id":1477179,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1477124-clan-tzimisce-is-the-least-interesting-clan?p=1477178#post1477178\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Tzmisce without Vicissitude are just lesser Ventrue who build domains on the fringes of society. That's... workable, but it's not any good.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, they're Sorcerer Ventrue who didn't modernize from the Dark Ages. Which is pretty damn cool.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Vicissitude however is interesting not only from a -what you can do with it- perspective but also from a society/theological point of view; is it right to change your unchanging body granted by the curse of caine? Wouldn't society become unstable if anyone could just change their face permanently after committing a crime? What kind of impact would all of your &quot;practice&quot; have on your humanity? There's some pretty solid reasons to condemn Vicissitude and there's some pretty solid reasons to champion it; it makes for an interesting debate. Thus, I can't agree with any notion that the game would be better off without it. That said, I don't think Tzmisce ever aught to be common. </div> </div> </div>Except we have Protean and Blood Sorcery for both.<br /> <br /> Vicissitude is basically a discipline that does way too much and yet not nearly as much different as people think. It's also a discipline that is so out of genre for the majority of the setting.<br /> <br /> Most vampire powers are very similar to what we know from fiction or mythology but it only applies to necroscope, and vampires in Necroscope are ALIENS.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-24T02:30:41-07:00","id":1477182,"title":"","content":"Not keeping up with the times is pretty damn stupid and very unlikely. <br /> <br /> Protean is temporary. Thaumaturgy can at most give you longer hair or a tattoo. Both are disciplines looking at Bestial or spiritual enlightenment; Viscissitude is simply magic surgery. Who are you to decide what Genre vampire's about? I think Vampire works best as political horror or a tense thriller: Does that mean we should return to high-power differences between neonates and elders and get rid of stupid things like TBA (The answer is yes, yes and yes, but that's because of-fucking-course we should. But I'm not going to get rid of Gangrel just because I like the games confined to cities) <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Most vampire powers are very similar to what we know from fiction or mythology but it only applies to necroscope, and vampires in Necroscope are ALIENS </div> </div> </div>Right, Aliens are silly and less believable than &quot;cursed by God&quot;. <br /> Must be nice being so comfortably wrong.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-24T05:06:18-07:00","id":1477191,"title":"","content":"I think the Old Clan/Vicissitude Clan split is half of the Tzimisce's problem. You can have one-note Slavic overlord sterotypes or you can have a discipline that's eternally doomed to be reduced to &quot;the body horror discipline&quot;.<br /> <br /> Anyway. My take on the fiends. Tzimisce are trapped by a part of their identity, yet equipped to prod at the boundaries of the rest of it. They remind me of the Ravnos, in a way.<br /> You can lean any way you like with them in this dichotomy.<br /> <br /> Chain yourself to the things that you feel connected to, and they to you? Own the land and everything in it to the point of considering/making them extensions of you, from every spirit down to every cell of the physical?<br /> <br /> Change everything and keep looking for new ways to change? Pushing always at the boundaries of what refuses to be changed? Change your face, your name, seek new ways of looking at things while you pursue transcendence? One has changed to overcome the frailties of mortal life, what are the frailties of the undead but more weaknesses to overcome in further metamorphosis?<br /> <br /> What is &quot;I&quot;? What is &quot;you&quot;? &quot;Us&quot;? Is there a difference? Yes? No?<br /> <br /> Or perhaps one lives their unlife somewhere between the two philosophies?<br /> <br /> Or fuck that dracula/philosophy crap altogether and just make a small fortune and a name for yourself being an undead plastic surgeon/tattoo artist, or something. Yay money. That works too. There are so many takes one could have on a Tzimisce.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><sup><i>Prone to hyperbole</i></sup>","edited":{"userid":26836,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26836-rhywbeth","user":"Rhywbeth","date":". 03-24-2022, 08:24 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26836-rhywbeth","name":"Rhywbeth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26836_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"377"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-24T05:37:25-07:00","id":1477192,"title":"","content":"I feel like Vicissitude is a treasure trove of potential and the concept is excellent but a little wasted. Like RAW it's useful for disguises, cosmetics, horrific art objects, and &quot;monsters&quot; only no monster Vicissitude can create is really worth the trouble in a world of semi-automatic firepower. Oh and of course turning yourself into a pool of blood is way cool but it's really not well intigrated with the rest of the powerset. Horrid form would work wonders if you could provide such a boost to other people rather than just yourself.<br /> <br /> IMO, Vicissitude should be a long list of specific operations that can be learned like thaumaturgy &quot;rituals&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-24T05:47:10-07:00","id":1477193,"title":"","content":"I feel an almost irrational disdain for the old clan.<br /> The discipline spread is fun, though Dominate doesn't belong to a clan that can't organize itself for shit. <br /> <br /> I just feel &quot;muh dracula&quot; and &quot;Nuh Vicissitude&quot; from it. The &quot;we're the original because we're the OLD clan&quot; is just aggravatingly petty bullshit that I want to throw to the side even moreso than TrBr.<br /> I like the revenant families. But they're too tied to this BS.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-24T05:50:47-07:00","id":1477194,"title":"","content":"They're actually one of the better fleshed (lol) out clans in teems of culture, bloodlines outlook and diversity. I'm unsure where you get this from compared to the more archeotypical ventrue or brujah.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-24T06:54:21-07:00","id":1477198,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1477124-clan-tzimisce-is-the-least-interesting-clan?p=1477179#post1477179\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Most vampire powers are very similar to what we know from fiction or mythology but it only applies to necroscope, and vampires in Necroscope are ALIENS.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't see half the problems you do with Vicissitude. I used to, not anymore, it isn't particularly OP or anything, and even its versatility isn't all that huge compared to other Disciplines when creatively used. It is just easier to see its creative potential.<br /> <br /> But that said I agree that it is too much of a reference to Necroscope and this ain't the best thing about it or the Tzimisce. By the way, I like 'em cold and detached, but not to a literal <b>alien</b> degree and not all of them. I pretty much don't like how TBH changed it from &quot;this is a nod to Necroscope&quot; to a full blown &quot;this is fucking Necroscope, enjoy&quot;. I think Vicissitude brings some interesting options to the table and that's that. Exchange it for Blood Sorcery if you want, it is just fine for me.<br /> <br /> My gripes with your house rule is just the lack of Auspex, really. It hurts the clan far more than lack of direct access to Vicissitude. My personal suggestion would be to ditch Blood Sorcery as in-clan and do it as it did before, with they having access to their sorcery tradition, but at out-of-clan cost. That or ditching Protean entirely for Blood Sorcery. Dominate is silly for the Tzimisce, and Auspex really should be there.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-24T07:14:31-07:00","id":1477205,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sergeant Brother</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1477124-clan-tzimisce-is-the-least-interesting-clan?p=1477167#post1477167\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">One of the cool things about the Tzimisce is that they are more than just a vampiric archetype. They aren\u2019t just lordly vampires or mystical vampires, they have a complex Clan culture and history that blends those various archetypes in a really interesting way. Drawing inspiration from some of the oldest popular vampire myths while also incorporating original ideas as well. In my opinion, they are one of the more interesting Clans.<br /> <br /> I guess my questions for Hello are: what do you think that the Tzimisce need to be interesting? What Clans do you think are the most interesting and why?</div> </div> </div> </div>IMO it would be more interesting if the tzimisce acted more like the progenitors from the technocracy, but without a lot of the morals and restraint. I also feel it would be a great change to have vicissitude act more like Lore of the flesh from DTF. This would make the tzimisce seem like misguided doctors and scientists who want to reveal the secrets of the human body, in the hopes of evolving humanity and even vampires to the next levels. <br /> <br /> I find the Baali to be the interesting clan, sure some people see them as a bloodline, but I think they work best as a clan. Just reading their clanbook gave me chills, it gives you insight into just how dark the world of darkness really is. They have such an interesting origin and history that it makes you want to read more about them. Somehow they make communing with demons more sinister than it already is. Ironically, for a clan that either worships, or fights demons, they give you the option to become a vampire. Sure the other option is to die, but that's a lot more freedom given to you than many other clans. <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"https://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://www.nodiatis.com/pub/18.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27313-hello","name":"Hello","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27313_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-24T07:19:33-07:00","id":1477207,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1477124-clan-tzimisce-is-the-least-interesting-clan?p=1477175#post1477175\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I have had a House Rule version of the Tzimsice that have <b>Animalism</b>,<b> Blood Sorcery</b>, and <b>Protean</b>.<br /> <br /> This version of the Tzimisce has most of the STORY elements of Vicissitude but very little of the game mechanics. In this version of the Tzimsice, they can shapeshift into bats and wolves as well as control them like the Gangrel. However, they have their Koldunic magic as rituals.They can communicate with the spirits of the land (either corrupted or by using magic to bind them) and they swiftly establish domination over their homelands through the use of shamanistic bindings.<br /> <br /> But in addition to this, the Tzimisce are also the people who discovered/possess the rituals for <b>Biothaumaturgical Experimentation</b> which effectively replaces Vicissitude in my games alongside Protean.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Biothaumaturgic_Experimentation\" target=\"_blank\">https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Bi...xperimentation</a><br /> <br /> Basicially, &quot;True Tzimisce&quot; as I call my House Ruled ones are ones that can't manipulate flesh by hand. They have to have a laboratory, dungeon, torture cellar, and workshop to do all their horrifying experiments to ghouls/humans/vampires and whatnot. It's not a fast process but one that takes time as well as money/resources. I think it makes Vicisstiude less OP and more interesting as a result. Combine Animalism, Blood Sorcery, and Protean with a Out of Clan Discipline for Dominate and you can understand why Dracula would be a Tzimisce better than in canon.<br /> <br /> Dracula doesn't much fit as a flesh-crafted monster but as a Sorcerer-Noble with lots of animal powers? Yes.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Bio thaumathurgy is perhaps on of the most interesting paths of blood sorcery, that cam out.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"https://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://www.nodiatis.com/pub/18.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":27313,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27313-hello","user":"Hello","date":". 03-24-2022, 11:11 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27313-hello","name":"Hello","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27313_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-24T07:19:42-07:00","id":1477208,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1477124-clan-tzimisce-is-the-least-interesting-clan?p=1477198#post1477198\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> My gripes with your house rule is just the lack of Auspex, really. It hurts the clan far more than lack of direct access to Vicissitude. My personal suggestion would be to ditch Blood Sorcery as in-clan and do it as it did before, with they having access to their sorcery tradition, but at out-of-clan cost. That or ditching Protean entirely for Blood Sorcery. Dominate is silly for the Tzimisce, and Auspex really should be there.</div> </div> </div> </div>I vehemently agree with this. Tzimisce need Auspex for all the same reasons Malkavians, Toreador and Tremere have Auspex. Neither Main Clan or Old Clan would psychically blind themselves by replacing Auspex (especially with V5's set up; Main Clan Tzimisce would be as unlikely to replace Auspex with Dominate as Old Clan would be to replace Auspex with Protean). <br /> <br /> Auspex gives potential and depth to the fiendish-yet-enlightened clan. It reflects not only their long-established penchant for insight, thirst for knowledge and oracular abilities, but also reflects their bent towards paranoia and territorialism, traits common to both mainstream Tzimisce and Old Clan alike.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24351-garygeneric","name":"Garygeneric","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24351_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"108"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-24T09:03:18-07:00","id":1477220,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1477124-clan-tzimisce-is-the-least-interesting-clan?p=1477182#post1477182\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Right, Aliens are silly and less believable than &quot;cursed by God&quot;.<br /> Must be nice being so comfortably wrong.</div> </div> </div> </div>In a Gothic Horror game?<br /> <br /> Yes, My Wife is Scary<br /> <br /> Aliens are much sillier and less believable.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Garygeneric</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1477124-clan-tzimisce-is-the-least-interesting-clan?p=1477208#post1477208\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I vehemently agree with this. Tzimisce need Auspex for all the same reasons Malkavians, Toreador and Tremere have Auspex. Neither Main Clan or Old Clan would psychically blind themselves by replacing Auspex (especially with V5's set up; Main Clan Tzimisce would be as unlikely to replace Auspex with Dominate as Old Clan would be to replace Auspex with Protean).<br /> <br /> Auspex gives potential and depth to the fiendish-yet-enlightened clan. It reflects not only their long-established penchant for insight, thirst for knowledge and oracular abilities, but also reflects their bent towards paranoia and territorialism, traits common to both mainstream Tzimisce and Old Clan alike.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think you can definitely roleplay them as them but I feel that the scientist-wizard element fits them better and if you had to give up any Discipline that Auspex is the best one to do so.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1477124-clan-tzimisce-is-the-least-interesting-clan?p=1477193#post1477193\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I feel an almost irrational disdain for the old clan.<br /> The discipline spread is fun, though Dominate doesn't belong to a clan that can't organize itself for shit.<br /> <br /> I just feel &quot;muh dracula&quot; and &quot;Nuh Vicissitude&quot; from it. The &quot;we're the original because we're the OLD clan&quot; is just aggravatingly petty bullshit that I want to throw to the side even moreso than TrBr.<br /> I like the revenant families. But they're too tied to this BS.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Old Clan basically exists as a critique of what a bunch of one-dimensional wannabes some fans think the Modern Tzimisce are.<br /> <br /> Which is, of course, me.<br /> <br /> The Old Clan is about saying, &quot;See how awesome they are without Vicisstiude?&quot; Which is, of course, incredibly.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 03-24-2022, 12:13 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-24T09:10:31-07:00","id":1477221,"title":"","content":"On having Auspex/Dominate: I feel it really comes down to whether you prefer the focus on the mystic or the rulership aspects, and which do you think is better for the primary focus of the Tzimisce.<br /> <br /> I find the latter much more interesting, as I feel Tremere, Malkavians and Hecata already fill the former niche well enough. And if they are to be a rulership clan, Dominate fits them much better. I know the whole &quot;The Tzimisce don't need Dominate, they enforce their command through the Blood Bond, torture and body horror!!&quot; thing but honestly, I find it stupid. It's like the Toreador not having Presence because they are so naturally charming, or the Nosferatu not having Obfuscate because they are naturally sneaky. If you have a Clan that enforces absolute control and does what dominate does, give them Dominate.<br /> <br /> Without Auspex, I find that it also allows Animalism to shine more, as they use the command over beasts to remain informed about their domain. <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27145-setitefriend","name":"SetiteFriend","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27145_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"255"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-24T10:22:19-07:00","id":1477228,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1477124-clan-tzimisce-is-the-least-interesting-clan?p=1477220#post1477220\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think you can definitely roleplay them as them but I feel that the scientist-wizard element fits them better and if you had to give up any Discipline that Auspex is the best one to do so.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> The Old Clan basically exists as a critique of what a bunch of one-dimensional wannabes some fans think the Modern Tzimisce are.<br /> <br /> Which is, of course, me.<br /> <br /> The Old Clan is about saying, &amp;quot;See how awesome they are without Vicisstiude?&amp;quot; Which is, of course, incredibly.</div> </div> </div> </div>You would take a scientist-wizard clan and the one Discipline you\u2019d remove is Auspex? I don\u2019t understand the rationale there. <br /> <br /> The thing about the Necroscope/The Thinng/The Resurrected body horror angle is that Tzimisce is designed to fill that niche, from a design standpoint. I wouldn\u2019t want to take that away from players completely. It\u2019s cool that people dig Old Clan Tzimisce and have that option, as well, but they have nothing to offer that can\u2019t be matched by several other clans and bloodlines. <br /> <br /> I also find Dominate too \u201csafe,\u201d too \u201cCamarilla.\u201d It\u2019s a subtle, non-Masquerade-threatening means to control mortals and their institutions, as well as the best method of maintaining the Masquerade. It\u2019s almost EZ Mode for vampires and I think without it, gameplay requires more creativity, and the lore of a Dominateless rulership clan becomes much more flavorful. Just my opinion though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24351-garygeneric","name":"Garygeneric","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24351_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"108"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-24T10:30:05-07:00","id":1477230,"title":"","content":"I don't really like Dominate as a Tzimisce Discipline because I like that they have to rely on Blood Bonds along with honor or terror to enforce their rule. It hearkens back to a time when rulers didn't have to be politicians. Plus, Tzimisce have all of those cool ghoul types.<br /> <br /> As for Disciplines that they should have, I feel a bit torn. I can see good arguments for Protean, Vicissitude, Auspex, or Sorcery.<br /> <br /> Years back, I experimented with some house rules for alternatives to Vicissitude based either on paths or by Revenant family.<br /> <br /> Vicissitude as Paths: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/187154-vicissitude-as-paths\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...itude-as-paths</a><br /> <br /> Vicissitude by Revenant Family: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/841919-vicissitude-by-revenant-family\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...evenant-family</a><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hello</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1477124-clan-tzimisce-is-the-least-interesting-clan?p=1477205#post1477205\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">IMO it would be more interesting if the tzimisce acted more like the progenitors from the technocracy, but without a lot of the morals and restraint. I also feel it would be a great change to have vicissitude act more like Lore of the flesh from DTF. This would make the tzimisce seem like misguided doctors and scientists who want to reveal the secrets of the human body, in the hopes of evolving humanity and even vampires to the next levels.</div> </div> </div> </div>I feel like you can already kind of do that with the Tzimisce, though that might be a very narrow focus of what some Tzimisce do now. I don't know if misguided biologist hoping to evolve humanity is a broad enough concept for a Clan, especially since a particular Tzimisce character could certainly be that concept.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hello</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1477124-clan-tzimisce-is-the-least-interesting-clan?p=1477205#post1477205\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I find the Baali to be the interesting clan, sure some people see them as a bloodline, but I think they work best as a clan. Just reading their clanbook gave me chills, it gives you insight into just how dark the world of darkness really is. They have such an interesting origin and history that it makes you want to read more about them. Somehow they make communing with demons more sinister than it already is. Ironically, for a clan that either worships, or fights demons, they give you the option to become a vampire. Sure the other option is to die, but that's a lot more freedom given to you than many other clans.</div> </div> </div> </div>I too like the Baali, though I didn't care much for their Clanbook.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1129-sergeant-brother","name":"Sergeant Brother","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1129_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-24T10:35:51-07:00","id":1477232,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Garygeneric</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1477124-clan-tzimisce-is-the-least-interesting-clan?p=1477228#post1477228\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You would take a scientist-wizard clan and the one Discipline you\u2019d remove is Auspex? I don\u2019t understand the rationale there.</div> </div> </div> </div>It helps differentiate them from the Tremere.<br /> <br /> Which is a concern because if they were Auspex, Blood Sorcery, and Protean/Vicissitude they come off as still WAY too close.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The thing about the Necroscope/The Thinng/The Resurrected body horror angle is that Tzimisce is designed to fill that niche, from a design standpoint. I wouldn\u2019t want to take that away from players completely. It\u2019s cool that people dig Old Clan Tzimisce and have that option, as well, but they have nothing to offer that can\u2019t be matched by several other clans and bloodlines. </div> </div> </div>I feel like they primarily have to offer a lot more in terms of clan history, politics, and feel than playing as an inhuman monster that barely has any feelings. Which is part of the issue. Tzimisce of the Body Horror/Soulless Monster type don't really fit very well into the Gothic Horror tragic monster feel of the game.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I also find Dominate too \u201csafe,\u201d too \u201cCamarilla.\u201d It\u2019s a subtle, non-Masquerade-threatening means to control mortals and their institutions, as well as the best method of maintaining the Masquerade. It\u2019s almost EZ Mode for vampires and I think without it, gameplay requires more creativity, and the lore of a Dominateless rulership clan becomes much more flavorful. Just my opinion though. </div> </div> </div>Maybe but it also is something that FITS the Tzimisce in that it gives them an absolute mastery of those who surround them. A Tzimisce without Dominate isn't a Tzimisce who has more flavor, it's just one who is less effective at ruling.<br /> <br /> However, if I have to choose, I'd always give them Blood Sorcery over Dominate.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 03-24-2022, 01:40 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-24T11:05:01-07:00","id":1477236,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ragged Robin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1477124-clan-tzimisce-is-the-least-interesting-clan?p=1477194#post1477194\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They're actually one of the better fleshed (lol) out clans in teems of culture, bloodlines outlook and diversity. I'm unsure where you get this from compared to the more archeotypical ventrue or brujah.</div> </div> </div> </div>I feel venture and brujah have to be archeotypical because of their clan curses. The tzimsce culture is very similar to venture culture, just with vicissitude, and a more sadistic apporach.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"https://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://www.nodiatis.com/pub/18.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27313-hello","name":"Hello","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27313_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-24T11:08:03-07:00","id":1477237,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sergeant Brother</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1477124-clan-tzimisce-is-the-least-interesting-clan?p=1477230#post1477230\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't really like Dominate as a Tzimisce Discipline because I like that they have to rely on Blood Bonds along with honor or terror to enforce their rule. It hearkens back to a time when rulers didn't have to be politicians. Plus, Tzimisce have all of those cool ghoul types.</div> </div> </div> </div>Isn't that Presence, though?<br /> <br /> Dominate isn't the power of winning someone over. Dominate is the power of., &quot;You obey because you fucking have to.&quot;<br /> <br /> It's the power of tyranny and absolute rule.<br /> <br /> Oddly, Blood Bonds are closer to Presence because you have to love a ruler who bonds you, no matter how abusive they are.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-24T11:11:55-07:00","id":1477238,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ragged Robin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1477124-clan-tzimisce-is-the-least-interesting-clan?p=1477194#post1477194\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They're actually one of the better fleshed (lol) out clans in teems of culture, bloodlines outlook and diversity. I'm unsure where you get this from compared to the more archeotypical ventrue or brujah.</div> </div> </div> </div>I actually think that's a <i>problem</i>. <br /> <br /> Clan cultures are natural, but for Tzmisce the lines between clan culture and mortal culture has been aggressively blurred. The Ventrue, Tremere or Toreador can adapt to any culture, the FoS and Giovanni can reinvent themselves for any culture, but the Tzmisce are explicitly archaic eastern europeans with slavic terminology and a demonic attachment to the carpathians, a perfectly fine and scenic place; as far as vampires go the Tzmisce are particularly backwards, which aligns with the 'murican perspective that eastern europe is backwards. It's a stupid, needless, harmful stereotype (but of course it's fine because eastern europeans are white... right? GFY) It's not an idea that lends itself to creative character building.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-24T11:28:10-07:00","id":1477242,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1477124-clan-tzimisce-is-the-least-interesting-clan?p=1477238#post1477238\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I actually think that's a <i>problem</i>. <br /> <br /> Clan cultures are natural, but for Tzmisce the lines between clan culture and mortal culture has been aggressively blurred. The Ventrue, Tremere or Toreador can adapt to any culture, the FoS and Giovanni can reinvent themselves for any culture, but the Tzmisce are explicitly archaic eastern europeans with slavic terminology and a demonic attachment to the carpathians, a perfectly fine and scenic place; as far as vampires go the Tzmisce are particularly backwards, which aligns with the 'murican perspective that eastern europe is backwards. It's a stupid, needless, harmful stereotype (but of course it's fine because eastern europeans are white... right? GFY) It's not an idea that lends itself to creative character building.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is a matter of taste but I don't think it is. I like the rooted aspects of clans, if anything the lack of historical grounding tends to make them less compelling. As though they somehow exist in a vacuum outside of the societies they infiltrate and embrace from.The historical roman pivot to germanic aspects of revised is a delight with the ventrue. <br /> <br /> I'm also surprised to see you approve of the homogenisation of the tremere. From what I recall you despised thr shift away from hermetic western aligned Occult circles into a generic blood magic archeotype?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":26986,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","user":"Ragged Robin","date":". 03-24-2022, 07:13 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-24T11:28:34-07:00","id":1477243,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1477124-clan-tzimisce-is-the-least-interesting-clan?p=1477238#post1477238\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I actually think that's a <i>problem</i>.<br /> <br /> Clan cultures are natural, but for Tzmisce the lines between clan culture and mortal culture has been aggressively blurred. The Ventrue, Tremere or Toreador can adapt to any culture, the FoS and Giovanni can reinvent themselves for any culture, but the Tzmisce are explicitly archaic eastern europeans with slavic terminology and a demonic attachment to the carpathians, a perfectly fine and scenic place; as far as vampires go the Tzmisce are particularly backwards, which aligns with the 'murican perspective that eastern europe is backwards. It's a stupid, needless, harmful stereotype (but of course it's fine because eastern europeans are white... right? GFY) It's not an idea that lends itself to creative character building.</div> </div> </div> </div>I really hope they make the Tzimisce a major clan for Asia.<br /> <br /> Shapeshifting vampires with magical powers have a lot of similarities there.<br /> <br /> They could really expand the Tzimisce beyond Eastern European mythology.<br /> <br /> One of the interesting ideas I liked from Lasombra Revised was their discussion of the Lasombra's power in the Chinese Imperial courts.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-24T11:45:30-07:00","id":1477248,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hello</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1477124-clan-tzimisce-is-the-least-interesting-clan?p=1477236#post1477236\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I feel venture and brujah have to be archeotypical because of their clan curses. The tzimsce culture is very similar to venture culture, just with vicissitude, and a more sadistic apporach.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm unsure how. From historical perspective the tzimsce arnt really like the ventrue at all. In terms of culture the fiends are orthodox the ventrue protestant/Catholic<br /> The ventrue clove very close to Humanity wereas the fiends distance themselves. The fiend tends to be very divergent in Interests by contrast the ventrue are hyper focussed on material power. Even in play they operate very different with not only no discipline overlap but also very distinct play style and stat building.<br /> On a practical level the brujah probably have more in common with the ventrue which i think speaks depths.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":26986,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","user":"Ragged Robin","date":". 03-24-2022, 02:52 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-24T12:01:18-07:00","id":1477251,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ragged Robin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1477124-clan-tzimisce-is-the-least-interesting-clan?p=1477248#post1477248\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'm unsure how. From historical perspective the tzimsce arnt really like the ventrue at all. In terms of culture the fiends are orthodox the ventrue protestant/Catholic<br /> The ventrue clove very close to Humanity wereas the fiends distance themselves. The fiend tends to be very divergent in Interests by contrast the ventrue are hyper focussed on material power. Even in play they operate very different with not only no discipline overlap but also very distinct play style and stat building.<br /> On a practical level the brujah probably have more in common with the ventrue which i think speaks depths.</div> </div> </div> </div>The brujah and venture are perhaps the clan furthest apart. The venture create and sustain, the brujah destroy and decay. If the venture are the ceo's of multi million dollar companies that bribe politicians to pass the laws they want, then the brujah are the ones who rouse others into tearing things down, but dont have any plan on how to build a better future.<br /> <br /> The venture and giovanni are a better comparison.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"https://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://www.nodiatis.com/pub/18.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27313-hello","name":"Hello","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27313_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-24T12:12:36-07:00","id":1477254,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hello</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1477124-clan-tzimisce-is-the-least-interesting-clan?p=1477251#post1477251\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The brujah and venture are perhaps the clan furthest apart. The venture create and sustain, the brujah destroy and decay. If the venture are the ceo's of multi million dollar companies that bribe politicians to pass the laws they want, then the brujah are the ones who rouse others into tearing things down, but dont have any plan on how to build a better future.<br /> <br /> The venture and giovanni are a better comparison.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oddly I've heard the exact opposite suggested, depending on your personal politics I suppose. But I consider both incorrect as neither genrally create or destroy, they just latch on or undermine or bolster based on desire to accumulate power or errode your enemies. Which is incidently what most clans do....arguably all clans. It's just a question of where you go for power.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":26986,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","user":"Ragged Robin","date":". 03-24-2022, 03:15 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-24T12:52:32-07:00","id":1477260,"title":"","content":"This thread took a bit of a jog after I went to bed last night, so I'm going to try and just quickly respond to the things that stand out to me:<br /> <br /> I disagree with the argument that Vicissitude cannot be Protean because Protean is only temporary. That's an extremely subtle distinction that can be pretty easily retconned in order to combine a pair of Disciplines that really don't have a huge difference between them otherwise, aside from Vicissitude being far more specialized. It's especially noticeable when you start comparing Elder-level Vicissitude with Elder-level Protean and see how the differences mostly seem to come down to flavour; being able to turn into a *fire-breathing dragon* seems more like Protean to me than the work of a vampiric mad biologist.<br /> <br /> And nothing bugs me more than the argument that the Tzimisce cannot be interesting without Vicissitude. I love the Path of Metamorphosis, and think that Vicissitude (whatever version of it you want to use) fits with that really well. But trying to argue that the Tzimisce or the Path of Metamorphosis must focus and rely on Vicissitude, with everything else being secondary or irrelevant, cheapens both of them.<br /> <br /> Again, I don't know much about how V5 handled things, but my understanding is they mostly made it into Amalgams with Dominate. I dislike that and disagree with it; I think they should have become an Amalgam with Blood Sorcery, because it makes sense for the idea of them being mystics (and eventually mad scientists/technomancers), and because most of the more infamous Vicissitude users were Blood Sorcerers already (Vykos, Yorak, Velya, etc.). I can kind of see what they were going for with Dominate, but it just doesn't seem right to me, and it seems like Blood Sorcery would be a smoother transition while also leaving more room for Tzimisce that don't use Vicissitude to be their own thing. It also heads off the argument &quot;Thaumaturgy/Blood Sorcery on its own simply isn't capable of such significant changes&quot;; well, combine Shapeshifting to cover the big changes with Blood Magic that makes the changes permanent, and voila.<br /> <br /> That being said, I do *not* think that Blood Sorcery should have been one of their Clan Disciplines. I rather appreciated the traditional conception of the Koldun, that while this was a big part of Clan tradition it was something separate from the main line, and required an extra amount of effort to dedicate yourself to it (the extra cost of an out-of-Clan Discipline). I think their spread should have been Animalism, Auspex, and Protean. I disagree with the idea that Tzimisce simply having Auspex makes them too close to the Tremere as a concept; that'd be the case if they had Dominate, but having Animalism and Protean puts some significant distance between the two IMO. Which doesn't even mention that having some similarity between the two makes a lot of sense from a lore perspective since Tzimisce blood was used in the ritual that created the original Tremere. I think Animalism/Auspex/Protean sets them up to be a more intellectual version of the Gangrel, while you can still have the &quot;Old Clan&quot; that replaces Protean with Dominate to represent the more lordship-focused Tzimisce (in fact, I tend to head-canon the idea that the Tzimisce used for the ritual was Old Clan since that easily explains 2/3 of the Tremere's Clan Disciplines). (PS I wouldn't really mind if Auspex was replaced with Dominate either, for those who really want those Dracula vibes)<br /> <br /> Of course, I don't especially care which of those spreads is the &quot;original&quot; vs. &quot;new&quot; bloodline. Again, I think flexibility and change are probably the most interesting aspect of the Tzimisce, rather than lordship or scholarship, which coincidentally leaves room for both if you allow for bloodlines that have &quot;evolved&quot; in different directions.<br /> <br /> To head off any arguments about the above Discipline spread being too close to the Gangrel, I'd point out that similar Discipline spreads don't automatically create redundancy once you include different weaknesses and Clan cultures; you could argue that either the Brujah or the Toreador invalidate the other because the only difference in Disciplines between them is Auspex vs. Potence. That one difference, combined with a distinct weakness and Clan culture, can result in something significantly different. Gangrel are (semi-)nomadic survivors, without necessarily having a specific attachment to a particular territory, whereas Tzimisce being strongly tied to a particular territory while also lacking the raw endurance provided by Fortitude creates the need to be a more strategic master of your domain, including fortification, which gives us our master-of-the-border-castle Dracula-style vampire lord.<br /> <br /> (I am mostly ignoring the new V5 Clan weakness because I know little about it, and am unsure how I feel about it based on what I know of it so far. But again, plenty of pull away from the Gangrel.)<br /> <br /> Regarding the ethnic stereotypes... *stares VERY HARD at the Banu Haqim* You have an example there of a Clan that has a traditional culture very strongly tied to a particular region and ethnicity that nonetheless leaves room for members of the Clan from outside that context to still have a place and help define it as something broader. There's no reason you can't do the same with the Tzimisce.<br /> <br /> In fact, there's more reason, because (again) I am of the opinion that change and &quot;evolution&quot; is the most interesting defining feature of the Tzimisce.<br /> <br /> But, to put my influences out in the open for a bit, I really got into Masquerade after spending a while with Requiem and the Ordo Dracul, which is why I dig the Path of Metamorphosis so much: the idea of vampires consciously working to overcome the weaknesses and limitations of their condition in order to become something MORE. I also found it the most interesting aspect of the backstory of the Eldest, the idea of the Antediluvian that rejected/challenged the notion of the Curse of Caine as static and dead.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25886-kharnov","user":"Kharnov","date":". 03-24-2022, 04:13 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25886-kharnov","name":"Kharnov","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"683"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-24T13:15:07-07:00","id":1477263,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1477124-clan-tzimisce-is-the-least-interesting-clan?p=1477238#post1477238\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Clan cultures are natural, but for Tzmisce the lines between clan culture and mortal culture has been aggressively blurred. The Ventrue, Tremere or Toreador can adapt to any culture, the FoS and Giovanni can reinvent themselves for any culture, but the Tzmisce are explicitly archaic eastern europeans with slavic terminology and a demonic attachment to the carpathians, a perfectly fine and scenic place; as far as vampires go the Tzmisce are particularly backwards, which aligns with the 'murican perspective that eastern europe is backwards.</div> </div> </div> </div>That has to do with laziness on the part of writers. They are looking for inspiration and therefore go to things that already exist, but them overemphasize them. The clan's two main inspirations - Dracula and Necroscope - rely heavily on the same tropes. (Plus for some strange reason, White Wolf seemed to think that Transylvania - a land populated by Romanians, Hungarians, and Germans - is Slavic when in fact none of those peoples are Slavic at all. The real life Vlad Tepes was Romanian, and the fictional Dracula describes himself as a Szekely.) So there's a lot of emphasis on those elements. Other clans too were stereotyped in certain cultures, but at least the Camarilla Clans had a more variety of examples.<br /> <br /> We knew that the Ventrue were heavily associated with Rome, but the game didn't use Latin and Roman structures to describe their modern organization of boards and directorates. And we had early examples of ancient Roman vampires that weren't Ventrue (like the Gangrel Lucian) and Ventrue vampires that were outside Rome (like Hrothgar and Siegfried). <br /> <br /> Because the Sabbat and Tzimisce were described much later, the clanbook ever later than that, and only had one Sabbat By Night for a long time, we didn't get anywhere near the variety of examples. It didn't help that because of the clan's role in the Anarch Revolt, almost all the backstory centers around that, and that takes place in the Balkans. So we've seen indiscriminate use of some Slavic terms in an effort to give them more depth and authenticity (cheap use of foreign words was a problem elsewhere too, just see any number of Werewolf tribebooks). But it actually doesn't do that because it's just superficial. There's no need to call the clan's &quot;warlords&quot; by the term &quot;voivode&quot; or their hulking monsters &quot;vozhd&quot;. We know that Carthage was a big thing for the Brujah, but writers never felt to use Phoenician terms for Brujah leaders or organization.<br /> <br /> So while I agree that the clan's presentation has to often been too strongly associated with Eastern Europe, it's not too hard to deemphasize those things. In terms of actual Tzimisce PCs and NPCs I've seen in chronicles, most have no connection to Eastern Europe at all. It's just an artifact of the official writers overusing characters with Slavic names especially for elders.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-24T13:46:26-07:00","id":1477265,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kharnov</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1477124-clan-tzimisce-is-the-least-interesting-clan?p=1477260#post1477260\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This<br /> <br /> Again, I don't know much about how V5 handled things, but my understanding is they mostly made it into Amalgams with Dominate. I dislike that and disagree with it; I think they should have become an Amalgam with Blood Sorcery, because it makes sense for the idea of them being mystics...</div> </div> </div> </div>Fun Fact: V5 originally designed Vicissitude as an Auspex amalgam (see Erzulie, V5 Chicago By Night). The out-of-the-blue Dominate thing in the Companion seems to have retconned the very same edition they were supposed to be writing for.<br /> <br /> I would love to have seen a Matthew Dawkins treatment for the clan, but sadly his Tzimisce writeups and Loresheets are under NDA.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24351-garygeneric","name":"Garygeneric","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24351_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"108"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-24T13:49:13-07:00","id":1477267,"title":"","content":"And now, to respond a bit more specifically to the OP:<br /> <br /> &quot;I wish the Tzimisce were more like amoral Progenitors&quot;: I think I need a bit of an explanation regarding how you think the Tzimisce *aren't* like amoral self-serving Progenitors, unless your argument is essentially &quot;not all of them are,&quot; in which case I'd be critical of making a clan entirely into a one-dimensional stereotype. Regardless of the Clan, trying to put the exact same Hat on every single member is boring. Or &quot;they don't care enough about evolving humans with them,&quot; to which I would respond &quot;why would you want to make your cattle more powerful and dangerous?&quot; That being said, I find the idea of a Tzimisce Metamorphosist who is 100% onboard with the segments of the Obertus Revenants that want to replace traditional humanity with themselves to be quite a neat idea personally. But I think the broad argument that most of the Clan view vampires as superior and aren't interested in turning their food supply into rivals makes a fair amount of sense.<br /> <br /> Baali as the example of an Interesting Clan: No disagreement, the Baali are pretty neat. But if Interesting = &quot;dark and twisted history&quot; and &quot;interesting philosophies,&quot; I'm again wondering how the Tzimisce fail to qualify, needs some clarification. If you want &quot;dark and twisted,&quot; why doesn't the Cathedral of Flesh qualify? &quot;Interesting philosophies?&quot; Setting aside Metamorphosis, you have the Christian mysticism of the Dracon and their followers in Constantinople, and the Tzimisce more generally being involved in the development of many of the Sabbat's modern Paths of Enlightenment. I'm not saying you can't make distinctions on those points, but I think you need to be more explicit about the &quot;why&quot; since there are a lot of superficial similarities.<br /> <br /> (I do note that the Clan's relationship with the demonic Kupala is one of the things you acknowledge as still being interesting regardless of your other critiques)<br /> <br /> &quot;I wish Vicissitude was more like Lore of the Flesh&quot;: This one just seems a bit nit-picky to me? It seems like you don't have any problem with the concept, just the particular mechanics in practice, and I don't see how that makes the Tzimisce as a whole uninteresting. But I am also not really familiar with the Lore of the Flesh, beyond the earlier topic that covered this point more specifically.<br /> <br /> &quot;Tzimisce are just more sadistic Ventrue&quot;: This is again a consequence of focusing on the Tzimisce culture as &quot;lordship&quot; rather than &quot;adaptation.&quot; It also ignores that Ventrue are fundamentally lords of *people* while Tzimisce are lords of the *land*, which is why they have Animalism and a prominent tradition of pagan Blood Sorcery. The Tzimisce have also always been depicted as more scholarly and mystic than the Ventrue; Ventrue scholars and sorcerers definitely exist, but they have never had a prominent place within the culture of the clan the way that Koldun and Metamorphosist philosophers have among the Tzimisce, to the best of my knowledge. Which is also why Auspex has historically been a Clan Discipline for Tzimisce, while Ventrue with Auspex in-Clan have always been a very minor bloodline or the consequence of ritual alteration.<br /> <br /> On separate notes:<br /> <br /> &quot;The Ventrue and the Brujah need to be Archetypal due to their Clan Weaknesses&quot;: Nope. The argument arguably holds better for the Ventrue, since their particular needs will kind of force them to adopt particular strategies to meet those needs, but even within that there is room for them to be battle-lords versus scheming aristocrats/businessmen. See the Antitribu. For the Brujah it's even more incorrect, because there are two fundamental approaches you can take to a weakness like theirs: lean into it, or strive to overcome it. Ancient Brujah developed an entire Path of Enlightenment that focuses on overcoming their destructive impulses, the Path of Entelechy. It's another Path I'm rather fond of, and it serves to demonstrate that the Brujah are capable of being more ordered and constructive than you imagine them. It's just more of a struggle for them. But to paraphrase old Paarthurnax, is it (morally) better to be born with a good temper, or to overcome a bad temper through great effort?<br /> <br /> &quot;Ventrue as creative vs. Brujah as destructive&quot;: Again, Nope. Setting aside the above point about Brujah and Entelechy, and setting aside the reasonable argument that all vampires are more parasitic than creative, it would probably be better to imagine a triad that includes the Toreador as Creative vs Ventrue as Static and Brujah as Destructive. And also to comment on the fact that Creation and Destruction are not as separate as they are often framed; the creation of something new almost always involves the destruction of something old (or at least radically changing something old). You destroy the natural stone of a quarry to make the bricks needed to create a city. Creating a new order almost always requires the overthrow of the old order. Which is what the Brujah ideal is all about, the creation of a Vampire/Human utopia. Many Brujah traditionally were part of a group known as <a href=\"https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Promethean_(VTM)\" target=\"_blank\">the Prometheans</a> who were all about the recreation of Carthage, which in their history was such a utopia (and in the rest of Kindred history was a Baali-infested hellhole, history is fun that way). I would argue that the difference between the Brujah and Ventrue is less about Creation vs. Destruction, and more about Order/Hierarchy vs. Chaos/Anarchy, which are very different things.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25886-kharnov","name":"Kharnov","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"683"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-24T15:37:47-07:00","id":1477278,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kharnov</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1477124-clan-tzimisce-is-the-least-interesting-clan?p=1477267#post1477267\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And now, to respond a bit more specifically to the OP:<br /> <br /> &quot;I wish the Tzimisce were more like amoral Progenitors&quot;: I think I need a bit of an explanation regarding how you think the Tzimisce *aren't* like amoral self-serving Progenitors, unless your argument is essentially &quot;not all of them are,&quot; in which case I'd be critical of making a clan entirely into a one-dimensional stereotype. Regardless of the Clan, trying to put the exact same Hat on every single member is boring. Or &quot;they don't care enough about evolving humans with them,&quot; to which I would respond &quot;why would you want to make your cattle more powerful and dangerous?&quot; That being said, I find the idea of a Tzimisce Metamorphosist who is 100% onboard with the segments of the Obertus Revenants that want to replace traditional humanity with themselves to be quite a neat idea personally. But I think the broad argument that most of the Clan view vampires as superior and aren't interested in turning their food supply into rivals makes a fair amount of sense.<br /> <br /> Baali as the example of an Interesting Clan: No disagreement, the Baali are pretty neat. But if Interesting = &quot;dark and twisted history&quot; and &quot;interesting philosophies,&quot; I'm again wondering how the Tzimisce fail to qualify, needs some clarification. If you want &quot;dark and twisted,&quot; why doesn't the Cathedral of Flesh qualify? &quot;Interesting philosophies?&quot; Setting aside Metamorphosis, you have the Christian mysticism of the Dracon and their followers in Constantinople, and the Tzimisce more generally being involved in the development of many of the Sabbat's modern Paths of Enlightenment. I'm not saying you can't make distinctions on those points, but I think you need to be more explicit about the &quot;why&quot; since there are a lot of superficial similarities.<br /> <br /> (I do note that the Clan's relationship with the demonic Kupala is one of the things you acknowledge as still being interesting regardless of your other critiques)<br /> <br /> &quot;I wish Vicissitude was more like Lore of the Flesh&quot;: This one just seems a bit nit-picky to me? It seems like you don't have any problem with the concept, just the particular mechanics in practice, and I don't see how that makes the Tzimisce as a whole uninteresting. But I am also not really familiar with the Lore of the Flesh, beyond the earlier topic that covered this point more specifically.<br /> <br /> &quot;Tzimisce are just more sadistic Ventrue&quot;: This is again a consequence of focusing on the Tzimisce culture as &quot;lordship&quot; rather than &quot;adaptation.&quot; It also ignores that Ventrue are fundamentally lords of *people* while Tzimisce are lords of the *land*, which is why they have Animalism and a prominent tradition of pagan Blood Sorcery. The Tzimisce have also always been depicted as more scholarly and mystic than the Ventrue; Ventrue scholars and sorcerers definitely exist, but they have never had a prominent place within the culture of the clan the way that Koldun and Metamorphosist philosophers have among the Tzimisce, to the best of my knowledge. Which is also why Auspex has historically been a Clan Discipline for Tzimisce, while Ventrue with Auspex in-Clan have always been a very minor bloodline or the consequence of ritual alteration.</div> </div> </div> </div>1)Progenitors are not amoral, if you read the progenitor book you would see that progenitors are trying their hardest to steer humanity away from what they believe as superstiion, and are trying to give humanity the ability to take care of their own wounds through science, instead of requiring mystics.<br /> <br /> 2)Baali philosophy is vastly different from tzimisce philosophy. Some serve demons, some enslave them, and some fight against them. They commune with demons, beings from planes of existence most cant even begin to comprehend, beings which even the mightiest of vampires fear. A structure made flesh cant really be compared to that. The path of enlightenment the baali follow like path of hive from both editions makes the baali feel like eldritch scholars and scientists. Paths like metamorphasis, while interesting, feels better for a mage who can manipulate their dna, than a vampire who can only change the shape and look of his flesh.<br /> <br /> 3)Lore of the flesh<br /> <a href=\"https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Lore_of_the_Flesh\" target=\"_blank\">https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Lore_of_the_Flesh</a>, it just need a couple changes here and there to make it more aplicable for vampires, but other than that it would be a great replacement.<br /> <br /> 4)OCT are the sorcerer branch of clan tzimisce, they are incredibally rare, these are the &quot;lord of the lands&quot;. Most tzimisce however don't know anything about sorcery, and are lords of the people, just like the venture, making the mystic aspect of the tzimisce, not that relevant. The only difference is that they have auspex, and the venture don't.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"https://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://www.nodiatis.com/pub/18.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27313-hello","name":"Hello","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27313_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-24T15:52:29-07:00","id":1477280,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 1)Progenitors are not amoral, if you read the progenitor book you would see that progenitors are trying their hardest to steer humanity away from what they believe as superstiion, and are trying to give humanity the ability to take care of their own wounds through science, instead of requiring mystics. </div> </div> </div>I prefer Progenitors who have armies of slaves like Blade Runner and The Island of Doctor Moreau to these losers. There's a name for scientists who put ethics over power: Traditionalists.<br /> <br /> See also: Losers.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-24T16:03:31-07:00","id":1477281,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hello</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1477124-clan-tzimisce-is-the-least-interesting-clan?p=1477278#post1477278\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> 1)Progenitors are not amoral, if you read the progenitor book you would see that progenitors are trying their hardest to steer humanity away from what they believe as superstiion, and are trying to give humanity the ability to take care of their own wounds through science, instead of requiring mystics.<br /> <br /> 2)Baali philosophy is vastly different from tzimisce philosophy. Some serve demons, some enslave them, and some fight against them. They commune with demons, beings from planes of existence most cant even begin to comprehend, beings which even the mightiest of vampires fear. A structure made flesh cant really be compared to that. The path of enlightenment the baali follow like path of hive from both editions makes the baali feel like eldritch scholars and scientists. Paths like metamorphasis, while interesting, feels better for a mage who can manipulate their dna, than a vampire who can only change the shape and look of his flesh.<br /> <br /> 3)Lore of the flesh<br /> <a href=\"https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Lore_of_the_Flesh\" target=\"_blank\">https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Lore_of_the_Flesh</a>, it just need a couple changes here and there to make it more aplicable for vampires, but other than that it would be a great replacement.<br /> <br /> 4)OCT are the sorcerer branch of clan tzimisce, they are incredibally rare, these are the &quot;lord of the lands&quot;. Most tzimisce however don't know anything about sorcery, and are lords of the people, just like the venture, making the mystic aspect of the tzimisce, not that relevant. The only difference is that they have auspex, and the venture don't.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>1) Adding the qualifiers &quot;amoral and self-serving&quot; when comparing the Tzimisce to the Progenitors was specifically meant to point out that the Progenitors AREN'T while the Tzimisce ARE. You did the the same, just including the word &quot;but.&quot;<br /> <br /> 2) I did agree they are different, just *superficially* similar in some respects. My point is you need to explain what makes horrible actions and twisted philosophy interesting in one example and not interesting in another. It seems like &quot;demons&quot; are the big difference, but I am open to more clarification. I don't need it explained that they *are* different, I want to understand which differences make one group interesting and the other not interesting.<br /> <br /> Also, DNA isn't an especially relevant topic for beings that explicitly defy traditional biology, being undead and all. There's a Tzimisce Methuselah who is suspected of having transformed themself into a disease. Elder-level Vicissitude can go far beyond the limitations of the first five dots.<br /> <br /> 3) Again, kind of missing the point. My point is that the specific rules for how Vicissitude should work shouldn't really affect whether or not the IDEA of how the Tzimisce use of Vicissitude is interesting or not.<br /> <br /> 4) This is just plain wrong. Koldun are MOST COMMON among the Old Clan. Velya the Vivisectionist, Yorak, and Dracula are three prominent examples of Koldun that use Vicissitude. And there are plenty of others, like Rustovich's sire who turned other vampires into magical grimoires.<br /> <br /> (PS Also, there are enough Tzimisce that combine skill with Vicissitude and magical knowledge that there is a title of respect afforded to such individuals, known as Zhupan.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25886-kharnov","user":"Kharnov","date":"feel this is more accurate 03-24-2022, 07:18 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25886-kharnov","name":"Kharnov","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"683"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-24T16:41:40-07:00","id":1477282,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1477124-clan-tzimisce-is-the-least-interesting-clan?p=1477280#post1477280\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I prefer Progenitors who have armies of slaves like Blade Runner and The Island of Doctor Moreau to these losers. There's a name for scientists who put ethics over power: Traditionalists.<br /> <br /> See also: Losers.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm pretty sure it was implied that some genegineers of the progenitors actually do have slaves.<br /> <br /> The wiki states-<br /> <br /> &quot;<span style=\"color:#3A3A3A\"><span style=\"font-family:rubik\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">During the </span></span></span><a href=\"https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Pogrom\" target=\"_blank\">Pogrom</a><span style=\"color:#3A3A3A\"><span style=\"font-family:rubik\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">, many of the Genegineers creations were used as warbeasts and guardians, and the methodology invested heavily in biological weaponry genetic enhancement for agents. Their recklessness is even seen with suspicion within the </span></span></span><a href=\"https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Technocracy\" target=\"_blank\">Technocracy</a><span style=\"color:#3A3A3A\"><span style=\"font-family:rubik\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">. This has lead many detractors to speak of </span></span></span><a href=\"https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Realm_(MTAs)\" target=\"_blank\">Realms</a><span style=\"color:#3A3A3A\"><span style=\"font-family:rubik\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"> modeled after Antebellum slave plantations, dark uses for the Human Genome project, and other abominations. In recent times, the Genegineers have tried to brighten their image by focusing on cancer research and genetic disorders, but the rest of the Convention still watches their activities carefully.&quot;</span></span></span><br /> <br /> This probably means that some of the progenitors have armies of slaves similar to blade runner and doctor moreau, its just that they want to hide it from the other progenitors and technocracy, for obvious reasons.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"https://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://www.nodiatis.com/pub/18.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":27313,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27313-hello","user":"Hello","date":". 03-24-2022, 08:05 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27313-hello","name":"Hello","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27313_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-24T18:08:54-07:00","id":1477294,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1477124-clan-tzimisce-is-the-least-interesting-clan?p=1477237#post1477237\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Isn't that Presence, though?<br /> <br /> Dominate isn't the power of winning someone over. Dominate is the power of., &quot;You obey because you fucking have to.&quot;<br /> <br /> It's the power of tyranny and absolute rule.<br /> <br /> Oddly, Blood Bonds are closer to Presence because you have to love a ruler who bonds you, no matter how abusive they are.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, that\u2019s kinda true, but Dominate is best used in subtle ways - erasing memories, conditioning servants, that sort of thing. The lord will seldom just start dominating everyone in front of everybody. <br /> <br /> It also strikes me as a bit too quick, where as the dominance of the blood bond is slower and requires an investment in servants. A Ventrue or Lasombra can go to the local rich guy, dominate him, and get that cushy business deal. The Tzimisce, on the other hand, spend generations cultivating families of servants, each individual has served loyally from childhood, leaving those servants somewhat detached from mainstream society as well.<br /> <br /> I actually don\u2019t think that the Tzimisce having Dominate is terrible or anything, but I actually prefer that they don\u2019t have it. <br /> <br /> I really like the Revenant families and I think it\u2019s cool to have the Tzimisce heavily draw from those families and have their Disciplines determined by that family origin.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1129,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1129-sergeant-brother","user":"Sergeant Brother","date":". 03-24-2022, 09:11 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1129-sergeant-brother","name":"Sergeant Brother","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1129_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-24T19:07:07-07:00","id":1477295,"title":"","content":"I haven't played Vampire in years.. obviously I still day-dream about it on occasion. I just wanted to say that, in my group, Tzimisce were the most feared and hated of all possible enemies. A Lasombra? A Werewolf? What? They're gonna be able to do 19 aggs on regular basis? Whatever. I can take them. A Tzimisce? My Appearance drops to what? and I can't get it back? Screw that. I'm outta here.<br /> <br /> Death is something that happens in RPG's. None of us really fear it, but being forced to play a character that has been horribly and irrevocably altered can be a big problem, so even if the Tzimisce doesn't seem that scary in lore, I find that, in actual game-play, Players (and therefor the protagonists of the story) tend to act more afraid of Tzimisce more than just about anything else. That's due entirely to vicissitude.<br /> <br /> Now that doesn't necessarily make the Tzimisce an interesting clan. I think the Tzimisce had an interesting thing going. The animosity between the Old Clan and the main Tzimisce was kinda interesting. It seems to me like the Tzimisce of the V5 era could go alot of different ways, so I think I would call them a clan with a great deal of potential, but I honestly think they need to keep the flesh crafting. I could see if the Tzimisce kind of &quot;retreat&quot; into western asia and my understanding is that fleshcrafting/shapeshiting is something asian vampires are known for. They might even start working with.. well.. whatever the Ravnos are now.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23753-gothik_knight","name":"Gothik_Knight","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"66"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-24T19:21:33-07:00","id":1477297,"title":"","content":"It makes perfect sense for people to be more terrified of Tzimisce than nearly any other group. The characters should be far more scared than the players. From the point of view of a V:tM player, a dead character is a dead character, but from the character\u2019s perspective, getting ripped apart by a lupine in half a second is far preferable to being captured by the Tzimisce and subjected to horrible torture over the course of months or years.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1129-sergeant-brother","name":"Sergeant Brother","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1129_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-24T20:16:15-07:00","id":1477299,"title":"","content":"Honestly, I hate the idea that Vicissitude is permanent and think it makes it even more overpowered. It shouldn't be something that can't be fixed with Blood Points, which it could be in the Clan Novels.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-24T20:27:03-07:00","id":1477301,"title":"","content":"Permanent for mortals, but vampires should be able to heal it like aggravated damage.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1129-sergeant-brother","name":"Sergeant Brother","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1129_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-24T20:52:50-07:00","id":1477304,"title":"","content":"I'm torn on that one. I feel like their needs to be a way to fix it, because it can lead to a bad feeling situation for players. On the other hand, if you make it too easy I think the genuine feeling of fear goes away. Better to err on the side of too easy though.. we want the players to come back after all.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23753-gothik_knight","name":"Gothik_Knight","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"66"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-24T21:02:44-07:00","id":1477305,"title":"","content":"Yeah, I've always allowed players to heal it. 5 blood points points per disfigurement, or attribute lost, heals while the vampire rests during the day. If you get badly messed up it could take you a week or more to heal everything and you might have to drain a half dozen people's worth of blood, so it can be a pretty serious issue, but it's not like it's something that's there forever.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-24T21:15:12-07:00","id":1477306,"title":"","content":"For interesting Clan usage; I used to ponder and tinker with Northeast Asia being primarily dominated by a tripartite alliance of Legalistic Lasombra who dip into Confucianism via ancestor cults, Daoist Tzimisce who play both the isolated sage and the man-eating monster in the mountains, and Buddhist Caitiff of suspiciously potent blood. They replaced the Wan Kuei, being the true source of the \u2018Cathayans\u2019 and the rumors about them. Nothing concrete was done, but it was fun.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-24T21:51:25-07:00","id":1477307,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1477124-clan-tzimisce-is-the-least-interesting-clan?p=1477306#post1477306\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For interesting Clan usage; I used to ponder and tinker with Northeast Asia being primarily dominated by a tripartite alliance of Legalistic Lasombra who dip into Confucianism via ancestor cults, Daoist Tzimisce who play both the isolated sage and the man-eating monster in the mountains, and Buddhist Caitiff of suspiciously potent blood. They replaced the Wan Kuei, being the true source of the \u2018Cathayans\u2019 and the rumors about them. Nothing concrete was done, but it was fun.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, I wouldn't be surprised if Ming Xiao is retconned as a East Clan Tzimisce.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-24T22:24:55-07:00","id":1477308,"title":"","content":"As I run it, nothing a Tzmisce can do in a turn or two of combat will be permanent. Difficult to heal? Sure. but permanent? No. For permanency, the Tzmisce needs you in a state where you can barely fight back, but at that point your life is in their hands and perhaps being disfigured is a mercy. One surefire way for higher gen to cure their disfigurements is to diablerize a Tzmisce of equal or greater generation than the one who disfigured them. Alternatively, they could get a lesser practitioner to try some kind of counter surgery.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-24T22:27:02-07:00","id":1477309,"title":"","content":"Mind you, if it's Aggravated Damage, I liked the 5 Blood Points to heal the damage which is basically killing a man per dot. The best Victoria Ash moment is the fact she killed almost a dozen people to get her looks back.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-24T23:14:18-07:00","id":1477312,"title":"","content":"I just realized something. Tzimisce was call the least interesting in this thread. How did we forget about brujah? They don't have a great discipline spread, literally just hit good, run fast, and smile. They're lore is so bland without the inclusion of the other clans, such as the Toreador and Tzimisce ironically. They're so disorganized, I have to wonder how they were ever considered a high clan. And to top it all off, I literally forgot they existed again.<br /> <br /> I'm starting to see why they fused brujah, gangrel, and tzimisce in the sister line requiem. But at least Gangrel can stand alone cause of protean, and tzimisce get cool powers and interesting clan culture.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><div align=\"left\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/7.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26764-vilenecromancer","name":"Vilenecromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26764_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"247"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-24T23:46:52-07:00","id":1477314,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vilenecromancer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1477124-clan-tzimisce-is-the-least-interesting-clan?p=1477312#post1477312\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I just realized something. Tzimisce was call the least interesting in this thread. How did we forget about brujah? They don't have a great discipline spread, literally just hit good, run fast, and smile. They're lore is so bland without the inclusion of the other clans, such as the Toreador and Tzimisce ironically. They're so disorganized, I have to wonder how they were ever considered a high clan. And to top it all off, I literally forgot they existed again.<br /> <br /> I'm starting to see why they fused brujah, gangrel, and tzimisce in the sister line requiem. But at least Gangrel can stand alone cause of protean, and tzimisce get cool powers and interesting clan culture.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Brujah are the least interesting history but the most fun to play generally.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-25T04:15:33-07:00","id":1477323,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SetiteFriend</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1477124-clan-tzimisce-is-the-least-interesting-clan?p=1477221#post1477221\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">On having Auspex/Dominate: I feel it really comes down to whether you prefer the focus on the mystic or the rulership aspects, and which do you think is better for the primary focus of the Tzimisce.</div> </div> </div> </div>I get what you mean, but to me it is more of a matter of what leadership means here.<br /> <br /> When I think about the Tzimisce as rulers, I do not think about them as commanders necessarily. It is instead as another aspect of their link to the land, as people that reign in because it is expected from them and that have the best interest of their land at heart at least in some sense, as twisted as may be, not necessarily because they're qualified as leaders. In this sense, the recourse to fear tactics comes precisely because they must overcome the lack of interpersonal talent.<br /> <br /> Sure, some do work better as Dominate users, I just think it works just fine as OoC for them. And some do not rely on fear tactics, <i>Dominate</i> or not, I think having every leadership Tzimisce be a fear monger limiting, it gets old fast.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1477124-clan-tzimisce-is-the-least-interesting-clan?p=1477232#post1477232\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Tzimisce of the Body Horror/Soulless Monster type don't really fit very well into the Gothic Horror tragic monster feel of the game.</div> </div> </div> </div>I really don't think the body horror is a problem, and as a broad game I can see the need to have non-Gothic niches here and there for players and STs that want it. But on the soulless aspect I totally agree and never liked this on the Tzimisce.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1477124-clan-tzimisce-is-the-least-interesting-clan?p=1477314#post1477314\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Brujah are the least interesting history but the most fun to play generally.</div> </div> </div> </div>Seconded, plus their characterization and agendas do have some depth despite their poor background. It isn't any hard to make a Brujah that is a really interesting and complex character.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-25T06:55:29-07:00","id":1477328,"title":"","content":"I always thought of the Tzims as ruling through information and terror. They know if you so much as think a rebellious thought, and their punishment is utterly horrific.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3598,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3598-cajunkhan","user":"CajunKhan","date":". 03-25-2022, 09:58 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3598-cajunkhan","name":"CajunKhan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3598_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1700"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-25T08:27:54-07:00","id":1477333,"title":"","content":"Personally I've always got the impression you don't usually rely on your disciplines for control anyway. Especially if you're a masquarade friendly clan like the ventrue. What's wrong the more conventional methods such as corruption, coercion, legitimate ownership and non supernatural violence afterall?<br /> <br /> I mean the fiends had an entire sub species of people who they bred to do stuff for them afterall.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":26986,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","user":"Ragged Robin","date":". 03-25-2022, 11:34 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-25T09:07:28-07:00","id":1477334,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CajunKhan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1477124-clan-tzimisce-is-the-least-interesting-clan?p=1477328#post1477328\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I always thought of the Tzims as ruling through information and terror. They know if you so much as think a rebellious thought, and their punishment is utterly horrific.</div> </div> </div> </div>Amusingly, I've always felt the Tzimisce kind of take their domination for granted. They rule because they are rulers, ex facto.<br /> <br /> They don't put much effort into it beyond that and if you disobey, you die.<br /> <br /> So Dominate works for them but so would physical intimidation powers if you wanted to give them something like Potence.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-25T09:47:07-07:00","id":1477340,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1477124-clan-tzimisce-is-the-least-interesting-clan?p=1477334#post1477334\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Amusingly, I've always felt the Tzimisce kind of take their domination for granted. They rule because they are rulers, ex facto.<br /> <br /> They don't put much effort into it beyond that and if you disobey, you die.<br /> <br /> So Dominate works for them but so would physical intimidation powers if you wanted to give them something like Potence.</div> </div> </div> </div>I have often thought that Tzimisce should be a bit more physically imposing. Well, Zulo form does that, but I can see a physical Discipline as being appropriate. Potence seems reasonable, though I could actually see Fortitude as being one of their Disciplines. Altering their physical forms make make them resistant to pain and injury. Being open rulers requires putting themselves in public and in danger. Even the conservatism of the Clan seems as though it should make them unyielding in mind and body. Then again, does that give us Animalism, Fortitude, and Protean as their Disciplines? Sounds kind of familiar.<br /> <br /> Hmmmm, maybe the Gangrel could just be a Tzimisce bloodline. Wild Tzimisce who have abandoned rulership of their domain to live in closer communion with nature. It's a weird idea, but in some ways it kinda makes sense.<br /> <br /> I can see all kinds of potentially appropriate Disciplines for them. It's one reason why I like tying them to the Revenant families. Bratovitches rule through physical intimidation, while the Zantosa are more charming, and so on.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1129-sergeant-brother","name":"Sergeant Brother","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1129_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-25T11:05:57-07:00","id":1477344,"title":"","content":"The issue with Dominate is that Tzmisce have always been disunified and an organizational mess. It was why the Tremere could easily avoid being stomped by then within a decade. Every clan with Dominate is well organized, without exception. The Tzmisce don't have the organization for it, it simply isn't a cultural fit. If we HAD to get rid of Visc, the sanest way to do it would be Auspex,Animalism and... Thaumaturgy.... Fortitude would be a good fit I guess if you really want to cut them off from flesh manipulation or magic. Protean is simply <i>beneath </i>most Tzmisce.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-25T11:37:47-07:00","id":1477345,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1477124-clan-tzimisce-is-the-least-interesting-clan?p=1477344#post1477344\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Protean is simply <i>beneath </i>most Tzmisce.</div> </div> </div> </div>I *really* need you to sell that idea better before I am going to even contemplate it. Protean is such a perfect fit for the Tzimisce in my opinion. For Earth Meld if *nothing* else, given how they have traditionally been tied to their land/territory. It's so obvious that they basically recreated Earth Meld, but bigger and better, using a blend of Vicissitude and Koldunic Sorcery in earlier editions. And before they changed how Protean-claws worked, adding Agg-damage onto your Zulo form with it seemed like a ridiculously obvious upgrade to me. Ignoring the adaptive powers of Protean is one of the main reasons I have so much contempt for Metamorphosists that focus exclusively on Vicissitude.<br /> <br /> You know what's beneath most Tzimisce? The rest of the world when they use Protean to transform into a bat, owl, raven, eagle, etc., and soar through the skies like the majestic badasses they are.<br /> <br /> There's an arbitrary snobbishness to declaring Protean &quot;beneath&quot; the Tzimisce without really clarifying what your reasoning is. Is it because the Gangrel have it and they are inferior? Is it because it turns you into animals? You're just making a declaration here that really seems like it needs a solid explanation to make any sense at all.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25886-kharnov","name":"Kharnov","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"683"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-25T12:00:17-07:00","id":1477347,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1477124-clan-tzimisce-is-the-least-interesting-clan?p=1477344#post1477344\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The issue with Dominate is that Tzmisce have always been disunified and an organizational mess. It was why the Tremere could easily avoid being stomped by then within a decade. Every clan with Dominate is well organized, without exception. The Tzmisce don't have the organization for it, it simply isn't a cultural fit. If we HAD to get rid of Visc, the sanest way to do it would be Auspex,Animalism and... Thaumaturgy.... Fortitude would be a good fit I guess if you really want to cut them off from flesh manipulation or magic</div> </div> </div> </div>Frankly, this is just outright wrong. The Tzimisce are actually one of the MOST unified clans since there was a Council of Voivodes that mean that unlike other clans, the Tzimisce actually had a central structure.<br /> <br /> They all answered to Yorak who answered to the Tzimise Antediluvian too.<br /> <br /> So no, this is not true and is a weird claim when most Clans have no structure whatsoever.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> . Protean is simply <i>beneath </i>most Tzmisce. </div> </div> </div>If a Discipline can do everything another Discipline, especially a central discipline like Protean, can do and more, it's a shittily designed OP Discipline.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-25T12:20:21-07:00","id":1477348,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1477124-clan-tzimisce-is-the-least-interesting-clan?p=1477344#post1477344\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It was why the Tremere could easily avoid being stomped by then within a decade.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh please, they were the designers pet project, smugled from Ars Magica, nothing more and had redicolus plot armour<br /> The Tzimsice, contrary of popular belife, are organized... were<br /> The legions of vassals, - usually Nosferatu and Gangrel, who were <i>allowed</i> to stay on their domain and hunt, and not treated like some animals (well, the Tzimsice are suprisingly in favour of vampiric equality, so to speak eg. there are the Tzimisce in question and every are equially benath him, but not treated differently; Nosferatu, Brujah, theye were equal and sometimes higly vallued in their eyes) and the simple fact they were treated &quot;good&quot; was usually enough to keep them loyal without any blood oath - web of children and their chilrens children, and their children's children's children, bound like hell with not only by blood but wit ancient rituals, not to mention the Ravenant and their nightmarish creations, be it an minor army of szlachta or even a Vhozd or two...<br /> Lets put aside koldunism, tho' if you were a Tzimisce land lorde back then, it was basically a requirement to know Koldunism, the spirits of the land they bound with blood and ancient oaths, to the point, the Tzimisce wre organized enough not to hand the Shadow Lords their furry behind to them, and freed (mostly) Kupala, but kept them at bay<br /> Not something most of the vampires could tell about themselves<br /> And if you read the older materials, it is described, the Tzimsice then worked hard and together, to keep their Land &quot;clean&quot;, Landlords gather in certain times of the year, when the stars were right, shared blood , transformed in to Zulo and hunted down the evil spirits &quot;kupalas&quot; of their land.<br /> Actually, if you look closely, the inhumane Tzimisce were spiritual enough to make a better job than the Garou, keeping the Wyrm spirits down, wich is frankly, hilarious; and their Koldun - either by oath and ancient pacts, either forcing and commanding, - but commanded the spirits of nature and had the ability to curse you to the point mother nature turned against you; (From players guide to the High Clans: Nemesis of the Living Earth: Beginning a long malediction lasting from midnight to sunrise, a koldun may name a target as an enemy of nature. If successful, the victim finds that the elements turn against it to harm it.)<br /> Lets put aside koldunism<br /> The central government of the Tzimisce, so to speak, was the Council of Voivodes, guided by the Viceroy. The Viceroy was elected by his peers, but his tenure was set &quot;for life&quot;. However, given the jealousy and suspicion among the Clan, there was a relatively regular progression of Viceroys, as one after another fell to the political or physical traps set by another ambitious clan member. The Council had anywhere from less than a dozen to nearly a hundred members during the Dark Ages, making it the single most influential factor in Clan politics.<br /> The rights and treatment of guests forms an indelible part of Tzimisce culture. There are many archaic rules concerning deportment, manners, greetings, goodbyes, allowances, and settlement of grievances, but there are a few Clan-wide obligations that are always honored. A guest of the Tzimisce is entitled to several things:<br /> Shelter and nourishment for three days and three nights (not counting the night of arrival)<br /> The protection of the host against third-party aggressors<br /> Suspension of inter-family grievances for the duration of the stay<br /> The best quarters in the home of the host (up to and including the host's own chambers)<br /> However, the guest also has a few obligations that makes them worthy of such special treatment<br /> A ritual exchange of gifts or services (on arriving, departing, or sometimes both)<br /> Respecting the host's boundaries and property<br /> Not needlessly angering the host or any of his family<br /> Not staying any longer than the requisite three days and three nights unless invited to.<br /> The balance of these laws is to ensure that no advantage is taken of either the host or guest \u2013 a Fiend's honor can be completely shattered by infringing upon either one of these sets of rules.<br /> Given the warfare that exists between lineages of Tzimisce, exercising patience and honoring these laws is a way to ensure that there is always a sort of &quot;neutral ground&quot; where combative families can meet and prevent any further outrages. The older a Tzimisce is, the more seriously they treat these laws, for they remember the nights when the only shelter to be had was in the domain of a rival voivode, when travel was arduous and only undertaken when necessary. Most elder Tzimisce respect these laws in the modern nights, but their grandchilder may not even be aware that these laws exist, much less still enforced in their ancestors' domains. Minor breaches can be forgiven, though some effort must be made to show that the trespasser is apologetic. Major breaches can fix a Tzimisce's reputation in a very bad way \u2013 slaughtering guests during the day is a sure way to make sure no one comes to visit you, or ever wants to make a deal.<br /> <br /> The Tzimsice were organized as HELL, and a serious force to be retcon with<br /> Logically, the Tremere had 0 chance, but had plot armour, rediculous plot armor, bacause not only the Tzimisce were against them but the Nosferatu (and tey had their &quot;network&quot; back then too) and the Gangrel too, tho I guess not on a clan level... Immagine a Great Gather (not a Gather or a Revel, a really Great Gather that summons all the Gangrel of the area, and nearby areas, or anyone who could travel, or god forbid, a <i>Grand Revel</i><span style=\"color:#3A3A3A\"><span style=\"font-family:rubik\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">, </span></span></span>which are essentially wars and battles involving the entire clan, and the Clan decides, kay hunt down these upstart sorcerers...<br /> Scary<br /> Scarier then the Tzimsice, actually<br /> Anyhow, Vicissitude actually have it roots in the in South Slavic folklore, where a vampire was believed to pass through several distinct stages in its development. The first 40 days were considered decisive for the making of a vampire; it started out as an invisible shadow and then gradually gained strength from the lifeblood of the living, forming a (typically invisible) jelly-like, boneless mass, and eventually building up a human-like body nearly identical to the one the person had had in life.<br /> Sure, other sources contributed too, but even if you take the aproach, Vicissitude is the twisted reflection how God formed Adam and Lilith from earth, like a sculptor (then built a second woman, allegedly the Crone from inside out, first bones, then muscles, then skin and Adam was awake and couldn't look the creature with love, so God threw her out from Eden then came the 3rd atempt, Eve) then after making sure Adam was asleep, took a bone from him and formed that in to another being? I think Vicissitue had a place in the VtM<br /> As protean? Meh... advanced protean, I guess...?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":23890,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23890-shadeprowler","user":"Shadeprowler","date":". 03-25-2022, 03:24 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23890-shadeprowler","name":"Shadeprowler","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23890_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-25T12:23:55-07:00","id":1477349,"title":"","content":"For their discipline spread, I go back to Necroscope. The Necroscope Wamphyri don't precisely have Viccissitude. They have something akin to 3 or 4 dots worth of Requiem Protean, and the ability to turn people into monsters or furniture, but only if they can spend a great deal of time in their laboratories. So the V5 Protean with Vic elements works fine, but I'd add some kind of slow ritual ability to it.<br /> <br /> They all have telepathy, and superhuman senses, so Auspex is obvious.<br /> <br /> And I'd give them a physical discipline. Which one is hard to say, since they are superhuman in a way that basically amounts to them having 6 to 8 in all three physicals. I'd probably go with Potence.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3598-cajunkhan","name":"CajunKhan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3598_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1700"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-25T12:28:29-07:00","id":1477351,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shadeprowler</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Tzimsice were organized as HELL, and a serious force to be retcon with<br /> Logically, the Tremere had 0 chance, but had plot armour, rediculous plot armor, bacause not only the Tzimisce were against them but the Nosferatu (and tey had their &quot;network&quot; back then too) and the Gangrel too, tho I guess not on a clan level... Immagine a Great Gather (not a Gather or a Revel, a really Great Gather that summons all the Gangrel of the area, and nearby areas, or anyone who could travel, or god forbid, a Grand Revel, which are essentially wars and battles involving the entire clan, and the Clan decides, kay hunt down these upstart sorcerers...</div> </div> </div> </div>I strongly disagree.<br /> <br /> Mind you, I view this as a WORLD of Darkness and the Tremere are the equivalent of a Tradition of Mages from the Modern Nights defecting to the Vampire Clan. It's a faction that is already massively powerful and organized becoming another faction. It's not something that was weak that joined, it was something incredibly POWERFUL that joined.<br /> <br /> And by the time the Omen War broke out, they had already diablerized the Salubri Clan with the almost certain explicit help of Saulot, which meant it was two Clans going at it with one of them being an <i>awakened Antediluvian</i> throwing his power into the market. For whatever reason, the Tzimisce Antediluvian chose not to help.<br /> (We know this is because in Gehenna, he actually can kill Tremere at any point he wants)<br /> <br /> The Tremere also had made a compact with what is almost certainly Kupala and later have the backing of the Ventrue. The Ventrue are the biggest allies the Tremere have because, well, they're happy to throw money and troops the Tremere's way if they can steal the Tzimisce's lands.<br /> <br /> The Gangrel and Nosferatu hate the Tremere for their actions in creating the Gargoyles but just because they hate them doesn't mean they're willing to risk their skins against them, especially since the Gargoyles are a Bloodline 100% enslaved to them right now.<br /> <br /> The Tremere survived because they were already a wrecking ball in the supernatural world.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-25T12:43:03-07:00","id":1477353,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sergeant Brother</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1477124-clan-tzimisce-is-the-least-interesting-clan?p=1477340#post1477340\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hmmmm, maybe the Gangrel could just be a Tzimisce bloodline. Wild Tzimisce who have abandoned rulership of their domain to live in closer communion with nature. It's a weird idea, but in some ways it kinda makes sense.</div> </div> </div> </div>Don't some believe Gangrel to be a Baali bloodline, or vice versa? This is the best part of VTM, the speculation!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><div align=\"left\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/7.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26764-vilenecromancer","name":"Vilenecromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26764_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"247"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-25T12:52:17-07:00","id":1477354,"title":"","content":"But yes, I also think its good to note the Tremere didn't WIN the Omen War.<br /> <br /> The Inquisition and Sabbat Revolt ended it.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-25T13:07:59-07:00","id":1477356,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shadeprowler</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1477124-clan-tzimisce-is-the-least-interesting-clan?p=1477348#post1477348\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Libertarian kool-aid</div> </div> </div> </div>Bruh they're landlords inspired by Poland-lithuania, a country that fell apart because the lords wanted as much autonomy as possible. The Tzmisce's whole deal is that they don't give a fuck about what goes on outside their borders and they're so bound to the land they're from it's a clan weakness. Being polite =/= getting along. <br /> <br /> Comparitively, the Tremere are supremely organized, and they've got a discipline with great economic value and which has it's value increased by being... really organized. Really organized and really motivated (to survive) but like, if the Tremere were thousands of years older, the Tzmisce would've been wiped out by now. It's just basic sense. The Tzmisce are too obsessed with their own domains to really try and help another Tzmisce deal with a Tremere problem. The Tremere are united enough that they would send reinforcements across the country to deal with a problematic Tzmisce. <i>Of fucking course</i> the Tremere would do better in the Omen war. The Tremere are a sound organization and they don't need plot armour to win. If anything the Tzmisce need plot armour to even hold domain rather than get regulated to the side like the capadocians. Ventrue, Toreador, Brujah, Malks... they all make better rulers than Tzmisce. <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-25T14:07:49-07:00","id":1477358,"title":"","content":"Important question about the Tzimisce<br /> <br /> What is Kupala\u2019s relationship to the Tzimisce? Friendly? Hostile? Somewhere in between?<br /> <br /> Also, what is Kupala? A Bane? An Earthbound demon? A Titan from Scion (probably not \ud83d\ude0a)?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Amethyst is my birthstone. She/they.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26996-amethyst","name":"Amethyst","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26996_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"873"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-25T14:23:08-07:00","id":1477360,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Amethyst</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1477124-clan-tzimisce-is-the-least-interesting-clan?p=1477358#post1477358\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Important question about the Tzimisce<br /> <br /> What is Kupala\u2019s relationship to the Tzimisce? Friendly? Hostile? Somewhere in between?<br /> <br /> Also, what is Kupala? A Bane? An Earthbound demon? A Titan from Scion (probably not \ud83d\ude0a)?</div> </div> </div> </div>I always have the view that when describing the difference between spiritual entities, you're probably best thinking that every race will interpret it through their own lens.<br /> <br /> A Garou finds the idea of Demon: The Fallen RIDICULOUS.<br /> <br /> And a Demon from Demon: The Fallen would roll their eyes at Garou stupidity.<br /> <br /> Changelings giggle at both.<br /> <br /> And they're all three objectively right about their reality.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-25T14:24:11-07:00","id":1477361,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1477124-clan-tzimisce-is-the-least-interesting-clan?p=1477356#post1477356\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Bruh they're landlords inspired by Poland-lithuania, a country that fell apart because the lords wanted as much autonomy as possible. The Tzmisce's whole deal is that they don't give a fuck about what goes on outside their borders and they're so bound to the land they're from it's a clan weakness. Being polite =/= getting along.<br /> <br /> Comparitively, the Tremere are supremely organized, and they've got a discipline with great economic value and which has it's value increased by being... really organized. Really organized and really motivated (to survive) but like, if the Tremere were thousands of years older, the Tzmisce would've been wiped out by now. It's just basic sense. The Tzmisce are too obsessed with their own domains to really try and help another Tzmisce deal with a Tremere problem. The Tremere are united enough that they would send reinforcements across the country to deal with a problematic Tzmisce. <i>Of fucking course</i> the Tremere would do better in the Omen war. The Tremere are a sound organization and they don't need plot armour to win. If anything the Tzmisce need plot armour to even hold domain rather than get regulated to the side like the capadocians. Ventrue, Toreador, Brujah, Malks... they all make better rulers than Tzmisce.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Just a reminder the Tremere were a 1000 year old organization dating back to Ancient Rome by the time they were created.<br /> <br /> They also DIDN'T win.<br /> <br /> They were stalemating the Tzimisce until the Tzimsice Elders were wiped out by their own children.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-25T15:13:35-07:00","id":1477366,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Amethyst</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1477124-clan-tzimisce-is-the-least-interesting-clan?p=1477358#post1477358\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Also, what is Kupala? A Bane? An Earthbound demon?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes.<br /> Also neither. You know that Malkavian story about the blind vampire bats?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> A Titan from Scion (probably not \ud83d\ude0a)? </div> </div> </div>Probably not, but I still want to say &quot;that too&quot; because the concept of making the WoD's cosmology even more convoluted by having legitimate demigods running around is hilarious. Wonder how the Setites respond to the scions of their god?<br /> <br /> Wait, Kupala is a pagan deity too, so what does that mean for the Tzimisce in this crossover?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><sup><i>Prone to hyperbole</i></sup>","edited":{"userid":26836,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26836-rhywbeth","user":"Rhywbeth","date":". 03-25-2022, 06:30 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26836-rhywbeth","name":"Rhywbeth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26836_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"377"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-25T15:19:31-07:00","id":1477368,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rhywbeth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1477124-clan-tzimisce-is-the-least-interesting-clan?p=1477366#post1477366\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Probably not, but I still want to say &quot;that too&quot; because the concept of making the WoD's cosmology even more convoluted by having legitimate demigods running around is hilarious. Wonder how the Setites respond to the scions of their god?</div> </div> </div> </div>Theirs going to be a question of whether their truly the scion of set or if its just some deluded malkavian.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"https://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://www.nodiatis.com/pub/18.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27313-hello","name":"Hello","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27313_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-25T15:31:09-07:00","id":1477369,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hello</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1477124-clan-tzimisce-is-the-least-interesting-clan?p=1477368#post1477368\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Theirs going to be a question of whether their truly the scion of set or if its just some deluded malkavian.</div> </div> </div> </div>Been a while since I've looked at Scion, but I'm pretty sure demigods are alive and wielding powers Malkavians don't typically wield. Probably also got a different aura. I figure they'd be easy enough to distinguish from vampires.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><sup><i>Prone to hyperbole</i></sup>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26836-rhywbeth","name":"Rhywbeth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26836_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"377"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-25T18:21:40-07:00","id":1477379,"title":"","content":"Regarding Tzimisce Culture and Organization <br /> <br /> It is true that the Tzimisce were relatively organized, but it's also true that most medieval Voivodes were highly independent and at conflict with each other as/more often than not. If you did not have a terrifying demigod like Yorak ordering something to happen, getting the various Tzimisce warlords to cooperate was a task that'd make herding cats seem simple by comparison. Their rules regarding hospitality do not necessarily translate to camaraderie on the battlefield. And even if you could get most of them aimed at the same goal, like wiping out the Tremere, you couldn't count on them collaborating to be as effective as their numbers might indicate; some might even undermine their rivals to the detriment of the Clan's larger conflict.<br /> <br /> Regarding The Power of the Tremere<br /> <br /> It's important to remember that the first Tremere, while organized and possessing a great deal of supernatural lore, did not immediately have the broad knowledge of Thaumaturgy that they came to possess. They needed time to learn how to convert their Hermetic arts into Kindred Blood Sorcery, and even after a while the variety of Paths at their disposal was still probably limited in comparison to what they have in the Modern Nights. Which doesn't even include learning about the more basic features of the Curse and their other Disciplines. They were definitely at a disadvantage initially, and there's a good chance they wouldn't have made it, IMO, if 1) their enemies weren't relatively disorganized, and 2) they didn't have allies like the Ventrue and the support of powerful supernatural entities like Saulot and Kupala (Stars-Above and Root-Of-All were the aliases for them in the book about Ceoris IIRC).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25886-kharnov","user":"Kharnov","date":". 03-25-2022, 09:24 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25886-kharnov","name":"Kharnov","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"683"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-25T20:26:04-07:00","id":1477391,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1477124-clan-tzimisce-is-the-least-interesting-clan?p=1477356#post1477356\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Bruh they're landlords inspired by Poland-lithuania, a country that fell apart because the lords wanted as much autonomy as possible. The Tzmisce's whole deal is that they don't give a fuck about what goes on outside their borders and they're so bound to the land they're from it's a clan weakness. Being polite =/= getting along.<br /> <br /> Comparitively, the Tremere are supremely organized, and they've got a discipline with great economic value and which has it's value increased by being... really organized. Really organized and really motivated (to survive) but like, if the Tremere were thousands of years older, the Tzmisce would've been wiped out by now. It's just basic sense. The Tzmisce are too obsessed with their own domains to really try and help another Tzmisce deal with a Tremere problem. The Tremere are united enough that they would send reinforcements across the country to deal with a problematic Tzmisce. <i>Of fucking course</i> the Tremere would do better in the Omen war. The Tremere are a sound organization and they don't need plot armour to win. If anything the Tzmisce need plot armour to even hold domain rather than get regulated to the side like the capadocians. Ventrue, Toreador, Brujah, Malks... they all make better rulers than Tzmisce.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> It makes a lot of sense when you think about why revenant families either defected to the other side, or killed their masters. The tzimisce are such terrible rulers, it makes you wonder how no angry mob with torches stormed their castles during the day. That's some strong plot armor right there.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"https://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://www.nodiatis.com/pub/18.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27313-hello","name":"Hello","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27313_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-25T20:26:04-07:00","id":1477392,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1477124-clan-tzimisce-is-the-least-interesting-clan?p=1477356#post1477356\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Bruh they're landlords inspired by Poland-lithuania, a country that fell apart because the lords wanted as much autonomy as possible. The Tzmisce's whole deal is that they don't give a fuck about what goes on outside their borders and they're so bound to the land they're from it's a clan weakness. Being polite =/= getting along.<br /> <br /> Comparitively, the Tremere are supremely organized, and they've got a discipline with great economic value and which has it's value increased by being... really organized. Really organized and really motivated (to survive) but like, if the Tremere were thousands of years older, the Tzmisce would've been wiped out by now. It's just basic sense. The Tzmisce are too obsessed with their own domains to really try and help another Tzmisce deal with a Tremere problem. The Tremere are united enough that they would send reinforcements across the country to deal with a problematic Tzmisce. <i>Of fucking course</i> the Tremere would do better in the Omen war. The Tremere are a sound organization and they don't need plot armour to win. If anything the Tzmisce need plot armour to even hold domain rather than get regulated to the side like the capadocians. Ventrue, Toreador, Brujah, Malks... they all make better rulers than Tzmisce.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> It makes a lot of sense when you think about why revenant families either defected to the other side, or killed their masters. The tzimisce are such terrible rulers, it makes you wonder how no angry mob with torches stormed their castles during the day. That's some strong plot armor right there.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"https://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://www.nodiatis.com/pub/18.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27313-hello","name":"Hello","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27313_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-25T22:13:57-07:00","id":1477406,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hello</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1477124-clan-tzimisce-is-the-least-interesting-clan?p=1477392#post1477392\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It makes a lot of sense when you think about why revenant families either defected to the other side, or killed their masters. The tzimisce are such terrible rulers, it makes you wonder how no angry mob with torches stormed their castles during the day. That's some strong plot armor right there.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Tzimisce often made heavy use of the Blood Bond, which means that regardless of how terrible they were as rulers, they did often have plenty of servants that would literally lay down their lives to defend them. While they lived in a castle. A random angry mob of villagers with pitchforks and torches is going to have a hard time breaching their defences, and if they don't succeed before sundown, they are in trouble. And assuming they *did* succeed, they'd better be able to rouse every other village in the region to their side, or the Tzimisce and their minions would leave their flayed corpses hanging from the rafters as a warning to the rest. If they were lucky; if they were unlucky, the Tzimisce would leave them in a state that would make them *wish* they were dead, as a warning to the rest.<br /> <br /> Setting aside their pride on its own as a motive, kine rising up to murder their Cainite overlord is *not* the kind of precedent that the Tzimisce are going to allow to stand for obvious pragmatic reasons. Organized or not, the Clan absolutely would collectively descend on the guilty party like a legion from Hell. It didn't become possible until the Clan began literally tearing itself apart during the Anarch Revolt.<br /> <br /> Regarding Revenant families, betraying the Tzimisce and living to tell about it is the exception rather than the rule. Ask the Basarabs. Or the Danislavs, who were literally thrown under the bus by one of their own... who became a Tzimisce as a reward for betraying his kin. The Ducheski are the only family known to have succeeded at such a betrayal, and they simply traded one asshole master for another slightly-less-asshole master. Which doesn't even mention the Vlaszy, who went down with their elder Tzimisce masters during the Anarch Revolt because (supposedly) willingly Blood Bonding yourself to your Tzimisce liege was part of their family culture. Most of the Revenant families have either remained loyal to the Tzimisce and the Sabbat, or they have disappeared.<br /> <br /> We need a Spider-man meme labeled as different Clans pointed at the others yelling &quot;plot armour!&quot;<br /> <br /> Really, it just mostly comes down to the fact that even the most organized Clans were not monolithic military empires that could genocide an entire Clan out of existence without considerable risk to themselves, assuming they even had the will to do it. In case you haven't noticed, the two most prominent examples of this being attempted 1) targeted Clans that were both highly disorganized and extremely peaceful compared to their peers, and 2) failed, often creating groups of extremely militant fanatics hell-bent on vengeance as blowback for even trying. In the case of the Tzimisce, they were extremely aggressive, moderately organized, and had a powerful home-field advantage in the form of a supernatural pact with a literal demon inhabiting their territory.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25886-kharnov","user":"Kharnov","date":". 03-26-2022, 01:44 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25886-kharnov","name":"Kharnov","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"683"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-25T22:24:08-07:00","id":1477408,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kharnov</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1477124-clan-tzimisce-is-the-least-interesting-clan?p=1477406#post1477406\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The Tzimisce often made heavy use of the Blood Bond, which means that regardless of how terrible they were as rulers, they did often have plenty of servants that would literally lay down their lives to defend them. While they lived in a castle. A random angry mob of villagers with pitchforks and torches is going to have a hard time breaching their defences, and if they don't succeed before sundown, they are in trouble. And assuming they *did* succeed, they'd better be able to rouse every other village in the region to their side, or the Tzimisce and their minions would leave their flayed corpses hanging from the rafters as a warning to the rest. If they were lucky; if they were unlucky, the Tzimisce would leave them in a state that would make them *wish* they were dead, as a warning to the rest.<br /> <br /> Setting aside their pride on its own as a motive, kine rising up to murder their Cainite overlord is *not* the kind of precedent that the Tzimisce are going to allow to stand for obvious pragmatic reasons. Organized or not, the Clan absolutely would collectively descend on the guilty party like a legion from Hell. It didn't become possible until the Clan began literally tearing itself apart during the Anarch Revolt.<br /> <br /> Regarding Revenant families, betraying the Tzimisce and living to tell about it is the exception rather than the rule. Ask the Basarabs. Or the Danislavs, who were literally thrown under the bus by one of their own... who became a Tzimisce as a reward for betraying his kin. The Ducheski are the only family known to have succeeded at such a betrayal, and they simply traded one asshole master for another slightly-less-asshole master. Which doesn't even mention the Vlaszy, who went down with their elder Tzimisce masters during the Anarch Revolt because (supposedly) willingly Blood Bonding yourself to your Tzimisce liege was part of their Clan culture. Most of the Revenant families have either remained loyal to the Tzimisce and the Sabbat, or they have disappeared.<br /> <br /> We need a Spider-man meme labeled as different Clans pointed at the others yelling &quot;plot armour!&quot;<br /> <br /> Really, it just mostly comes down to the fact that even the most organized Clans were not monolithic military empires that could genocide an entire Clan out of existence without considerable risk to themselves, assuming they even had the will to do it. In case you haven't noticed, the two most prominent examples of this being attempted 1) targeted Clans that were both highly disorganized and extremely peaceful compared to their peers, and 2) failed, often creating groups of extremely militant fanatics hell-bent on vengeance as blowback for even trying. In the case of the Tzimisce, they were extremely aggressive, moderately organized, and had a powerful home-field advantage in the form of a supernatural pact with a literal demon inhabiting their territory.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I feel a lot of revenant families were loyal to their masters because they were raised in a culture where the tzimisce were given utmost importance, not entirely because of a blood bond. Its going to be impossible to blood bond an entire village.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"https://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://www.nodiatis.com/pub/18.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27313-hello","name":"Hello","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27313_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-25T22:40:13-07:00","id":1477411,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hello</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1477124-clan-tzimisce-is-the-least-interesting-clan?p=1477408#post1477408\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I feel a lot of revenant families were loyal to their masters because they were raised in a culture where the tzimisce were given utmost importance, not entirely because of a blood bond. Its going to be impossible to blood bond an entire village.</div> </div> </div> </div>1) You don't need to Blood Bond the village. You just need to Blood Bond or hold onto the loyalty of the people that can murder the village if they give you side-eye. That's the point I was making. Or even just enough people to keep the villagers out of your castle until you can wake up and rip them to pieces with your Zulo-form. Or just escape to another castle and plot your revenge. I'm just challenging the idea that angry mobs of villagers swarming their castles would be enough by itself to unseat the Tzimisce.<br /> <br /> And regarding Revenants, I agree you don't necessarily need to Blood Bond them. Putting aside indoctrination, teasing them with the possibility of the Embrace can work wonders. Again, see the Danislavs.<br /> <br /> 2) To be fair, probably an example of early-installment weirdness. But there is an example of a Tzimisce voivode putting a (probably weak) Blood Bond on the local population by putting his vitae into their water-supply: <a href=\"https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Hedeon_Yaroslavich\" target=\"_blank\">Hedeon Yaroslavich</a>.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25886-kharnov","name":"Kharnov","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"683"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-25T22:49:14-07:00","id":1477412,"title":"","content":"Castles routinely held out against besieging armies for months, sometimes years. It\u2019s highly unlikely that an angry mob of peasants are going to get in before the sun goes down.<br /> <br /> Though, how bad are the Tzimisce as rulers really? Would their subjects just live in constant misery? It seems like the honorable traditions of the Old Clan would cause them to be protective of loyal subjects. Of course, disloyal ones would suffer horribly. Kind of a carrot and stick situation.<br /> <br /> As Roose Bolton says: \u201cA peaceful land, a quiet people.\u201d","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1129-sergeant-brother","name":"Sergeant Brother","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1129_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-25T23:43:25-07:00","id":1477413,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1477124-clan-tzimisce-is-the-least-interesting-clan?p=1477361#post1477361\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Just a reminder the Tremere were a 1000 year old organization dating back to Ancient Rome by the time they were created.<br /> <br /> They also DIDN'T win.<br /> <br /> They were stalemating the Tzimisce until the Tzimsice Elders were wiped out by their own children.</div> </div> </div> </div>Even then, not ALL the Tzimisce elders. Who holds praxis in most of Eastern Europe today? Hint: it ain't the Tremere.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3505-matt-the-bruins-fan","name":"Matt the Bruins fan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3505_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-26T02:12:58-07:00","id":1477421,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Matt the Bruins fan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1477124-clan-tzimisce-is-the-least-interesting-clan?p=1477413#post1477413\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Even then, not ALL the Tzimisce elders. Who holds praxis in most of Eastern Europe today? Hint: it ain't the Tremere.</div> </div> </div> </div>A less charitable person might actually suggest the Tremere moving their HQ from Ceoris to Austria was a sort of...retreat.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-26T10:47:50-07:00","id":1477452,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ragged Robin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1477124-clan-tzimisce-is-the-least-interesting-clan?p=1477333#post1477333\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Personally I've always got the impression you don't usually rely on your disciplines for control anyway. Especially if you're a masquarade friendly clan like the ventrue. What's wrong the more conventional methods such as corruption, coercion, legitimate ownership and non supernatural violence afterall?<br /> <br /> I mean the fiends had an entire sub species of people who they bred to do stuff for them afterall.</div> </div> </div> </div>Indeed, but while I don't agree on MWIS' extreme take on the role of Disciplines, there's still a link between Discipline spread and theme/style of a clan. Most successful Ventrue do not rely on either Dominate or Presence a lot of the time, yet it fits them to send a message and work as a fallback plan for their main strategy when the usual methods fail. Otherwise they would also be better with any other spread, maybe all Physical, because they don't need Dominate and Presence for their shtick. It also help to keep the clan's themes and methods when you have a member that isn't personally that good at their thing (of course, they'll also not be that good with the Discipline rolls, but they'll at least have a clear advantage over mortals).<br /> <br /> Were the Tzimisce regularly competent with personally commanding people, I would at least find it thematic to give them Dominate. Were them expected to be regularly hypnotizing and doing BS to other's minds, Dominate would make a lot of sense. But as lords that mostly live isolated in their havens and most receive their orders through messengers and servants, that you obey not because of their wonderful or fearsome personal presence, but because you know you belong to them even if you never saw them personally, then I don't think Dominate fits in well.<br /> <br /> And again, some will do any or all of those things, they can and should buy Dominate as OoC, the clan probably has reasonably easy access to it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kharnov</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1477124-clan-tzimisce-is-the-least-interesting-clan?p=1477345#post1477345\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There's an arbitrary snobbishness to declaring Protean &quot;beneath&quot; the Tzimisce without really clarifying what your reasoning is. Is it because the Gangrel have it and they are inferior? Is it because it turns you into animals? You're just making a declaration here that really seems like it needs a solid explanation to make any sense at all.</div> </div> </div> </div>I second this. While I'm fine with Vicissitude, Protean also fits them really well and the &quot;beneath&quot; commentary is odd at best.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1477124-clan-tzimisce-is-the-least-interesting-clan?p=1477347#post1477347\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Frankly, this is just outright wrong. The Tzimisce are actually one of the MOST unified clans since there was a Council of Voivodes that mean that unlike other clans, the Tzimisce actually had a central structure.</div> </div> </div> </div>Also second this. While I don't think they're as organized as the Ventrue, and they're certainly not as organized as the Tremere, those are very high bars on themselves. It is just that their organization is predicated in law and tradition instead of personal leadership and hierarchy (they have one, but are mostly left to their own devices instead of constantly answering to superiors).<br /> <br /> I don't think their style of organization meshes well with Dominate, but saying they're not highly organized is simply plain wrong.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vilenecromancer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1477124-clan-tzimisce-is-the-least-interesting-clan?p=1477353#post1477353\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Don't some believe Gangrel to be a Baali bloodline, or vice versa? This is the best part of VTM, the speculation!</div> </div> </div> </div>Some believe each and every single clan to either be a Baali bloodline or vice-versa.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Amethyst</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1477124-clan-tzimisce-is-the-least-interesting-clan?p=1477358#post1477358\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Important question about the TzimisceWhat is Kupala\u2019s relationship to the Tzimisce? Friendly? Hostile? Somewhere in between?<br /> <br /> Also, what is Kupala? A Bane? An Earthbound demon? A Titan from Scion (probably not \ud83d\ude0a)?</div> </div> </div> </div>Somewhere in between. They have some mutual understanding, but at the end of the day the Tzimisce freed Kupala to an extend, but keep it bound tp another, and Kupala knows, so they're in a complicated dance.<br /> <br /> A lot of later material gives more credence to Kupala being an Earthbound, but that's mostly because Demon was the last line before the end of the world, so it is actually in the air if it is a very powerful Earthbound, a very powerful Wyrm Head, a very powerful Dream God, or some weird other option that includes any, all or none of those.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kharnov</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1477124-clan-tzimisce-is-the-least-interesting-clan?p=1477406#post1477406\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Tzimisce often made heavy use of the Blood Bond, which means that regardless of how terrible they were as rulers, they did often have plenty of servants that would literally lay down their lives to defend them. While they lived in a castle. A random angry mob of villagers with pitchforks and torches is going to have a hard time breaching their defences, and if they don't succeed before sundown, they are in trouble. And assuming they *did* succeed, they'd better be able to rouse every other village in the region to their side, or the Tzimisce and their minions would leave their flayed corpses hanging from the rafters as a warning to the rest. If they were lucky; if they were unlucky, the Tzimisce would leave them in a state that would make them *wish* they were dead, as a warning to the rest.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not to say that for most villagers of the time there was no such a thing as an actual vampire lord. There was the lord of the castle, and the fact it was a vampire was both unknown and meaningless. To them there was the Voivode and the next Voivode, all of them equally ruthless and disinterested on the commoners' personal affairs. Why bother? That when the vampire lord was known in any capacity, as most probably ruled from the shadows through their living kin (something people forget the Tzimisce used to do back then similarly to how the Giovanni operate today, Revenants or not).<br /> <br /> It is like Strahd in Ravenloft. People in Barovia call their lord the Devil Strahd, but they don't really think he's a vampire, they think he's a lineage of ruthless but ultimately mortal lords. And to most of them it would change little if it actually was the case, many people with actual claims to Strahd's throne should he been eliminated wouldn't be any less evil, maybe just less competent and ultimately worse for Barovia.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sergeant Brother</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1477124-clan-tzimisce-is-the-least-interesting-clan?p=1477412#post1477412\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Though, how bad are the Tzimisce as rulers really? Would their subjects just live in constant misery? It seems like the honorable traditions of the Old Clan would cause them to be protective of loyal subjects. Of course, disloyal ones would suffer horribly. Kind of a carrot and stick situation.</div> </div> </div> </div>Throwing your people in misery in the Middle Ages usually means throwing yourself in misery with them as they become far less productive. Imagine if on top of that you need them healthy for your own dietary needs.<br /> <br /> While they can be terrifying for anyone facing them, the Tzimisce, or any vampire lord for that matter, back then or in the modern nights, probably had the best interests of the people mostly in mind as rulers of their territory, so their territory has the means to become rich, prosperous and powerful. There are many ways you can be a good ruler for the land, and many ways you can be a terrible ruler, but they have little to do with you being a good or evil person and more to do with you being competent or stupidly self-serving (instead of pragmatic self-serving).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-26T20:11:50-07:00","id":1477510,"title":"","content":"1. I've lived in Eastern Europe and I have to say that the people of Eastern Europe are perfectly civilized and have all the components of a civilization and civilized people. That fact they are at a distance from London, New York, and Peoria doesn't mean much except we traditionally write them off. Relevant here is that even if you decide the Tzimsice are Ventrue, they are still powerful and not to be written off as weirdos just because you think they have an accent. <br /> <br /> 2. I replaced Kupula with Yog Sothoth to make them strange. Vicissitude is not just flesh becoming soft and malleable, but metaphorically reality becoming soft and malleable.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1208-grumpy-rpg-reviews","name":"Grumpy RPG Reviews","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1208_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1888"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-26T20:46:53-07:00","id":1477512,"title":"","content":"One of my players is a Polish woman and basically rolls her eyes at all things Tzimisce and wishes they had a different Clan. Also, a lot of the random Polish words in their clan that make it just sound silly to her.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-26T21:41:51-07:00","id":1477514,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1477124-clan-tzimisce-is-the-least-interesting-clan?p=1477512#post1477512\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">One of my players is a Polish woman and basically rolls her eyes at all things Tzimisce and wishes they had a different Clan. Also, a lot of the random Polish words in their clan that make it just sound silly to her.</div> </div> </div> </div>Considering White Wolf basically never cared about context for the words, titles, and ideas that inspired their world this is no surprise. Just look at the Assamites, Ravnos, Metis, Windegos, Baali, Samedi, and so...so much more.<br /> <br /> This isn't always a bad thing, but sometimes you got stereotypical concepts that are really offensive when you think about it. Like the Metis...especially the metis.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><div align=\"left\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/7.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26764-vilenecromancer","name":"Vilenecromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26764_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"247"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-26T21:54:06-07:00","id":1477515,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vilenecromancer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1477124-clan-tzimisce-is-the-least-interesting-clan?p=1477514#post1477514\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Considering White Wolf basically never cared about context for the words, titles, and ideas that inspired their world this is no surprise. Just look at the Assamites, Ravnos, Metis, Windegos, Baali, Samedi, and so...so much more.<br /> <br /> This isn't always a bad thing, but sometimes you got stereotypical concepts that are really offensive when you think about it.</div> </div> </div> </div>If you're a fan of Outstar's channels, she also being Polish, her playing Vampire: The Masquerade: Redemption, you can watch her struggle not to get pissed off the more and more they randomly throw out polish words that make no sense.<br /> <br /> &quot;The Tzimisce's cannon fodder ghouls are named <span style=\"color:#ea3724\">Szlachta. </span>Which means nobility and no that doesn't make any sense.&quot;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Like the Metis...especially the metis </div> </div> </div>Having actual Native American relatives, yeah.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-26T22:15:09-07:00","id":1477518,"title":"","content":"I always thought the Tzims naming them szlachta was a very in-character example of cruel mockery, rather like &quot;ancilae&quot;, which means house-slave, and shows the cruel way ancients think of younger vampires.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3598-cajunkhan","name":"CajunKhan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3598_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1700"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-27T02:25:10-07:00","id":1477522,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1477124-clan-tzimisce-is-the-least-interesting-clan?p=1477512#post1477512\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">One of my players is a Polish woman and basically rolls her eyes at all things Tzimisce and wishes they had a different Clan. Also, a lot of the random Polish words in their clan that make it just sound silly to her.</div> </div> </div> </div>Weirdly the bulgarian guy I know is positively gleeful about playing them. I suspect its a matter of personal taste.<br /> <br /> Edit-its also probably worth noting in Revised a big chunk of the clan are Mexican, African, Greek and Indian respectively.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":26986,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","user":"Ragged Robin","date":". 03-27-2022, 05:29 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-27T11:05:50-07:00","id":1477535,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1477124-clan-tzimisce-is-the-least-interesting-clan?p=1477512#post1477512\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">One of my players is a Polish woman and basically rolls her eyes at all things Tzimisce and wishes they had a different Clan. Also, a lot of the random Polish words in their clan that make it just sound silly to her.</div> </div> </div> </div>The WW Word Salad is a mess everywhere. If you understand the language of a word, you roll your eyes for that word in how WW used it.<br /> <br /> Other than that, it seems to be more a matter of taste than anything. I mean, it sure isn't good that the clan is so heavily tied to the Carpathians and all that, but that can be corrected as they were already doing in Revised.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-27T11:24:35-07:00","id":1477537,"title":"","content":"The Carpathians is where Tzim himself laired and periodically popped out baby 4th gens. Of course the Carpathians would have a large number of powerful, old Tzims. Just as most of the old Lasombras are from the Mediterranean, where Lasombra himself laired and periodically popped out baby 4rth gens. I've always thought that whatever region an Ante laired in being dominated by that particular clan made perfect sense. The only ones for whom that wouldn't be true would be the Gangrel and Ravnos.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3598-cajunkhan","name":"CajunKhan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3598_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1700"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-27T11:42:04-07:00","id":1477538,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1477124-clan-tzimisce-is-the-least-interesting-clan?p=1477512#post1477512\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">One of my players is a Polish woman and basically rolls her eyes at all things Tzimisce and wishes they had a different Clan. Also, a lot of the random Polish words in their clan that make it just sound silly to her.</div> </div> </div> </div>The fact that the two primary-Sabbat Clans are specifically culturally Iberian and Easter European does seem to echo some traditional English xenophobia. I\u2019m not accusing the writers of said prejudice! Just that it\u2019s in popular anglosphere culture (including via Bram Stoker) and they unknowingly reproduced it by drawing on those roots.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-27T12:13:56-07:00","id":1477539,"title":"","content":"<br /> I always thought it was because the two best early Dracula movies starred an Eastern European and a Spaniard.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://www.denofgeek.com/wp-content/uploads/2017/06/dracula-bela-lugosi.jpg?fit=970%2C545\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://www.denofgeek.com/wp-content/uploads/2017/06/dracula-bela-lugosi.jpg?fit=970%2C545\" target=\"_blank\"> </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://www.denofgeek.com/wp-content/uploads/2017/06/dracula-bela-lugosi.jpg?fit=970%2C545\" target=\"_blank\"> https://www.denofgeek.com/wp-content/uploads/2017/06/dracula-bela-lugosi.jpg?fit=970%2C545 </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://i.guim.co.uk/img/media/8d7256adf1d7d4d97e725653e463317b6a038aa8/79_516_5812_3487/master/5812.jpg?width=465&amp;quality=45&amp;auto=format&amp;fit=max&amp;dpr=2&amp;s=2bb8b1eace066c000f2a7b726b467d56\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://i.guim.co.uk/img/media/8d7256adf1d7d4d97e725653e463317b6a038aa8/79_516_5812_3487/master/5812.jpg?width=465&amp;quality=45&amp;auto=format&amp;fit=max&amp;dpr=2&amp;s=2bb8b1eace066c000f2a7b726b467d56\" target=\"_blank\"> </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://i.guim.co.uk/img/media/8d7256adf1d7d4d97e725653e463317b6a038aa8/79_516_5812_3487/master/5812.jpg?width=465&amp;quality=45&amp;auto=format&amp;fit=max&amp;dpr=2&amp;s=2bb8b1eace066c000f2a7b726b467d56\" target=\"_blank\"> https://i.guim.co.uk/img/media/8d7256adf1d7d4d97e725653e463317b6a038aa8/79_516_5812_3487/master/5812.jpg?width=465&amp;quality=45&amp;auto=format&amp;fit=max&amp;dpr=2&amp;s=2bb8b1eace066c000f2a7b726b467d56 </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3598,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3598-cajunkhan","user":"CajunKhan","date":". 03-27-2022, 03:17 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3598-cajunkhan","name":"CajunKhan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3598_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1700"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-27T13:02:02-07:00","id":1477543,"title":"","content":"The Lasombra are Anne Rice's Armand, transformed from a Slavic Russian into a Spaniard when Antonio Banderas portrayed him in the 1994 film version of &quot;Interview With the Vampire.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11599-reasor","name":"Reasor","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-27T13:13:10-07:00","id":1477544,"title":"","content":"Nevermind, got a date wrong.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3598-cajunkhan","name":"CajunKhan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3598_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1700"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-27T15:35:24-07:00","id":1477549,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CajunKhan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1477124-clan-tzimisce-is-the-least-interesting-clan?p=1477537#post1477537\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Carpathians is where Tzim himself laired and periodically popped out baby 4th gens. Of course the Carpathians would have a large number of powerful, old Tzims. Just as most of the old Lasombras are from the Mediterranean, where Lasombra himself laired and periodically popped out baby 4rth gens. I've always thought that whatever region an Ante laired in being dominated by that particular clan made perfect sense. The only ones for whom that wouldn't be true would be the Gangrel and Ravnos.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Tzimisce have more than that anchoring them to the Carpathians, it is a deeper link than what happens to most clans. It <b>is</b> more strongly the Region X clan than any other regardless of Antes. Even when a geographical location is cited as really important and the birthplace of a clan, they generally grew over it a long time ago.The prime exceptions are Tzimisce, Lasombra, Giovanni and FoS, and even then their dependence on their home turf varies, with Giovanni and FoS depending on it only for their central bases, while Lasombra and Tzimisce are still extremely tied to the power struggles and power bases there.<br /> <br /> What would happen if you took that land from under them on a swift strike? For the FoS and Giovanni you would create some temporary power vacuum until their leaders showed up somewhere else and setup shop. If you do this to the Lasombra, you take down their main seats of power and assets, the clan would be greatly crippled, because its tendrils outside Italy are far weaker than their tendrils elsewhere. If you do this to the Tzimisce as written, <i>especially before Revised</i>, you basically nuke their power and resources, and for a lot of players their <i>raison d'\u00eatre</i>. It also means for most that there will be no more vampires in the Carpathians even if you only took out the Tzimisce.<br /> <br /> And this is a problem, a sure sign of ethnic coding in the setting. It is best for the clan to be untied from that specific place, for it and for the real people that actually lives there and may not be fond of the clan link to them. It is also completely doable without changing significantly the clan's history with the place, or even with Kupala (that arguably shouldn't be tied to the entire mountain range and at the same time a single clan, though. This is hugely silly).<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar25794_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"25794\" data-vbnamecard=\"25794\">MyWifeIsScary</a> is right on one thing, we can't write off one issue just because the affected people are white. Prejudice against Eastern Europe is also a thing, and a strong one in the US. WoD itself is deeply guilty of depicting Europe in general as as backwaters a place as possible, especially Eastern Europe. And the Tzimisce got to be linked to a lot of this, like in the millennia old struggle between the Eastern Coded Castlevania Villains Clan and the Eastern Coded Bond Villains Tribe.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-27T18:34:29-07:00","id":1477554,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1477124-clan-tzimisce-is-the-least-interesting-clan?p=1477549#post1477549\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">...we can't write off one issue just because the affected people are white. Prejudice against Eastern Europe is also a thing, and a strong one in the US. WoD itself is deeply guilty of depicting Europe in general as as backwaters a place as possible, especially Eastern Europe. And the Tzimisce got to be linked to a lot of this, like in the millennia old struggle between the Eastern Coded Castlevania Villains Clan and the Eastern Coded Bond Villains Tribe.</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree with all of this and will add that I've lived in Eastern Europe and toured the region as well. I'm not going to speak for Eastern Europe, except to say that the depictions in most WoD books are bad. Transylvania is a developed industrial and (mostly) agricultural region, and is multi-ethnic. Saying it is backwards, and home to monsters is a bit like saying the most productive and bucolic parts of the American Midwest are home to monsters and backwards.<br /> <br /> On a related note, I moved the origins of the Tremere from Transylvania to the nation of Georgia the last time I ran VtM.<br /> <br /> Also, I am fine with making Vicissitude an amalgam power in V5. Equally I don't have a problem with Tzimisce using Vicissitude as I see it as the result of the clan's founder making a desperate deal with Kupula (or Yog Sothoth in my games). It is Vicissitude, and the clans deal with a demon, that make them &quot;eldritch.&quot; Dwelling in Eastern Europe doesn't make them strange.<br /> <br /> Edit; The Old Clan might be the Tzimisce who don't pursue the Vicissitude amalgam powers. So they are not &quot;weird&quot; or &quot;eldritch' but are still assholes. But they are assholes because they are vampires. Neither being an asshole or strange is connected to being from Eastern Europe or Slavic.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1208,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1208-grumpy-rpg-reviews","user":"Grumpy RPG Reviews","date":". 03-27-2022, 09:39 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1208-grumpy-rpg-reviews","name":"Grumpy RPG Reviews","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1208_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1888"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-27T19:04:45-07:00","id":1477558,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Grumpy RPG Reviews</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1477124-clan-tzimisce-is-the-least-interesting-clan?p=1477554#post1477554\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I agree with all of this and will add that I've lived in Eastern Europe and toured the region as well. I'm not going to speak for Eastern Europe, except to say that the depictions in most WoD books are bad. Transylvania is a developed industrial and (mostly) agricultural region, and is multi-ethnic. Saying it is backwards, and home to monsters is a bit like saying the most productive and bucolic parts of the American Midwest are home to monsters and backwards.</div> </div> </div> </div>Part of this was just unfamiliarity with that part of the world. And when most of the setting material was written in the 1990s, the region was mostly known for its transition from Communism to a functioning market economy. Twenty years after that, those countries are all very different. (Originally as written, the writers tried to do a good job at describing the actual world as such as then back determine how vampires managed to create that. If the game had continued with it, they would have reevaluated how changes in the real world during the nineties would have determined what vampires did. But they didn't. Metaplot became its own thing. And therefore the economic boom of the 1990s didn't mean the Sabbat had somehow lost control and the Camarilla retook major portions lost to them in decades past, but the Sabbat expanding during this time. So as the metaplot diverged from reality, the difference between the two worlds (the real and the fictional WoD) diverged as well.) And part of this is just old gothic tropes of <a href=\"https://tvtropes.org/pmwiki/pmwiki.php/Main/UberWald\" target=\"_blank\">Uberwald</a> which are now well over a hundred years out of date, but it forms the basis of much popular fiction about vampires, werewolves, and such.<br /> <br /> At the same time, the official World of Darkness version of the Midwest <i>is</i> home to monsters and backwards. There's supposed to be less modern and more gothic architecture in Chicago and other cities, things like the Chicago Union Stock Yards which closed in 1971 were still open in the early nineties when Chicago By Night came out and are presumably still there in WoD Chicago. Vampires and ghouls run underground slavery rings throughout the region. The Obertus control an entire village somewhere in Nebraska or Kansas. PENTEX is dumping pollution like it's still 1950 ignoring the vast amount of environmental laws and improvement that have actually happened in the US and other parts of the world. Fomori serial killers rampage everywhere. Sabbat perform Palla Grandes in the middle of Detroit. And so on. In other words, the WoD American Midwest isn't anything like the actual Midwest either.<br /> <br /> Before complaining about racism and prejudice, people need to keep this in mind.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-27T21:09:31-07:00","id":1477564,"title":"","content":"I admit, it's my wife's Eastern European heritage that helps me think about the fact that the Tzimisce should be seperated from Vicissitude so much. The Tzimisce as presented in the Sabbat book were deliberately the grossest, sickest, and most irredeemable Clan in the entire game and that includes the Followers of Set or Baali. They have almost no dignity and are used as the inhuman &quot;gross out&quot; factor.<br /> <br /> I support Old Clan Tzimisce because they're not so...well, despicable.<br /> <br /> Obviously, you want Eastern European gamers to want to play their own groups. As Outstar and my Eastern European players have stated, they would much rather play Toreador and Ventrue in Poland than Tzimisce.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-27T21:35:19-07:00","id":1477565,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1477124-clan-tzimisce-is-the-least-interesting-clan?p=1477564#post1477564\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I admit, it's my wife's Eastern European heritage that helps me think about the fact that the Tzimisce should be seperated from Vicissitude so much. The Tzimisce as presented in the Sabbat book were deliberately the grossest, sickest, and most irredeemable Clan in the entire game and that includes the Followers of Set or Baali. They have almost no dignity and are used as the inhuman &quot;gross out&quot; factor.<br /> <br /> I support Old Clan Tzimisce because they're not so...well, despicable.<br /> <br /> Obviously, you want Eastern European gamers to want to play their own groups. As Outstar and my Eastern European players have stated, they would much rather play Toreador and Ventrue in Poland than Tzimisce.</div> </div> </div> </div>I just think that blaming Vicissitude on this doesn't really help.<br /> <br /> The initial depiction of the Tzimisce does its best to be gross for shock value, and is Eastern Coded because of it. I really don't think the <a href=\"https://tvtropes.org/pmwiki/pmwiki.php/Main/Ruritania\" target=\"_blank\">Ruritania</a>-style depiction of Europe and especially Eastern Europe should be forgiven or taken as not prejudice. Vicissitude was also a part of this.<br /> <br /> But the problem is the gross-for-shock-value, not any particular piece. It is perfectly doable to dissociate the clan from this behavior without taking the Discipline out of them, Vicissitude is still plenty useful without constantly trying to prove that vampires can puke out of disgust, the same way that you don't need to turn on Presence every time you enter a room just because Toreador or to bare fangs all the time because Gangrel. You correct this by keeping in mind that acting like that only makes you be seen as obnoxious by your peers.<br /> <br /> On the part of &quot;their clan&quot;, what must be done is to both take the Tzimisce to wander more around the world without always bringing up that they talk in a Ruritania/\u00dcberwald accent or are at most two steps away from an Eastern European, and at the same time describe more the countries and cities in Eastern Europe as having a Kindred community just as cosmopolitan as everywhere else.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-28T02:09:24-07:00","id":1477572,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1477124-clan-tzimisce-is-the-least-interesting-clan?p=1477564#post1477564\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I admit, it's my wife's Eastern European heritage that helps me think about the fact that the Tzimisce should be seperated from Vicissitude so much. The Tzimisce as presented in the Sabbat book were deliberately the grossest, sickest, and most irredeemable Clan in the entire game and that includes the Followers of Set or Baali. They have almost no dignity and are used as the inhuman &quot;gross out&quot; factor.<br /> <br /> I support Old Clan Tzimisce because they're not so...well, despicable.<br /> <br /> Obviously, you want Eastern European gamers to want to play their own groups. As Outstar and my Eastern European players have stated, they would much rather play Toreador and Ventrue in Poland than Tzimisce.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Respectfully, the Giovanni are (were) the &quot;grossest, sickest, and most irredeemable Clan&quot;. There's a difference though, in that many &quot;decent&quot; clans have heavy representation in Italy. You're certainly correct that Tzimisce are used for a &quot;gross out&quot; factor though.<br /> <br /> I like Old Clan Tzimisce for the same reason, but I would also point out that ALL of the older Tzimisce tend to be much more pleasant (affably evil) than the Tzimisce neonates and ancillas who are still experimenting with their monstrous talents and were likely born/sired in less polite times. In other words, the American Tzimisce are meant to be more gross and sick than their European counterparts.. although as far as Irredeemable, I think the elders are certainly more set in their ways.<br /> <br /> I think there's a problem that many people see the Tzimisce as being &quot;the&quot; eastern European vampires. I think people need to be reminded that the Gangrel are very active in the region as well (especially Poland and north east Europe), and the Ravnos had a strong presence in south east Europe and western Asia (Although, as much as I love the Ravnos, they have similar problems to the Tzimisce, imo). Isn't their a certain powerful branch of Nosferatu in the area as well? I mean eastern Europe is where all of the oldest Tzimisce are.. it's their power-base, but that doesn't necessarily mean that they're the only clan with influence there.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23753-gothik_knight","name":"Gothik_Knight","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"66"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-28T08:32:21-07:00","id":1477587,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gothik_Knight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1477124-clan-tzimisce-is-the-least-interesting-clan?p=1477572#post1477572\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Respectfully, the Giovanni are (were) the &quot;grossest, sickest, and most irredeemable Clan&quot;. There's a difference though, in that many &quot;decent&quot; clans have heavy representation in Italy. You're certainly correct that Tzimisce are used for a &quot;gross out&quot; factor though.<br /> <br /> I like Old Clan Tzimisce for the same reason, but I would also point out that ALL of the older Tzimisce tend to be much more pleasant (affably evil) than the Tzimisce neonates and ancillas who are still experimenting with their monstrous talents and were likely born/sired in less polite times. In other words, the American Tzimisce are meant to be more gross and sick than their European counterparts.. although as far as Irredeemable, I think the elders are certainly more set in their ways.<br /> <br /> I think there's a problem that many people see the Tzimisce as being &quot;the&quot; eastern European vampires. I think people need to be reminded that the Gangrel are very active in the region as well (especially Poland and north east Europe), and the Ravnos had a strong presence in south east Europe and western Asia (Although, as much as I love the Ravnos, they have similar problems to the Tzimisce, imo). Isn't their a certain powerful branch of Nosferatu in the area as well? I mean eastern Europe is where all of the oldest Tzimisce are.. it's their power-base, but that doesn't necessarily mean that they're the only clan with influence there.</div> </div> </div> </div>Again, the problem here is how the game presents them.<br /> <br /> Which of them is the grossest is up for personal opinion, but while the Giovanni goes for the theme of &quot;skeletons in the closet&quot;, with most their gross factor played as family secrets (if not so secret), the Tzimisce was meant to be as blatantly evil as possible.<br /> <br /> On the matter of Eastern Europe, while there are other vampires there, the game always leaned heavily on presenting it as overwhelmed by Tzimisce presence, especially on older material. It is not even a matter of three or something more clans also having a presence there, just why aren't there any mentions to cities in the region being currently as cosmopolitan as everywhere else, with a presence of every clan? The game went for years as treating the entirety of Eastern Europe as a backwaters place where even the biggest cities still feel like rural towns.<br /> <br /> For the matter of elders and neonates, I agree with a caveat, the idea that neonates are a relatively homogeneous bunch is silly in any clan whatsoever. I don't think a recently embraced person that still remembers and cherish their human life in any way would &quot;revel&quot; in their evil and alien outlook, unless they were already like that in life. There are people like that, but it isn't that common to think the Tzimisce only Embrace those people.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-28T09:04:47-07:00","id":1477588,"title":"","content":"I think that we should always keep in mind that just because a vampire faction comes from some region doesn't mean that the vampires from there are some kind of a reflection on the people from that region. WW wasn't saying* that Eastern Europeans are like the Tzimisce, that Italians are like the Giovanni, that Hispanic people are like the Lasombra, or anything like that. That would be as silly as saying that white people are like bears and black people are like lions, since there are bears in Europe and lions in Africa.<br /> <br /> Also, another things to keep in mind, as Black Fox suggests above, the World of Darkness is not a good way to learn about real world people, customs, regions, religions, cultures, etc. If you want to learn about the history of Romania, Clanbook Tzimisce is the wrong place to look. The at WW were creating a game in a fantasy world roughly based on our own, we really can't expect too much in depth research on real world cultures. It's still silly top call the darkness controlling Clan &quot;Theshadow&quot; in Spanish, but it's not bigoted.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> * I will add one caveat, that there were a few WW books that did indeed make certain supernatural groups represent certain real cultures.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1129-sergeant-brother","name":"Sergeant Brother","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1129_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-28T20:24:10-07:00","id":1477610,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sergeant Brother</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1477124-clan-tzimisce-is-the-least-interesting-clan?p=1477588#post1477588\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think that we should always keep in mind that just because a vampire faction comes from some region doesn't mean that the vampires from there are some kind of a reflection on the people from that region. WW wasn't saying* that Eastern Europeans are like the Tzimisce, that Italians are like the Giovanni, that Hispanic people are like the Lasombra, or anything like that. That would be as silly as saying that white people are like bears and black people are like lions, since there are bears in Europe and lions in Africa.<br /> <br /> Also, another things to keep in mind, as Black Fox suggests above, the World of Darkness is not a good way to learn about real world people, customs, regions, religions, cultures, etc. If you want to learn about the history of Romania, Clanbook Tzimisce is the wrong place to look. The at WW were creating a game in a fantasy world roughly based on our own, we really can't expect too much in depth research on real world cultures. It's still silly top call the darkness controlling Clan &quot;Theshadow&quot; in Spanish, but it's not bigoted.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> * I will add one caveat, that there were a few WW books that did indeed make certain supernatural groups represent certain real cultures.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'll partly disagree, although I'll say that &quot;offenses&quot; aren't equal in <i>gravitas</i>, so saying something is wrong isn't to say it is equally wrong to everything else that is also wrong in the same general manner. That's clearly an issue for a lot of people here.<br /> <br /> Now, by themselves all those things are true. No clan is a statement about an area or its people, and as a fictional setting WoD isn't a faithful representation of the world and shouldn't be taken as such.<br /> <br /> That said, it is sad that so frequently it must be repeated that <b><u>context matters</u></b>. None of those things was written in a void and their context can and does say something, either on purpose or not. And frequently the context was WW repeating common prejudices and stereotypes of the time, not criticizing or questioning them, just taking them at face value.<br /> <br /> \u00dcberwalds/Ruritanias aren't an excuse that makes the problem go away, they're the problem itself. Representing a region as quirky and primitive send a whole different message if it is done for the first time or for the thousandth, especially such depiction comprises virtually all the representation of the region in media, bonus points if natives never had a say in such representations.<br /> <br /> So, the Tzimisce and Shadow Lords aren't a direct statement on Eastern Europe. But they're the two main representations of Eastern Europe in the game. Few if any material ever touches the subject of Eastern Europe without heavily talking about them, so there are virtually no other statements about Eastern Europe. And the game just uses common tropes and stereotypes. That weren't new at the time, were already pretty common across all media and genres. At face value, by the way.<br /> <br /> And finally, while fiction isn't the place to learn about how the world works, it is the place to represent and challenge your ideas about the world. And this whole discussion and many others happen around representation and its effects IRL, as fiction isn't reality but sends a message that is interpreted in reality.<br /> <br /> Yes. It <b>was</b> racism, and Communist-related xenophobia. No beating around the bushes. Tzimisce depiction was born out of racism and Eastern Europe got a heavily racist depiction. It just isn't irredeemable or anything like that. It doesn't make the clan bad, it just means there are things that must be corrected. Revised was timidly starting to do this, too timid in my opinion. And all that can be said about Africa, Asia and South America. Even about bits and pieces of the US. But as we're speaking the Tzimisce, yes, it must be said about Eastern Europe here.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-28T21:46:58-07:00","id":1477615,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1477124-clan-tzimisce-is-the-least-interesting-clan?p=1477610#post1477610\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes. It <b>was</b> racism, and Communist-related xenophobia. No beating around the bushes. Tzimisce depiction was born out of racism and Eastern Europe got a heavily racist depiction. It just isn't irredeemable or anything like that. It doesn't make the clan bad, it just means there are things that must be corrected. Revised was timidly starting to do this, too timid in my opinion. And all that can be said about Africa, Asia and South America. Even about bits and pieces of the US. But as we're speaking the Tzimisce, yes, it must be said about Eastern Europe here.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think you're both right and also that the problem is its based on wholesale plagiarism of the Necroscope concept. The Necroscope books are not SERIOUS books despite being HORROR books. They have the protagonist channel the power of Bruce Lee's ghost at one point. Vampires are all Dracula-esque Bela Lugosi aliens because it is a deliberately RIDICULOUS premise played violent and straight.<br /> <br /> The problem is that alien space vampires who act like Dracula have NOTHING to do with a Gothic Horror game where they're meant to be the protagonists.<br /> <br /> Except the Tzimisce weren't meant to be protagonists.<br /> <br /> They also weren't even meant to be Eastern European. The Modern Tzimisce were meant to be American and Sabbat.<br /> <br /> It's just everyone kept going back to the Old Clan/Dark Ages Tzimisce because the modern ones had no story or history while the Dark Ages ones did.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-28T22:33:58-07:00","id":1477616,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1477124-clan-tzimisce-is-the-least-interesting-clan?p=1477564#post1477564\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I admit, it's my wife's Eastern European heritage that helps me think about the fact that the Tzimisce should be seperated from Vicissitude so much. The Tzimisce as presented in the Sabbat book were deliberately the grossest, sickest, and most irredeemable Clan in the entire game and that includes the Followers of Set or Baali. They have almost no dignity and are used as the inhuman &quot;gross out&quot; factor.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't know that they were worse than the Baali. The Baali were presented in a Black Dog book for a reason. But it is pretty clear that the Tzimisce have fallen harder than any other clan in the Sabbat - and that's saying something because every clan in the Sabbat is grosser, sicker and more monstrous than their non-Sabbat brethren. The Sabbat Tzimisce cast away many of their traditions and legacies and embraced a new existence as inhuman monsters, losing nearly all of their nobility in the process. I assume that at least part of this is the Tzimisce's reliance and psuedo-worship of Kupala, and the unholy rituals that they perform.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-28T23:34:00-07:00","id":1477618,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1477124-clan-tzimisce-is-the-least-interesting-clan?p=1477610#post1477610\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes. It <b>was</b> racism, and Communist-related xenophobia. No beating around the bushes. Tzimisce depiction was born out of racism and Eastern Europe got a heavily racist depiction.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm sorry, but this is complete nonsense. <br /> <br /> Americans did not think of Eastern Europeans as being another race, or held even more mild ethnic prejudices. This wasn't the 1890s or 1920s when immigrants from Eastern Europe were unfamiliar. Many Americans by then were of Eastern European extraction and completely assimilated, and Mark Rein*Hagen himself was a huge fan of Vaclav Havel as can be seen by many of his dedications. By the time the WoD came out, the Cold War was over. Americans were incredibly sympathetic to the people who lived in former Communist countries and wanted to see them succeed. We didn't see people from Poland, Romania, Russia, or elsewhere as bizarre aliens we didn't understand. Americans didn't see Poles, Russians, Romanians, Hungarians, etc. as the enemy during the Cold War. We saw Communism as the enemy. We knew of the rebellions against Communism in 1956 Hungary, 1968 Czechoslovakia, and Solidarity era Poland. We knew about Russian dissidents like Sakharov and Solzhenitsyn. We were incredibly sympathetic to the people of those countries. We distinguished between the people who lived under Communism and the ideology itself. Since there were many examples of the same ethnic groups living under two different systems, this was easy to do (North Korea/South Korea, West Germany/East Germany, China/Taiwan). After the fall of European Communism, we certainly didn't see them as strange outsiders.<br /> <br /> Furthermore, there is absolutely nothing about the Tzimisce that was connected to Communism or even the people of Eastern Europe itself. It was either vague Dracula stuff, or strange Necroscope stuff. There was nothing that associated it with stereotypes about Communism or any stereotype of Eastern European ethnicity. Americans were eagerly putting the Cold War behind us because we were greatly relieved that it was over. As a college student at the time, I know we embraced many students at our universities from the former Soviet Bloc at this time, and were very interested in sharing stories and overcoming any lingering divides as a result of the Iron Curtain.<br /> <br /> If anything, the clan most heavily associated with the former Eastern Bloc was the Brujah, not the Tzimisce. The Brujah were the revolutionaries which metaphorically tied to the Communists. The Brujah was one of the original clans presented in the corebook and best known to players. We knew that the Soviet Union was supposed to have been ruled by a Brujah Council. And the Brujah Justicar had a very Slavic sounding name, Carlak. The Tzimisce clanbook, in contrast, was many years off. And the Sabbat, while present in Europe, was mainly a North American phenomenon except for a few select cities and regions in Europe. Europe was instead the stronghold of the Camarilla.<br /> <br /> You can think of the depiction of the Tzimisce as awful, in poor taste, ignorant, and ridiculous, and that's fine. I am not a big fan of the clan itself primarily because I never liked the Vicissitude Discipline, and too much of the clan's characteristics is based on its signature Discipline. That lends to a stereotype. But you shouldn't be ascribing bad writing to the motivations of racism.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-29T01:30:36-07:00","id":1477619,"title":"","content":"Personally, I've always loved the Tzimisce, and loved Vicissitude. I have never thought of them as boring or bland.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-29T12:17:38-07:00","id":1477639,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>adambeyoncelowe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1477124-clan-tzimisce-is-the-least-interesting-clan?p=1477619#post1477619\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Personally, I've always loved the Tzimisce, and loved Vicissitude. I have never thought of them as boring or bland.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I agree completely, but I think I can also understand why others might feel that way. The New World Tzimisce are very much like the Brujah, Gangrel, Toreador, and Ravnos, but all of those clans were more developed before the Tzimisce started to be fleshed out (pun unintended?). So the only things that people find to differentiate the Tzimisce from those clans that they love are: Vicissitude, Monstrous behavior, and the dracula archetype. As for me, those are all things that I like in my game of personal horror, but I can't help but notice a great deal of hate for vicissitude amongst some people, and also hate for the dracula archetype.. the hate for their monstrous behavior is really expected, except that, V:TM is meant to be a game of horror so I'd think the monstrosity would be more expected and accepted by fans of the setting.<br /> <br /> I think it would be a mistake to get away from Vicissitude. As someone who had no idea what Necroscope is before visiting these forums, I never associated the Tzimisce with anything because of vicissitude. I never understood why some people insisted on calling vicissitude &quot;alien&quot; instead of referring to it as a disease or possibly demonic corruption, although I never really wanted vicissitude to be anything more than a simple discipline. I was okay with the &quot;living vicissitude&quot; concept because I became familiar with that from &quot;Dirty Secrets of the Black Hand&quot; (not sure if that was it's origin in white wolf books though) and I appreciated the idea of the Old Clan and their quest to rid the Tzimisce of that corruption.<br /> <br /> I really don't think the Tzimisce need to be &quot;corrected&quot; at all. Rather, someone needs to explain how/why the &quot;rebelliousness&quot; of the New World Tzimisce is different from that of the Brujah, Gangrel, and Ravnos without relying on the clan's history.. I mean they need to be different here and now, not centuries ago and half a world away. If I sit down and chat with a Tzimisce Ancilla in New York, how will they come off as different from any of the other Anti-establishmentarian and inhuman clans running around the world of darkness? To me, the answer probably has to do with the idea that the Tzimisce don't necessarily desire change, but are the embodiment of change. While the Tzimisce may appear to be trying to bring chaos to the natural order of the world, they're actually trying to bring order to the chaos of their unnatural being. Tzimisce don't learn dominate or potence because they're not worried about trying to manipulate others, they need to worry about controlling themselves. They lack fortitude and presence because those disciplines usually represent a certainty of self that the Tzimisce will never have. The Tzimisce do not wish to mimic a beast, as the Gangrel do, but they are trying to avoid losing themselves to the beast, and so they tend to negotiate away their very humanity so that the beast will never take full control. At least that's what I think is cool, and all the while they're trying to fight off god-like beings as well.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23753-gothik_knight","name":"Gothik_Knight","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"66"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-29T15:47:49-07:00","id":1477648,"title":"","content":"(Caveat: Haven't read any of 5th ed, unlikely to ever change that.) <br /> <br /> I've always rather enjoyed the Tzimisce. While the sort of David Cronenberg/Clive Barker style body-horror aspects of Vicissitude are probably a bit overplayed, I still find that aspect effective in moderation. Likewise the potential it gives for exploring things like trans-humanism/trans-vampirism, gender fluidity, body-modification subcultures, and some of the stranger corners of pre-modern natural philosophy and more modern biological and anatomical sciences. <br /> Beyond that, I do also enjoy the &quot;Dracula thing&quot; and all it entails, with Carpathian/Romanian history, the rather distinctive German/Slavic cultural divide that used to exist in that region, medieval warlords, and the like. Also the real world Vlad the Impaler and his curious legacy as historic tyrant, national hero, and arguably one of the most death metal rulers of the early Renaissance period. Equally so the literary and cinematic Dracula, from Stoker's original story with its haunted castle and black magic, up to the over the top Hammer films, and beyond. <br /> Then there's the angle of mysticism and &quot;witchcraft&quot; (ie Eastern European pagan sorcery and folk magic), which plays well with folk horror tropes. Tied into this is the Orthodox monasteries of the old Byzantine empire and whatever heresies or &quot;Things Man Should Not Know&quot; they are hiding. <br /> Overall, I've always found a lot of interesting material to work with over the years. <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-29T18:57:42-07:00","id":1477660,"title":"","content":"I\u2019ve never that interested in the freakish gross out alien Sabbat Tzimisce. I have always much preferred the Old Clan or at least the Medieval version of the Clan. I like the evil yet honorable lords of the land, the utterly subservient ghouls, Revenant families, feudalism, and all of the things associated with that interpretation of the Clan. I don\u2019t dislike Vicissitude exactly, it has some cool aspects to it, though I think that they are as interesting or more so without it or with some variant of the Discipline. <br /> <br /> The freak show version of the Clan has literally nothing about them which is stereotypically Eastern European. With the Old Clan, maybe there is a slight association with things stereotypically Eastern European, in as much as they represent a connection to the Middle Ages. Then again, for Americans, all European nations have an association with medieval history.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1129-sergeant-brother","name":"Sergeant Brother","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1129_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-30T05:55:02-07:00","id":1477681,"title":"","content":"Well one thing can be concured the heated topics and discussion of radically distinct aspects of the clan kind of disproves them being an uninteresting clan. I'd be surprised if it got as heated about the toreador or what works as a toreador.<br /> <br /> As a side if you're going to argue viscitude is the same as protean theirs as strong an argument presence and Dominate are too simular or you could just fuse oblivion and blood sorcery under a general vampire magic discipline with a min of 55+ powers theirs going to be some risk of overlap. Its infinity preferable to a homogenous sludge where mechanical distinctions become completly superficial.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":26986,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","user":"Ragged Robin","date":". 03-30-2022, 05:13 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-30T06:38:35-07:00","id":1477683,"title":"","content":"If they were serious about streamlining disciplines they would combine Animalism with Dominate and Potence with Fortitude. Both of those mergers makes way more sense than Obtenebration with Necromancy or Vicissitude with Protean. <br /> <br /> Concerning racist stereotype, I feel that the depiction of cruelty and debased evil among the Tzimisce is a better commentary/satire on feudalism and not specific ethnicities, but I might be naive.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24351-garygeneric","name":"Garygeneric","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24351_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"108"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-30T14:16:23-07:00","id":1477705,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Garygeneric</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1477124-clan-tzimisce-is-the-least-interesting-clan?p=1477683#post1477683\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If they were serious about streamlining disciplines they would combine Animalism with Dominate and Potence with Fortitude. Both of those mergers makes way more sense than Obtenebration with Necromancy or Vicissitude with Protean. <br /> <br /> .</div> </div> </div> </div>Thinking on it you could probably compress the disciplines down to maybe 5-mystic, mind control, morphic, physical and perception alterations. It's just you probably shouldn't.<br /> <br /> I havnt really got much to input on tzmisce as problematic outside of more niche analytical lenses and not providing benefit of doubt. which obviously doesn't reflect day to day standards of what is or isn't racist . They're horrible vampires from Eastern europe much like ventrue are horrible vampires from upper western societies and lasombra are horrible vampires from the med.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":26986,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","user":"Ragged Robin","date":". 03-30-2022, 05:24 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-30T15:07:09-07:00","id":1477710,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ragged Robin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1477124-clan-tzimisce-is-the-least-interesting-clan?p=1477705#post1477705\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Thinking on it you could probably compress the disciplines down to maybe 5-mystic, mind control, morphic, physical and perception alterations. It's just you probably shouldn't.</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree. Sometimes less is more, sure, but in an expansive fantasy universe, paring down can feel terrible. Just my opinion, but I\u2019ve never had an issue with clan unique disciplines or clan flavor being heavily influenced by discipline sets. It\u2019s no different in my mind then the recent Clans Are Verbs list the released a while back.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24351-garygeneric","name":"Garygeneric","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24351_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"108"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-30T15:16:28-07:00","id":1477711,"title":"","content":"Regarding the Tzimisce and stereotypes:<br /> <br /> I don't necessarily think that I have too much to add on this front either, but a couple of points for consideration. I don't necessarily think that the Tzimisce themselves should be seen as a statement about Eastern Europe, but how Eastern Europe has been described and defined in relation to the Tzimisce is something that should be considered. It was pointed out earlier that portions of the real life USA do not entirely line up with their depiction in the WoD, but there is a difference between having particular differences or small divergences in history versus completely altering the reality in order to better fit a classic trope, a classic trope that was kind of racist even in its time. If modern Eastern Europe is still being presented as a quirky rural backwater in order to make it fit better with Tzimisce-as-Draculas, when in reality it is as industrialized and modernized as most other places, that is a problem in my opinion. I haven't read the &quot;A World of Darkness&quot; books closely, so I don't know how places like Romania are described, but I think it would be a problem if their reality was being completely ignored in order to make it better fit the preconceptions of outsiders, preconceptions that are based on a trope conceived of by outsiders which characterized the region as backwards and superstitious a hundred or more years ago.<br /> <br /> I also think it should be pointed out that &quot;appeal to Dracula&quot; is something that should be done with careful consideration. It's pretty commonly agreed among literary critics and scholars that Dracula the vampire resonated with Victorian audiences at least in part due to it paralleling stereotypes about foreign immigration as invasion, sexual violence, and STIs like syphilis. When you add in the fact that Tzimisce torture and body horror often carries sexualized aspects, there are some comparisons that merit reflection. I don't think these ideas dominate the entire character of the Clan, or that the Tzimisce concept is unsalvageable as a result, but I do think that they ought to be considered, and making efforts to expand the Clan beyond its association with Dracula is probably wise for that reason.<br /> <br /> Regarding Disciplines:<br /> <br /> I think it's a bit of a strawman to claim that combining Vicissitude with Protean is like wanting to combine Dominate and Presence, or Fortitude and Potence. Generally speaking, proponents are not arguing that it should be collapsed into Protean exclusively, but as an Amalgam with some other Discipline that can explain the distinctions between the two, while acknowledge that there is a considerable amount of overlap. The fact that Vicissitude can be used on other bodies, either to alter them or to transplant features from one specimen to another, is the main distinction. Protean is definitely altering flesh and bone when it adds claws to your hands or changes you into an animal, and the transformation to Zulo does not require the sculpting-by-hand required by earlier Vicissitude powers AFAIK. Presence and Dominate have significant differences in how they operate; one influences emotions, and thus can only affect thoughts and actions indirectly; the other directly manipulates actions, thoughts, and memories. There is some common ground between the two, but there are clear fundamental distinctions as well. And while increasing physical power via Potence could reasonably used to explain a greater resilience against physical damage, it is less obvious how that could reasonably explain the resistance to fire and sunlight provided by Fortitude.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25886-kharnov","name":"Kharnov","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"683"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-30T18:03:49-07:00","id":1477719,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kharnov</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1477124-clan-tzimisce-is-the-least-interesting-clan?p=1477711#post1477711\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Regarding the Tzimisce and <br /> <br /> Regarding Disciplines:<br /> <br /> I think it's a bit of a strawman to claim that combining Vicissitude with Protean is like wanting to combine Dominate and Presence, or Fortitude and Potence. Generally speaking, proponents are not arguing that it should be collapsed into Protean exclusively, but as an Amalgam with some other Discipline that can explain the distinctions between the two, while acknowledge that there is a considerable amount of overlap. The fact that Vicissitude can be used on other bodies, either to alter them or to transplant features from one specimen to another, is the main distinction. Protean is definitely altering flesh and bone when it adds claws to your hands or changes you into an animal, and the transformation to Zulo does not require the sculpting-by-hand required by earlier Vicissitude powers AFAIK. Presence and Dominate have significant differences in how they operate; one influences emotions, and thus can only affect thoughts and actions indirectly; the other directly manipulates actions, thoughts, and memories. There is some common ground between the two, but there are clear fundamental distinctions as well. And while increasing physical power via Potence could reasonably used to explain a greater resilience against physical damage, it is less obvious how that could reasonably explain the resistance to fire and sunlight provided by Fortitude.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Well that would be more a Comparative fallacy than a strawman but I think you're missing the point. The issue isn't that Dominate and presence should be fused but that a lot of disciplines have overlap or established similarities and they're just an example of that. I could construct a counter example and line of reason why Dominate and presence are very simular but protean and viss arnt (In fact my first attempt at a reply did just that until I realised i was missing my own arguement) but that misses the core point that v5 discipline removals and fusions are often rather abrtrary and based on the designers disdain for unique disciplines rather than some idealised valid discipline lineup.<br /> <br /> Ultimately I'd argue viscitude should exist because its fun and enhances the game and the plot point it's considered uniquely messed up is awesome it doesn't really need anything more than that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":26986,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","user":"Ragged Robin","date":". 03-30-2022, 09:10 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-30T21:59:58-07:00","id":1477745,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ragged Robin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1477124-clan-tzimisce-is-the-least-interesting-clan?p=1477719#post1477719\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well that would be more a Comparative fallacy than a strawman but I think you're missing the point. The issue isn't that Dominate and presence should be fused but that a lot of disciplines have overlap or established similarities and they're just an example of that. I could construct a counter example and line of reason why Dominate and presence are very simular but protean and viss arnt (In fact my first attempt at a reply did just that until I realised i was missing my own arguement) but that misses the core point that v5 discipline removals and fusions are often rather abrtrary and based on the designers disdain for unique disciplines rather than some idealised valid discipline lineup.<br /> <br /> Ultimately I'd argue viscitude should exist because its fun and enhances the game and the plot point it's considered uniquely messed up is awesome it doesn't really need anything more than that.</div> </div> </div> </div>It might be both; when I look up the &quot;comparative fallacy&quot; it seems to focus on something specific to linguistics, so I'm not sure if I'm just not familiar enough with the term to understand its application here, or if you're talking about false equivalence. I used &quot;strawman&quot; because simply framing it as &quot;some people think Vicissitude and Protean can be merged&quot; without discussing the specific examples misses out on a bunch of nuance and, IMO, alters the opposing position into one that is easier to disagree with, a strawman.<br /> <br /> I think the logic that merging Dominate and Presence is equally reasonable as Vicissitude as an Amalgam with Protean makes more sense perhaps in V5, where any given Discipline consists of a broad list of powers. I'm not going to crusade for the idea that Vicissitude absolutely should not exist as an independent Discipline. But I do think it's reasonable to say that a Discipline like Vicissitude is far more specialized and niche than a lot of the other &quot;core&quot; Disciplines; if it's going to be a Discipline on its own, it seems more like something that would fit a specialized Bloodline than a core Clan. A large number of the core Disciplines can be pretty easily summed up by a one-or-two-word broad archetype that covers a reasonably basic concept. &quot;Strength,&quot; &quot;Agility,&quot; or &quot;Shapeshifting&quot; seem to me like broad categories that cover a wide range of possibilities. &quot;Flesh-crafting&quot; by comparison sounds quite specialized, IMO.<br /> <br /> I would honestly be quite interested to hear your argument about what makes Protean and Vicissitude less compatible for a merge than Presence and Dominate, beyond the couple of distinctions I've already outlined above, that doesn't appeal to extremely nuanced points of how the functions of the Disciplines have been described. I feel like the distinction &quot;thoughts versus feelings&quot; sums up a significant gap between Dominate and Presence in a very simple fashion; if you think the gap between Vicissitude and Protean can be reduced to such a simple but significant distinction, I'm all ears.<br /> <br /> And I'm not entirely in disagreement with you about some of the decisions made in V5 either. I think Obtenebration is similarly more niche and specialized than a lot of other Disciplines, but the merge with Necromancy into Oblivion does rub me the wrong way. I just don't think turning Vicissitude into a Protean Amalgam is one of those unreasonable decisions, even if I disagree with them using Dominate as the other part of the Amalgam.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25886-kharnov","name":"Kharnov","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"683"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-31T02:44:43-07:00","id":1477757,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kharnov</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1477124-clan-tzimisce-is-the-least-interesting-clan?p=1477745#post1477745\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It might be both; when I look up the &quot;comparative fallacy&quot; it seems to focus on something specific to linguistics, so I'm not sure if I'm just not familiar enough with the term to understand its application here, or if you're talking about false equivalence. I used &quot;strawman&quot; because simply framing it as &quot;some people think Vicissitude and Protean can be merged&quot; without discussing the specific examples misses out on a bunch of nuance and, IMO, alters the opposing position into one that is easier to disagree with, a strawman.<br /> <br /> I think the logic that merging Dominate and Presence is equally reasonable as Vicissitude as an Amalgam with Protean makes more sense perhaps in V5, where any given Discipline consists of a broad list of powers. I'm not going to crusade for the idea that Vicissitude absolutely should not exist as an independent Discipline. But I do think it's reasonable to say that a Discipline like Vicissitude is far more specialized and niche than a lot of the other &quot;core&quot; Disciplines; if it's going to be a Discipline on its own, it seems more like something that would fit a specialized Bloodline than a core Clan. A large number of the core Disciplines can be pretty easily summed up by a one-or-two-word broad archetype that covers a reasonably basic concept. &quot;Strength,&quot; &quot;Agility,&quot; or &quot;Shapeshifting&quot; seem to me like broad categories that cover a wide range of possibilities. &quot;Flesh-crafting&quot; by comparison sounds quite specialized, IMO.<br /> <br /> I would honestly be quite interested to hear your argument about what makes Protean and Vicissitude less compatible for a merge than Presence and Dominate, beyond the couple of distinctions I've already outlined above, that doesn't appeal to extremely nuanced points of how the functions of the Disciplines have been described. I feel like the distinction &quot;thoughts versus feelings&quot; sums up a significant gap between Dominate and Presence in a very simple fashion; if you think the gap between Vicissitude and Protean can be reduced to such a simple but significant distinction, I'm all ears.<br /> <br /> And I'm not entirely in disagreement with you about some of the decisions made in V5 either. I think Obtenebration is similarly more niche and specialized than a lot of other Disciplines, but the merge with Necromancy into Oblivion does rub me the wrong way. I just don't think turning Vicissitude into a Protean Amalgam is one of those unreasonable decisions, even if I disagree with them using Dominate as the other part of the Amalgam.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Its more a short hand than anything which still wouldn't really be a strawman. The observation that viccistude can be merges with Protean is the aspect I was commenting on. It's not a strawman because that was an angle which has been discussed A strawman would be something like me suggesting the argument all disciplines be mushed into 5 and attacking that. Which I explored as tagent<br /> <br /> I agree that it's quite specific to the clan and specialised but I don't really see that as a disadvantage or an argument against it being its own power range.<br /> <br /> I don't really think either should be merged to be honest. More genrally my point is theirs a lot of broad overlap with Dominate/presence and it would be theoretically plausible to merge the two. You can go into minutae of the How's and whys but I think that misses the point I'm making (and would be ultimatly tedious.).<br /> <br /> I tend to frown on most of the mergers since they're ultimatly pointless. Oblivion is the only one which is categorically bad writting. But non of them provide any meaningful benifit they just seem to have happened because someone doesn't like clan disciplines rather than any need to 'clean up' the powers if that helps you get my perspective.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-31T05:19:00-07:00","id":1477758,"title":"","content":"I think we may be getting off topic. I have my own thoughts on whether a Protean/Vicissitude merge makes sense. Heck, I have thoughts on all the other discipline merge stuff as well, but for the purposes of this thread and topic, does anyone believe the Tzimisce would be &quot;more interesting&quot; if Tzimisce had protean instead of vicissitude? Would the clan be more interesting if Protean and Vicissitude were mixed? Apart from power levels, how does blending disciplines effect how interesting clans are in general, and the Tzimisce are in comparison to other clans in particular?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23753-gothik_knight","name":"Gothik_Knight","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"66"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-31T07:55:52-07:00","id":1477768,"title":"","content":"To me it all boils down to what movies/novels the discipline was supposed to duplicate. In the case of Vicissitude, it was supposed to duplicate the Wamphyri, but it didn't do it very well. Wamphyri basically have three or four dots worth of Requiem Protean, plus the ability to slowly create monsters in a laboratory. Vicissitude did a horrible job of duplicating that. It works better as a variation on Protean.<br /> <br /> Chimerstry was supposed to duplicate the Lost Boys ability to make people see things. This was clearly intended to be a variation on hypnotism in the movie, and so works best as a Dominate power.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3598-cajunkhan","name":"CajunKhan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3598_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1700"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-31T07:57:32-07:00","id":1477769,"title":"","content":"In some cases, I like combining multiple Disciplines into one, in other cases, I don't like it. It depends on the Disciplines. I would oppose combining Dominate and Presence because they are different thematically, even though they do both involve influencing people's minds. Combining Serpentis and Protean makes complete sense to me. I like getting rid of Dementation and putting some of its powers into Auspex or Dominate. Combining Potence and Fortitude is an interesting idea, as Celerity has long been considered the most powerful of the physical Disciplines - maybe instead of nerfing Celerity we could have just combined Potence and Fortitude. Realistically, to pick up cars or break chains with your bare hands, you need tougher flesh and bones.<br /> <br /> When it comes to Vicissitude, I can certainly see an argument for keeping them as separate because they are both mechanically and thematically very different. Though for me personally, since I favor Old Clan theme and aesthetics, I like using Protean because it's more like Dracula (or feudal lord of the land) than Necroscope. I understand why some would feel differently though.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1129-sergeant-brother","name":"Sergeant Brother","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1129_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-31T08:59:56-07:00","id":1477777,"title":"","content":"I like the merger because I can choose whether I want the Vicissitude or the standard Protean powers. For some characters the former fits, while for others the latter is a better option.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27145-setitefriend","name":"SetiteFriend","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27145_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"255"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-31T09:47:44-07:00","id":1477782,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ragged Robin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1477124-clan-tzimisce-is-the-least-interesting-clan?p=1477757#post1477757\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Its more a short hand than anything which still wouldn't really be a strawman. The observation that viccistude can be merges with Protean is the aspect I was commenting on. It's not a strawman because that was an angle which has been discussed A strawman would be something like me suggesting the argument all disciplines be mushed into 5 and attacking that. Which I explored as tagent<br /> <br /> I agree that it's quite specific to the clan and specialised but I don't really see that as a disadvantage or an argument against it being its own power range.<br /> <br /> I don't really think either should be merged to be honest. More genrally my point is theirs a lot of broad overlap with Dominate/presence and it would be theoretically plausible to merge the two. You can go into minutae of the How's and whys but I think that misses the point I'm making (and would be ultimatly tedious.).<br /> <br /> I tend to frown on most of the mergers since they're ultimatly pointless. Oblivion is the only one which is categorically bad writting. But non of them provide any meaningful benifit they just seem to have happened because someone doesn't like clan disciplines rather than any need to 'clean up' the powers if that helps you get my perspective.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not really important and it doesn't seem like we're going to agree, so I'll leave that one be.<br /> <br /> That seems to be the key point of contention or disagreement; I do think that a Discipline being highly niche or specialized supports making it into an Amalgam of more general powers that could reasonably produce its effects when combined, or the unique Discipline of a specialized Bloodline. Most of the Clans have Disciplines that focus on covering broad categories of vampiric power that show up throughout the genre, while a handful have highly specialized ones that are references to very particular pieces of fiction (like Vicissitude) or an extremely specific niche that was constructed by the designers (like Quietus). Again, it's not a matter I'm interested in going on a crusade over; if they had decided to keep Vicissitude as-is in V5, I wouldn't be complaining about it at all. I just don't think the idea of making it into a Protean Amalgam warrants complaint either.<br /> <br /> Maybe I am more invested in keeping things tidy and organized, but the idea of &quot;cleaning up&quot; the powers by combining ones that have a lot in common, or where one seems like a more specialized application of a broader category, is an exercise that makes some sense in my opinion. I think this is just something we have fundamentally different perspectives on, but I see where you are coming from.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gothik_Knight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1477124-clan-tzimisce-is-the-least-interesting-clan?p=1477758#post1477758\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think we may be getting off topic. I have my own thoughts on whether a Protean/Vicissitude merge makes sense. Heck, I have thoughts on all the other discipline merge stuff as well, but for the purposes of this thread and topic, does anyone believe the Tzimisce would be &quot;more interesting&quot; if Tzimisce had protean instead of vicissitude? Would the clan be more interesting if Protean and Vicissitude were mixed? Apart from power levels, how does blending disciplines effect how interesting clans are in general, and the Tzimisce are in comparison to other clans in particular?</div> </div> </div> </div>I suppose for me, it's more interesting if the Tzimisce have Protean AND Vicissitude-as-Protean-Amalgam for a few reasons. I discussed a few examples above of Protean powers that make a lot of sense for the Tzimisce to have, like Earth Meld. I also think having a more broadly applicable Discipline rather than a highly-specialized one opens up more types of characters that you can make as Tzimisce, rather than having one of their Disciplines be borderline useless if the wielder isn't willing to specialize in a very niche skillset (note that earlier editions literally created a special skill to be used with Vicissitude). Giving them Protean makes Dracula-as-Tzimisce fit a little better since shapeshifting into animals, mist, etc., was one of his most commonly-used powers. And I think the Path of Metamorphosis is more interesting when it's allowed to focus on adaptation and change more generally rather than flesh-crafting specifically.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25886-kharnov","name":"Kharnov","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"683"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-31T10:58:25-07:00","id":1477792,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sergeant Brother</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1477124-clan-tzimisce-is-the-least-interesting-clan?p=1477769#post1477769\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In some cases, I like combining multiple Disciplines into one, in other cases, I don't like it. It depends on the Disciplines. I would oppose combining Dominate and Presence because they are different thematically, even though they do both involve influencing people's minds. Combining Serpentis and Protean makes complete sense to me. I like getting rid of Dementation and putting some of its powers into Auspex or Dominate. Combining Potence and Fortitude is an interesting idea, as Celerity has long been considered the most powerful of the physical Disciplines - maybe instead of nerfing Celerity we could have just combined Potence and Fortitude. Realistically, to pick up cars or break chains with your bare hands, you need tougher flesh and bones.<br /> <br /> When it comes to Vicissitude, I can certainly see an argument for keeping them as separate because they are both mechanically and thematically very different. Though for me personally, since I favor Old Clan theme and aesthetics, I like using Protean because it's more like Dracula (or feudal lord of the land) than Necroscope. I understand why some would feel differently though.</div> </div> </div> </div>Vicissitude is horrible at duplicating Necroscope anyway. Wamphyi extend their jaws and claws, change into a loping four-legged form that is more or less a wolf, change into giant bats, and very slowly turn people into monsters and biomachinery when they have access to a laboratory. If I were to create them using VTM rules, I'd give them Protean 4, and a kind of specialized ritual biothaumaturgy that only works in conjunction with Protean. Maybe just give them a Protean 5 power that doesn't have prerequisites, is very powerful, but also extremely slow and in need of a laboratory.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3598-cajunkhan","name":"CajunKhan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3598_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1700"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-31T18:58:28-07:00","id":1477818,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kharnov</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1477124-clan-tzimisce-is-the-least-interesting-clan?p=1477745#post1477745\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">if it's going to be a Discipline on its own, it seems more like something that would fit a specialized Bloodline than a core Clan.</div> </div> </div> </div>Something must be said here.<br /> <br /> Categorizations aside, the Great Clans are <b>not</b> the core clans, and that's a part of the problem you see here.<br /> <br /> Buy it or not, from a design perspective the game has <b>seven core clans, no more</b>. All others, without exception, are specialized extra options through and through. They're defined as clans because of their major roles in the setting, but although major those roles are still specialized from the POV of the authors.<br /> <br /> That's why Vicissitude is a specialized gimmick. As are Obtenebration, Necromancy, Chimerstry, Quietus and Serpentis. Each is a very specialized gimmick in origin, meant to quickly and easily emphasize that clan's role in the setting as NPCs and frequently not designed for PC use.<br /> <br /> My own thought on that, as already discussed in other threads, is that fusing Disciplines doesn't work for V20 and previous edition. The Discipline mechanics <b>may</b> demand an entire overhaul, as they did both in V5 and Requiem (very differently), but if you don't do it, then just getting used to their many similarities is the way to go. Otherwise you'll spend a lot of time and effort to make adjustments that may at best serve you for a couple powers while letting 50 other <b>sets</b> untouched and most people still not agree with your changes,<br /> <br /> V5's take works. It isn't the best (because this is <b>Requiem</b>'s by far), but it works just fine, it is just another way of doing it. The only problem is the ever hated limit of one power per level, that creates so much unnecessary restrictions.<br /> <br /> Why cleaning-up powers doesn't work with Original Rules\u2122? Because they're inflexible as designed, so no matter how much you see any other as similar, merging them simply doesn't work, you'll still end up with a power set that doesn't do what they're meant to do separately. Why V5's Vicissitude is a problem? Because beyond the whole point of Dominate-Amalgam not working, with the power limit it means that actually the Tzimisce don't fully have a third Discipline if they want to go Vicissitude. They have Protean and the slot to be used for making Protean also have Vicissitude effects. <b>Now</b> similarity is a problem as the same character is bound to have both powers, and is left with a dead Dominate slot effectively making them just two-Disciplines strong with a gimmicky extra.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-31T21:53:20-07:00","id":1477830,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1477124-clan-tzimisce-is-the-least-interesting-clan?p=1477818#post1477818\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Something must be said here.<br /> <br /> Categorizations aside, the Great Clans are <b>not</b> the core clans, and that's a part of the problem you see here.<br /> <br /> Buy it or not, from a design perspective the game has <b>seven core clans, no more</b>. All others, without exception, are specialized extra options through and through. They're defined as clans because of their major roles in the setting, but although major those roles are still specialized from the POV of the authors.<br /> <br /> That's why Vicissitude is a specialized gimmick. As are Obtenebration, Necromancy, Chimerstry, Quietus and Serpentis. Each is a very specialized gimmick in origin, meant to quickly and easily emphasize that clan's role in the setting as NPCs and frequently not designed for PC use.<br /> <br /> My own thought on that, as already discussed in other threads, is that fusing Disciplines doesn't work for V20 and previous edition. The Discipline mechanics <b>may</b> demand an entire overhaul, as they did both in V5 and Requiem (very differently), but if you don't do it, then just getting used to their many similarities is the way to go. Otherwise you'll spend a lot of time and effort to make adjustments that may at best serve you for a couple powers while letting 50 other <b>sets</b> untouched and most people still not agree with your changes,<br /> <br /> V5's take works. It isn't the best (because this is <b>Requiem</b>'s by far), but it works just fine, it is just another way of doing it. The only problem is the ever hated limit of one power per level, that creates so much unnecessary restrictions.<br /> <br /> Why cleaning-up powers doesn't work with Original Rules\u2122? Because they're inflexible as designed, so no matter how much you see any other as similar, merging them simply doesn't work, you'll still end up with a power set that doesn't do what they're meant to do separately. Why V5's Vicissitude is a problem? Because beyond the whole point of Dominate-Amalgam not working, with the power limit it means that actually the Tzimisce don't fully have a third Discipline if they want to go Vicissitude. They have Protean and the slot to be used for making Protean also have Vicissitude effects. <b>Now</b> similarity is a problem as the same character is bound to have both powers, and is left with a dead Dominate slot effectively making them just two-Disciplines strong with a gimmicky extra.</div> </div> </div> </div>Fair point for sure, although I think the Malkavians are an interesting border-case, because I would include Dementation in the list of &quot;specialized gimmicks&quot; despite being a Discipline of a &quot;core&quot; Clan, but it's complicated by the fact that Dementation was not originally part of their &quot;core&quot; Discipline spread IIRC, but rather specific to their (again, antagonist/NPC) Sabbat counterparts. Only later was it retconned that Dementation was their original Discipline, with Dominate Malkavians being (in lore) the result of a powerful ritual, &quot;the Great Trick,&quot; that was meant to make them fit into the Camarilla better.<br /> <br /> Necromancy is interesting as well, because I think there's some rationale for having it distinct from other kinds of Blood Magic, but you could just as easily imagine it as part of a &quot;core&quot; Blood Sorcery Discipline instead.<br /> <br /> I was not aware that Amalgams counted towards the stupid 1-power-per-level restriction of V5, that certainly makes it even more annoying.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25886-kharnov","name":"Kharnov","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"683"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-04-01T02:51:54-07:00","id":1477838,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1477124-clan-tzimisce-is-the-least-interesting-clan?p=1477818#post1477818\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Something must be said here.<br /> <br /> Categorizations aside, the Great Clans are <b>not</b> the core clans, and that's a part of the problem you see here.<br /> <br /> Buy it or not, from a design perspective the game has <b>seven core clans, no more</b>. All others, without exception, are specialized extra options through and through. They're defined as clans because of their major roles in the setting, but although major those roles are still specialized from the POV of the authors.<br /> <br /> That's why Vicissitude is a specialized gimmick. As are Obtenebration, Necromancy, Chimerstry, Quietus and Serpentis. Each is a very specialized gimmick in origin, meant to quickly and easily emphasize that clan's role in the setting as NPCs and frequently not designed for PC use.<br /> <br /> My own thought on that, as already discussed in other threads, is that fusing Disciplines doesn't work for V20 and previous edition. The Discipline mechanics <b>may</b> demand an entire overhaul, as they did both in V5 and Requiem (very differently), but if you don't do it, then just getting used to their many similarities is the way to go. Otherwise you'll spend a lot of time and effort to make adjustments that may at best serve you for a couple powers while letting 50 other <b>sets</b> untouched and most people still not agree with your changes,<br /> <br /> V5's take works. It isn't the best (because this is <b>Requiem</b>'s by far), but it works just fine, it is just another way of doing it. The only problem is the ever hated limit of one power per level, that creates so much unnecessary restrictions.<br /> <br /> Why cleaning-up powers doesn't work with Original Rules\u2122? Because they're inflexible as designed, so no matter how much you see any other as similar, merging them simply doesn't work, you'll still end up with a power set that doesn't do what they're meant to do separately. Why V5's Vicissitude is a problem? Because beyond the whole point of Dominate-Amalgam not working, with the power limit it means that actually the Tzimisce don't fully have a third Discipline if they want to go Vicissitude. They have Protean and the slot to be used for making Protean also have Vicissitude effects. <b>Now</b> similarity is a problem as the same character is bound to have both powers, and is left with a dead Dominate slot effectively making them just two-Disciplines strong with a gimmicky extra.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Wouldn't this effectively mean two of the 'core' clans have unique gimmick disciplines? Especially in v5 were blood sorcery is more of a quirky blood manipulation power rather than a magic system.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-04-01T05:38:18-07:00","id":1477843,"title":"","content":"I think it's fair to argue that the &quot;core clans&quot; are whatever the 7 clans of the Camarilla are at the moment, meaning that Gangrel and Brujah started as &quot;core clans&quot;, but no longer are, while Lasombra and Assamite were not core clans, but Lasombra and Banu Haqim now are.<br /> <br /> Also, there are currently no unique disciplines amongst the Camarilla clans. Banu Haqim and Tremere share blood sorcery. Lasombra and Hekata (sp?) share Oblivion. Malkavians lost dementation and the Gangrel are no longer a &quot;core clan&quot; (at least in one world view).<br /> <br /> As for the Tzimisce, I feel like they're not only not a core clan at the moment, but they're really in Limbo. They have a purpose, to oppose the antediluvians, but their goal at this point seems so impossible that it takes the purpose from the Tzimisce (and isn't that why the Lasombra left the sabbat?) Are the Tzimisce more interesting as the suicidal knights who refuse to give in even when they know the cause is lost? Or is there some other role for them to play still?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23753-gothik_knight","name":"Gothik_Knight","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"66"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-04-01T05:59:10-07:00","id":1477844,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gothik_Knight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1477124-clan-tzimisce-is-the-least-interesting-clan?p=1477843#post1477843\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think it's fair to argue that the &quot;core clans&quot; are whatever the 7 clans of the Camarilla are at the moment, meaning that Gangrel and Brujah started as &quot;core clans&quot;, but no longer are, while Lasombra and Assamite were not core clans, but Lasombra and Banu Haqim now are.<br /> <br /> Also, there are currently no unique disciplines amongst the Camarilla clans. Banu Haqim and Tremere share blood sorcery. Lasombra and Hekata (sp?) share Oblivion. Malkavians lost dementation and the Gangrel are no longer a &quot;core clan&quot; (at least in one world view).<br /> <br /> As for the Tzimisce, I feel like they're not only not a core clan at the moment, but they're really in Limbo. They have a purpose, to oppose the antediluvians, but their goal at this point seems so impossible that it takes the purpose from the Tzimisce (and isn't that why the Lasombra left the sabbat?) Are the Tzimisce more interesting as the suicidal knights who refuse to give in even when they know the cause is lost? Or is there some other role for them to play still?</div> </div> </div> </div>I disagree. They have been pushing the Anarchs and thinbloods hard. The idea that this is fundamentally a Camarilla game is over. In some ways I think even the idea that this is a vampire game is over. You are intended to play people who are barely vampires, fighting the REAL vampires. You are intended to play someone who barely has any powers, but also barely has a bane and has high humanity, who fights the vampires by exploiting the subtle advantages of having high humanity and barely any bane.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3598-cajunkhan","name":"CajunKhan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3598_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1700"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-04-01T06:07:45-07:00","id":1477845,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CajunKhan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1477124-clan-tzimisce-is-the-least-interesting-clan?p=1477844#post1477844\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I disagree. They have been pushing the Anarchs and thinbloods hard. The idea that this is fundamentally a Camarilla game is over. In some ways I think even the idea that this is a vampire game is over. You are intended to play people who are barely vampires, fighting the REAL vampires. You are intended to play someone who barely has any powers, but also barely has a bane and has high humanity, who fights the vampires by exploiting the subtle advantages of having high humanity and barely any bane.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, basically. I heard a rumours that v5 was initially going to be thin blood only for..... reasons I'm guessing someone interveniened before it got too far since it's a terrible idea but if true you can see hints of it how relentlessly thin blood have been pushed in this edition. With unique mechanics and powers after everyone else's got stripped <br /> <br /> Personally I'm hoping they'll knock it off soon but it's an interesting aspect of the game going forward.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":26986,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","user":"Ragged Robin","date":". 04-01-2022, 09:14 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-04-01T08:34:20-07:00","id":1477854,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gothik_Knight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1477124-clan-tzimisce-is-the-least-interesting-clan?p=1477843#post1477843\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think it's fair to argue that the &quot;core clans&quot; are whatever the 7 clans of the Camarilla are at the moment, meaning that Gangrel and Brujah started as &quot;core clans&quot;, but no longer are, while Lasombra and Assamite were not core clans, but Lasombra and Banu Haqim now are.?</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't really think that is accurate at all. Aside from Anarch being a main faction in V5, the edition has pushed for greater freedom between Clan and Sect. Especially considering how clans, especially the independents, were revamped into broad archetypes similar to the core 7.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CajunKhan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1477124-clan-tzimisce-is-the-least-interesting-clan?p=1477844#post1477844\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I disagree. They have been pushing the Anarchs and thinbloods hard. The idea that this is fundamentally a Camarilla game is over. </div> </div> </div> </div>Of course they have been pushing Anarchs hard, they are the main player faction besides the Camarilla. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> In some ways I think even the idea that this is a vampire game is over. You are intended to play people who are barely vampires, fighting the REAL vampires. You are intended to play someone who barely has any powers, but also barely has a bane and has high humanity, who fights the vampires by exploiting the subtle advantages of having high humanity and barely any bane. </div> </div> </div>This is completely baseless. Though I'd love to see some text that somehow supports this. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ragged Robin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1477124-clan-tzimisce-is-the-least-interesting-clan?p=1477845#post1477845\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yeah, basically. I heard a rumours that v5 was initially going to be thin blood only for..... reasons I'm guessing someone interveniened before it got too far since it's a terrible idea but if true you can see hints of it how relentlessly thin blood have been pushed in this edition. With unique mechanics and powers after everyone else's got stripped<br /> <br /> Personally I'm hoping they'll knock it off soon but it's an interesting aspect of the game going forward.</div> </div> </div> </div>A. That might have been for Bloodlines 2, and I do dislike their choice of a Thin-Blood Protagonist there, even if it is for a small part of the game.<br /> <br /> B. In what world releasing an edition of VTM with only Thin Bloods makes any sense. Like seriously, it's a parody-level assumption. Thin Bloods do get some focus as they were the hot new thing of the edition. <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27145-setitefriend","name":"SetiteFriend","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27145_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"255"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-04-01T08:41:47-07:00","id":1477855,"title":"","content":"If thin blood were a clan I would have just said &quot;No Tzimisce aren't the least interesting, look at Thin-bloods.&quot; The best thing about thin-bloods is that every player I know would happily ignore them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23753-gothik_knight","name":"Gothik_Knight","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"66"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-04-01T09:41:17-07:00","id":1477862,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ragged Robin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1477124-clan-tzimisce-is-the-least-interesting-clan?p=1477838#post1477838\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Wouldn't this effectively mean two of the 'core' clans have unique gimmick disciplines? Especially in v5 were blood sorcery is more of a quirky blood manipulation power rather than a magic system.</div> </div> </div> </div>I can't speak for how Blood Sorcery works in V5, but I do feel like &quot;magic&quot; is a broad category or theme, in terms of abilities for fictional characters at least.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gothik_Knight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1477124-clan-tzimisce-is-the-least-interesting-clan?p=1477843#post1477843\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think it's fair to argue that the &quot;core clans&quot; are whatever the 7 clans of the Camarilla are at the moment, meaning that Gangrel and Brujah started as &quot;core clans&quot;, but no longer are, while Lasombra and Assamite were not core clans, but Lasombra and Banu Haqim now are.<br /> <br /> Also, there are currently no unique disciplines amongst the Camarilla clans. Banu Haqim and Tremere share blood sorcery. Lasombra and Hekata (sp?) share Oblivion. Malkavians lost dementation and the Gangrel are no longer a &quot;core clan&quot; (at least in one world view).<br /> <br /> As for the Tzimisce, I feel like they're not only not a core clan at the moment, but they're really in Limbo. They have a purpose, to oppose the antediluvians, but their goal at this point seems so impossible that it takes the purpose from the Tzimisce (and isn't that why the Lasombra left the sabbat?) Are the Tzimisce more interesting as the suicidal knights who refuse to give in even when they know the cause is lost? Or is there some other role for them to play still?</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bI think what <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar5826_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"5826\" data-vbnamecard=\"5826\">monteparnas</a> is commenting on is that the &quot;core Clans&quot; are the ones that were initially released when VtM came out originally, and that the rest of the Clans are &quot;not Core&quot; by virtue of having been added on later, often starting in NPC/antagonist territory before becoming available to PCs. Being &quot;Camarilla Clans&quot; is just a coincidence because they were also the &quot;Anarch Clans&quot; effectively at the beginning as well.<br /> <br /> Going back to the Tzimisce, I think it's important to remember that for every Tzimisce that is fully onboard with the Sabbat's &quot;kill the Antediluvians&quot; mission, there is another who just wants to be left alone to do their Metamorphosist experimenting and theorizing, or holding onto the domains that they never quite lost even back during the Anarch Revolt like the Oradea League. The Tzimisce are more than just Sabbat diehards. Which is basically the same for every other Clan in the Sabbat as well. The Tzimisce are just kind of unique in having little to no official presence in any other sect, but that doesn't mean they're all committed to the mission.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25886-kharnov","name":"Kharnov","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"683"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-04-01T14:46:51-07:00","id":1477867,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SetiteFriend</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1477124-clan-tzimisce-is-the-least-interesting-clan?p=1477854#post1477854\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> A. That might have been for Bloodlines 2, and I do dislike their choice of a Thin-Blood Protagonist there, even if it is for a small part of the game.<br /> <br /> B. In what world releasing an edition of VTM with only Thin Bloods makes any sense. Like seriously, it's a parody-level assumption. Thin Bloods do get some focus as they were the hot new thing of the edition. <br /> <br /></div> </div> </div> </div>1) I'm unsure that it's anymore plausible than my suggestion? Structuring your entire release around a minor part of a associated game to the point were they not only get unique powers but play completly different from all classes is way more absurd than development changes.<br /> <br /> 2) the sort of world were the developers got fired for sparking an international incident, in such a universe its a pretty tame possibility. Especially when you look at how much print they get for a previously niche character class .speaking of which thin blood arnt new kids-they've been playable for at least 23 years.<br /> Frankly I'm unsure if the rumours true and if it is someone clearly realised it was a horrible mistake but it does explain the sheer scale of distinct rules thinbloods get in an edition which aggressively cuts down on it everywhere else.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":26986,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","user":"Ragged Robin","date":". 04-01-2022, 06:00 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-04-01T16:21:34-07:00","id":1477871,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ragged Robin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1477124-clan-tzimisce-is-the-least-interesting-clan?p=1477867#post1477867\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> 1) I'm unsure that it's anymore plausible than my suggestion? Structuring your entire release around a minor part of a associated game to the point were they not only get unique powers but play completly different from all classes is way more absurd than development changes.</div> </div> </div> </div>I meant that the rumor could have been about Bloodlines 2 possibly only having Thin-Bloods, which would have been a more logical explanation, in my opinion. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ragged Robin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1477124-clan-tzimisce-is-the-least-interesting-clan?p=1477867#post1477867\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">2) the sort of world were the developers got fired for sparking an international incident, in such a universe its a pretty tame possibility.</div> </div> </div> </div>No? Bad takes on international politics weren't a new thing for White Wolf and it's a completely different thing from making thin-bloods the only playable option. Cutting out Clans and good part of the horror of Kindred for no given reason is nonsensical. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ragged Robin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1477124-clan-tzimisce-is-the-least-interesting-clan?p=1477867#post1477867\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Especially when you look at how much print they get for a previously niche character class .</div> </div> </div> </div>Because it is a new edition that does new things and expands on an older concept? The Caitif also get an expanded write-up in V5, was V5 originally going to be only Caitiff too?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ragged Robin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1477124-clan-tzimisce-is-the-least-interesting-clan?p=1477867#post1477867\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">speaking of which thin blood arnt new kids-they've been playable for at least 23 years.</div> </div> </div> </div>Their new mechanics and Alchemy are very much a new thing. \u200bPlus, they are no longer a flaw one takes, but a completely different &quot;Clan&quot; that gives an opportunity for a different type of game. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ragged Robin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1477124-clan-tzimisce-is-the-least-interesting-clan?p=1477867#post1477867\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Frankly I'm unsure if the rumours true and if it is someone clearly realised it was a horrible mistake but it does explain the sheer scale of distinct rules thinbloods get in an edition which aggressively cuts down on it everywhere else.</div> </div> </div> </div>New editions do try new things (sometimes).<br /> <br /> And it's not a huge amount of distinct rules, they get a couple pages detailing what the differences are between them and Kindred, a couple more on their merits, plus a write-up for Thin-Blood Alchemy. The amount text they get isn't much different from what Blood Sorcery gets.<br /> <br /> Speaking about cutting down, the Thin-Bloods do cut down on the odd distinctions of thin-bloods in previous editions. No longer are there separate flaws for Thin-Blood, 14th, 15th or 16th gens. Just a singular set of characteristics and the ways each thin-blood is different. Or inceptor disciplines.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27145-setitefriend","name":"SetiteFriend","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27145_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"255"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-04-01T16:59:43-07:00","id":1477874,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SetiteFriend</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1477124-clan-tzimisce-is-the-least-interesting-clan?p=1477871#post1477871\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I meant that the rumor could have been about Bloodlines 2 possibly only having Thin-Bloods, which would have been a more logical explanation, in my opinion. <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> No? Bad takes on international politics weren't a new thing for White Wolf and it's a completely different thing from making thin-bloods the only playable option. Cutting out Clans and good part of the horror of Kindred for no given reason is nonsensical. <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Because it is a new edition that does new things and expands on an older concept? The Caitif also get an expanded write-up in V5, was V5 originally going to be only Caitiff too?<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Their new mechanics and Alchemy are very much a new thing. \u200bPlus, they are no longer a flaw one takes, but a completely different &quot;Clan&quot; that gives an opportunity for a different type of game. <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> New editions do try new things (sometimes).<br /> <br /> And it's not a huge amount of distinct rules, they get a couple pages detailing what the differences are between them and Kindred, a couple more on their merits, plus a write-up for Thin-Blood Alchemy. The amount text they get isn't much different from what Blood Sorcery gets.<br /> <br /> Speaking about cutting down, the Thin-Bloods do cut down on the odd distinctions of thin-bloods in previous editions. No longer are there separate flaws for Thin-Blood, 14th, 15th or 16th gens. Just a singular set of characteristics and the ways each thin-blood is different. Or inceptor disciplines.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think so. I mean you're effectively modelling your franchise going forces on one spin of game. Which incidently is in development hell.<br /> <br /> Would you conceed that the international incident is a worse idea than thinkblood only though?<br /> <br /> Well yes especially as they're trimming back everywhere else drastically. Caitiff are mechanically very simular to regular clans in v5 as opposed to thin blood who are borderline a different type of supernatural and have way more writting.<br /> <br /> Yes but they're not a new group so they're not the new kids are they?<br /> <br /> Yes but the writting around thinbloods sticks out a sore thumb compared to everything else in v5.<br /> <br /> New discipline is an understatement, they work completly differently. They get big chunks dedicated to them in books eg path of sun. No other class gets this despite this apparently being the new player edition.<br /> <br /> I'd argue that was better and messed better in Revised than thin bloods do in v5.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":26986,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","user":"Ragged Robin","date":". 04-01-2022, 09:01 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-04-01T18:03:41-07:00","id":1477878,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ragged Robin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1477124-clan-tzimisce-is-the-least-interesting-clan?p=1477874#post1477874\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I don't think so. I mean you're effectively modelling your franchise going forces on one spin of game. Which incidently is in development hell.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's not remotely what I said. Again, I meant that if that rumor even existed, it would make sense that it was for BL 2 and not V5<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Would you conceed that the international incident is a worse idea than thinkblood only though? </div> </div> </div>It's a nonsensical comparison. One is a mistake in writing and lack of diversity reading, the other is deliberate choice in game direction. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Well yes especially as they're trimming back everywhere else drastically. Caitiff are mechanically very simular to regular clans in v5 as opposed to thin blood who are borderline a different type of supernatural and have way more writting. </div> </div> </div>They expanded with the Resonance System, Touchstones, Tenets and Convictions, Blood Potency, Loresheets, Predator Types, the Thin-Bloods and other stuff. They did more than just trim horrible amounts of bloat.<br /> <br /> Yes Thin-Blood get different mechanics, but how is that anyway indicative that &quot;v5 was initially going to be thin blood only&quot;. If anything, the way their mechanics are presented, they were added afterward, considering they follow standard mechanics for vampires unless otherwise stated, as quoted further below.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Yes but they're not a new group so they're not the new kids are they? </div> </div> </div>Their mechanics are. And this pedantism is irrelevant to the point &quot;v5 was initially going to be thin blood only&quot;.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Yes but the writting around thinbloods sticks out a sore thumb compared to everything else in v5.<br /> <br /> New discipline, they work completky differently. </div> </div> </div>I disagree that it sticks out, if anything they provide an interesting midpoint to explore between humans and vampires.<br /> <br /> And they don't work completely different, to quote the Corebook &quot;Despite this, your thin-blood character is still fundamentally a vampire, and unless otherwise stated follows the same rules as other vampires in this book.&quot;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> They gey big chunks dedicated to them in books eg path of sun. </div> </div> </div>The Sabbat Book, released 3 years after the Corebook, is an indicative that &quot;v5 was initially going to be thin blood only&quot;?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> No one gets this despite this apparently being the new player edition. </div> </div> </div>Gets what? Unique disciplines (Which is the opposite of making it new player friendly) and big chunks of books dedicated to them (which they do anyway? Especially since you are no longer talking about the Corebook) ?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I'd argue that was better and messed better in Revised than thin bloods do in v5. </div> </div> </div>&quot;Who did it better&quot; is not really what the discussion is about.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27145-setitefriend","name":"SetiteFriend","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27145_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"255"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-04-01T23:11:11-07:00","id":1477885,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ragged Robin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1477124-clan-tzimisce-is-the-least-interesting-clan?p=1477838#post1477838\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Wouldn't this effectively mean two of the 'core' clans have unique gimmick disciplines? Especially in v5 were blood sorcery is more of a quirky blood manipulation power rather than a magic system.</div> </div> </div> </div>Nope, at least not for their main design.<br /> <br /> \u200bAs <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25886-kharnov\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"25886\" data-vbnamecard=\"25886\">Kharnov</a> nicely pointed out Dementation <b>is</b> a unique gimmick Discipline. But it isn't the original Malkavian Discipline from a game perspective. DA takes a completely different approach on the clans that makes it acceptable for the Malks to have a gimmick Discipline (in a sense it works on making all clans more gimmicky than their modern counterparts one way or another), and only Revised moved Dementation to the Core, but Revised did a lot of changes to mechanics here and there for metaplot reasons even in the core, so it is also following very distinct and specific design principles.<br /> <br /> For &quot;stable, metaplot-agnostic&quot; games, Malkavian was designed with Dominate.<br /> <br /> Thaumaturgy is an interesting case as it is limited in lore, but it is actually the core mechanic for &quot;Vampire Magic&quot; even if other magical Disciplines tried to stir away from it to some degree. Mechanically speaking, Thaumaturgy isn't simply Tremere Blood Magic, but the very core magic system for vampires. And as such, it is designed versatile, broad and stable as other Disciplines, even if specific Paths may not be so much.<br /> <br /> Yes, the lore makes it unique. But it isn't designed as just a limited, specialized gimmick.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gothik_Knight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1477124-clan-tzimisce-is-the-least-interesting-clan?p=1477843#post1477843\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think it's fair to argue that the &quot;core clans&quot; are whatever the 7 clans of the Camarilla are at the moment,</div> </div> </div> </div>Not at all.<br /> <br /> This is a game design decision, not a social status in-lore. Open the core for V5 and you'll see the same 7 clans from before, down to the last, and no others. The new edition made sure to give players the option to play Mostly-Anarch clans (and even for that to be a thing) on the core, but it didn't really change the host of main PC clans. Those are meant as main PC options and main political actors, and all others as specialized roles in the setting/plot.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CajunKhan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1477124-clan-tzimisce-is-the-least-interesting-clan?p=1477844#post1477844\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I disagree. They have been pushing the Anarchs and thinbloods hard. The idea that this is fundamentally a Camarilla game is over. In some ways I think even the idea that this is a vampire game is over. You are intended to play people who are barely vampires, fighting the REAL vampires. You are intended to play someone who barely has any powers, but also barely has a bane and has high humanity, who fights the vampires by exploiting the subtle advantages of having high humanity and barely any bane.</div> </div> </div> </div>Pretty much, yeah. Not exactly the point of the tangent, but this is the truth through and through.<br /> <br /> \u200b<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SetiteFriend</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1477124-clan-tzimisce-is-the-least-interesting-clan?p=1477854#post1477854\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Aside from Anarch being a main faction in V5, the edition has pushed for greater freedom between Clan and Sect. Especially considering how clans, especially the independents, were revamped into broad archetypes similar to the core 7.</div> </div> </div> </div>Regardless of my opinions on how some of this was done, that's absolutely true.<br /> <br /> Yet, for the purposes of saying what a core clan is, as I explained above, we still have the same 7 at the core and as the mainly developed for use as PCs. Even if less heavily handed in that regard.<br /> <br /> \u200b<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SetiteFriend</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1477124-clan-tzimisce-is-the-least-interesting-clan?p=1477854#post1477854\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is completely baseless. Though I'd love to see some text that somehow supports this.</div> </div> </div> </div>Same reason why we can say the Anarchs were already the heroes since 1st ed. Subtext. While the text does not directly says that you should play this or that or that there is a hero or a villain, it heavily implies possibilities and gives hints to the best &quot;solutions&quot; for the many &quot;problems&quot; it presents, along with rules that mechanically reward specific goals even if it never say you should take those goals as yours.<br /> <br /> 1st and 2nd editions paint a bleak existence for Vampires because they directly say that Vampires do politics and power plays, but the Jyhad is ultimately an unwinnable game. But the subtext is clear that <b><i>not playing the Jyhad</i></b> is an option and that you can &quot;win the game&quot; through that. V5 paints a world of even more terrible vampires than before struggling against equally terrible hunters, but Thin Bloods, while persecuted by everyone, get to bypass every single big obstacle and have an actual shot at achieving meaningful and lasting good for themselves or others.<br /> <br /> Vampire has always been shock full of subtext, and isn't particularly subtle about it. But if you just take everything you read at face value you may indeed not see it, as it is still subtext.<br /> <br /> \u200b<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SetiteFriend</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1477124-clan-tzimisce-is-the-least-interesting-clan?p=1477854#post1477854\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That might have been for Bloodlines 2, and I do dislike their choice of a Thin-Blood Protagonist there, even if it is for a small part of the game.</div> </div> </div> </div>I have nothing against it, it all depends on how the game works with it in the end.<br /> <br /> \u200b<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SetiteFriend</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1477124-clan-tzimisce-is-the-least-interesting-clan?p=1477854#post1477854\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thin Bloods do get some focus as they were the hot new thing of the edition.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thin Bloods have been a thing since forever in the game and got direct, clear rules focusing on them in 1999 with their titular book. It makes no sense whatsoever to say that they're V5's hot new thing. They're not.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SetiteFriend</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1477124-clan-tzimisce-is-the-least-interesting-clan?p=1477871#post1477871\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Because it is a new edition that does new things and expands on an older concept? The Caitif also get an expanded write-up in V5, was V5 originally going to be only Caitiff too?</div> </div> </div> </div>There are few if any new thing about the Thin Bloods in V5. Their mechanics and powers are basically based on their write-up in 1999's Time of Thin Blood. They're been playable basically <b>as presented</b> for 23 years, not just as a Flaw. The changes are more of an update of their rules than anything, and while mechanically different, TB Alchemy is clearly based on their original mechanics for developing weird unique powers.<br /> <br /> Now, if the game was ever meant to be TB-only, for now I can only say that this much seems to be unsubstantiated regardless of the attention given to them, but if unlikely, it is possible. I see no sense in arguing such rumors, though, as they seem really wild.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-04-02T02:04:35-07:00","id":1477888,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1477124-clan-tzimisce-is-the-least-interesting-clan?p=1477885#post1477885\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Nope, at least not for their main design.<br /> <br /> \u200bAs <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25886-kharnov\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"25886\" data-vbnamecard=\"25886\">Kharnov</a> nicely pointed out Dementation <b>is</b> a unique gimmick Discipline. But it isn't the original Malkavian Discipline from a game perspective. DA takes a completely different approach on the clans that makes it acceptable for the Malks to have a gimmick Discipline (in a sense it works on making all clans more gimmicky than their modern counterparts one way or another), and only Revised moved Dementation to the Core, but Revised did a lot of changes to mechanics here and there for metaplot reasons even in the core, so it is also following very distinct and specific design principles.<br /> <br /> For &quot;stable, metaplot-agnostic&quot; games, Malkavian was designed with Dominate.<br /> <br /> Thaumaturgy is an interesting case as it is limited in lore, but it is actually the core mechanic for &quot;Vampire Magic&quot; even if other magical Disciplines tried to stir away from it to some degree. Mechanically speaking, Thaumaturgy isn't simply Tremere Blood Magic, but the very core magic system for vampires. And as such, it is designed versatile, broad and stable as other Disciplines, even if specific Paths may not be so much.<br /> <br /> Yes, the lore makes it unique. But it isn't designed as just a limited, specialized gimmick.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm sorry I should have been clearer here. I was referring to the gangrel and Protean. if the core clans are the player clans protean qualifies since its uniquely gangrel and leans into animal clan gimmick.<br /> <br /> <br /> I was also referring to v5 blood sorcery rather than previous Ed Thaumaturgy. Were it feels more like a series of blood based powers than a magic rule set.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":26986,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","user":"Ragged Robin","date":". 04-02-2022, 09:37 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-04-02T02:16:56-07:00","id":1477889,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SetiteFriend</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1477124-clan-tzimisce-is-the-least-interesting-clan?p=1477878#post1477878\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That's not remotely what I said. Again, I meant that if that rumor even existed, it would make sense that it was for BL 2 and not V5<br /> <br /> <br /> It's a nonsensical comparison. One is a mistake in writing and lack of diversity reading, the other is deliberate choice in game direction. <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> They expanded with the Resonance System, Touchstones, Tenets and Convictions, Blood Potency, Loresheets, Predator Types, the Thin-Bloods and other stuff. They did more than just trim horrible amounts of bloat.<br /> <br /> Yes Thin-Blood get different mechanics, but how is that anyway indicative that &quot;v5 was initially going to be thin blood only&quot;. If anything, the way their mechanics are presented, they were added afterward, considering they follow standard mechanics for vampires unless otherwise stated, as quoted further below.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Their mechanics are. And this pedantism is irrelevant to the point &quot;v5 was initially going to be thin blood only&quot;.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> I disagree that it sticks out, if anything they provide an interesting midpoint to explore between humans and vampires.<br /> <br /> And they don't work completely different, to quote the Corebook &quot;Despite this, your thin-blood character is still fundamentally a vampire, and unless otherwise stated follows the same rules as other vampires in this book.&quot;<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> The Sabbat Book, released 3 years after the Corebook, is an indicative that &quot;v5 was initially going to be thin blood only&quot;?<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Gets what? Unique disciplines (Which is the opposite of making it new player friendly) and big chunks of books dedicated to them (which they do anyway? Especially since you are no longer talking about the Corebook) ?<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> &quot;Who did it better&quot; is not really what the discussion is about.</div> </div> </div> </div>Which would be even more extreme in my opinion. Extreme remodeling your game is one thing remodelling your game for a spin off product is quite another <br /> <br /> But do you get my point that absurd behavoir amd bad decisions isn't exactly out the norms in v5?<br /> <br /> True they did ad a lot of bloat to feeding but the game design intent is quite clear-streamline to personal horror, less 'gimmicks'. Then you've got this extra set of rules for a completly different supernatural stapled on. They even get a quirky gimmicky power set.<br /> <br /> It isn't pedantism, your argument is they're a new thing and that's why they get a load if stuff theyre not. They had unique mechanics for 23 years they're not a new thing either mechanically thematically or plot wise. They're just incredibly favoured this edition.<br /> <br /> They stick out strongly, distinct mechanics and thematic differences from all other player options in a edition which trimmed that put for everyone else.<br /> <br /> It isn't but it feeds into how focussed v5 is on thin bloods we're seeing this stuff pop up three years in. I could pick other examples but I went for the most extreme to make my point.<br /> <br /> Big chunks of writting and supplementary unique mechanics.<br /> <br /> True.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":26986,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","user":"Ragged Robin","date":". 04-02-2022, 09:35 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-04-02T09:47:27-07:00","id":1477905,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ragged Robin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1477124-clan-tzimisce-is-the-least-interesting-clan?p=1477889#post1477889\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> But do you get my point that absurd behavoir amd bad decisions isn't exactly out the norms in v5?</div> </div> </div> </div>It's still not comparable. &quot;They wrote an offensive section in a book, so it makes sense that they'd publish it exclusively in Swahili&quot; , &quot;They wrote an offensive section in a book, so it makes sense that they'd add chimerical damage as a game mechanic&quot; or &quot;They wrote an offensive section in a book, so it makes sense that they were originally changing the setting to Morrowind&quot;. How is &quot;They wrote an offensive section in a book, so it makes sense that they were originally only having Thin-Bloods&quot;. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> True they did ad a lot of bloat to feeding but the game design intent is quite clear-streamline to personal horror, less 'gimmicks'. Then you've got this extra set of rules for a completly different supernatural stapled on. They even get a quirky gimmicky power set. </div> </div> </div>&quot;Completely different supernatural&quot; &quot;Despite this, your thin-blood character is still fundamentally a vampire, and unless otherwise stated follows the same rules as other vampires in this book.&quot;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> It isn't pedantism, your argument is they're a new thing and that's why they get a load if stuff theyre not. They had unique mechanics for 23 years they're not a new thing either mechanically thematically or plot wise. They're just incredibly favoured this edition.<br /> <br /> They stick out strongly, distinct mechanics and thematic differences from all other player options in a edition which trimmed that put for everyone else. </div> </div> </div>Of course it is pedantism, I've clarified time and time again that I meant the mechanics of Thin-blood Alchemy and their Merits and Flaws being a new thing, not TBs <i>per se</i>. <br /> <br /> Also, since they've had unique mechanics for 23 years, it makes less sense that their mechanics being expanded means V5 was originally about them?<br /> <br /> Expanding on the above, the TBs having some different themes is intentional and part of why they get additional focus. Again, New editions sometimes try new things. Just because V5 cuts down on stuff doesn't mean they can't expand on old stuff too, adding new mechanics and systems, as I mentioned before.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> It isn't but it feeds into how focussed v5 is on thin bloods we're seeing this stuff pop up three years in. I could pick other examples but I went for the most extreme to make my point </div> </div> </div>They should have ignore Thinbloods then? Even though they are, following old metaplot even, supposed to be more common each night? They should have given them this focus you talk about in the corebook and then completely ignored them for the rest of the edition?<br /> <br /> Plus, they get 1 dedicated cult, 1 dedicated loresheet and 1 Path, plus a handful of formulas. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Big chunks of writting and supplementary unique mechanics. </div> </div> </div>Which makes since full-bloods have more in common with each other and so need less dedicated text to them.<br /> <br /> And again the idea that V5 was originally only been about thin-blood is clearly a baseless rumor. I have read the developers talk about things that were changed over the course of V5's development, like the Ministry originally joining the Camarilla, but TB being the main focus was never even mentioned.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27145-setitefriend","name":"SetiteFriend","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27145_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"255"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-04-02T09:54:10-07:00","id":1477906,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ragged Robin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1477124-clan-tzimisce-is-the-least-interesting-clan?p=1477888#post1477888\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'm sorry I should have been clearer here. I was referring to the gangrel and Protean. if the core clans are the player clans protean qualifies since its uniquely gangrel and leans into animal clan gimmick.<br /> <br /> <br /> I was also referring to v5 blood sorcery rather than previous Ed Thaumaturgy. Were it feels more like a series of blood based powers than a magic rule set.</div> </div> </div> </div>I do think you make a fair point about the fact that all of the other Disciplines found among the &quot;Core&quot; Clans can be found among multiple Clans. But Protean is more than just an &quot;animal&quot; power, it's a &quot;shapeshifting&quot; power, which is a pretty broad category, and a common archetype in vampire fiction. I think in this case they're just kind of painted into a corner, and don't have any &quot;Core&quot; Clans that they can give it to where it is as or more thematically appropriate than Disciplines they already have.<br /> <br /> Having taken a bit of time to look up the new V5 Blood Sorcery, I find the decision on how they've chosen to handle it... interesting. In most respects, they have simply made it more like the Blood Sorcery Disciplines found in VtR, where most of the wide array of powers available are exclusively found in Rituals, which I do like; it draws a greater distinction between &quot;regular&quot; Disciplines and Blood Sorcery. In recent years I've become more appreciative of having magic in games be treated more like how it was historically depicted, requiring preparation and ritual rather than just being a grab-bag of powers you can toss around at a moment's notice.<br /> <br /> But unlike VtR, they have given the Discipline itself a set of powers that don't require you to learn Rituals in order to use it, and those powers are indeed focused around blood and vitae specifically. I think this is supposed to represent two things. Firstly, the Path of Blood was frequently described as the Path that most Tremere were taught first, before branching out into other kinds of sorcery. And secondly, Blood Sorcery is also being used as a replacement for Quietus, which was also a Discipline with blood manipulation as its primary gimmick. It seems a bit clumsy to me, and I find it a bit odd having Blood Sorcery be a universal among the Banu Haqim when it was originally supposed to be the focus of just one branch, but I can see what they were trying to do.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25886-kharnov","name":"Kharnov","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"683"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-04-02T10:10:41-07:00","id":1477907,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1477124-clan-tzimisce-is-the-least-interesting-clan?p=1477885#post1477885\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u200bSame reason why we can say the Anarchs were already the heroes since 1st ed. Subtext. While the text does not directly says that you should play this or that or that there is a hero or a villain, it heavily implies possibilities and gives hints to the best &quot;solutions&quot; for the many &quot;problems&quot; it presents, along with rules that mechanically reward specific goals even if it never say you should take those goals as yours.<br /> <br /> 1st and 2nd editions paint a bleak existence for Vampires because they directly say that Vampires do politics and power plays, but the Jyhad is ultimately an unwinnable game. But the subtext is clear that <b><i>not playing the Jyhad</i></b> is an option and that you can &quot;win the game&quot; through that. V5 paints a world of even more terrible vampires than before struggling against equally terrible hunters, but Thin Bloods, while persecuted by everyone, get to bypass every single big obstacle and have an actual shot at achieving meaningful and lasting good for themselves or others.<br /> <br /> Vampire has always been shock full of subtext, and isn't particularly subtle about it. But if you just take everything you read at face value you may indeed not see it, as it is still subtext.</div> </div> </div> </div>Anarchs are certainly less heroes now, and Thin Bloods have different themes, a slightly easier shot at a mortal life and redemption being one of them.<br /> <br /> But the V5 is not about being the good guys at all. &quot;Perhaps your character tries desperately to hold on to vestiges of human morality despite the sordid demands of vampiric existence. Or maybe they have already adjusted their morality to their new condition...Using this game to explore moral questions and immoral acts can be interesting and emotionally meaningful.&quot; <br /> <br /> But I'm still waiting for the text (or subtext) that somehow supports this &quot;You are intended to play people who are barely vampires, fighting the REAL vampires. You are intended to play someone who barely has any powers, but also barely has a bane and has high humanity, who fights the vampires by exploiting the subtle advantages of having high humanity and barely any bane.&quot; <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27145-setitefriend","name":"SetiteFriend","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27145_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"255"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-04-02T11:25:01-07:00","id":1477912,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ragged Robin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1477124-clan-tzimisce-is-the-least-interesting-clan?p=1477888#post1477888\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm sorry I should have been clearer here. I was referring to the gangrel and Protean. if the core clans are the player clans protean qualifies since its uniquely gangrel and leans into animal clan gimmick.<br /> <br /> <br /> I was also referring to v5 blood sorcery rather than previous Ed Thaumaturgy. Were it feels more like a series of blood based powers than a magic rule set.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, my bad.<br /> <br /> But Protean is more of a case of badly written power than purposefully non-broad. Shapechanging is as much a traditional vampire power as possible, and Protean tries to cover all the spectrum of iconic transformation through its 5 levels. So I wouldn't really say it is a unique and niche gimmick, despite it being made unnecessarily rigid to the point of Snake-Themed Protean having to be mechanically its own Discipline.<br /> <br /> Requiem 2nd edition did it perfectly, and the V5 mechanic works far better for Protean, but its design purpose was clearly more aligned to the other main Disciplines.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SetiteFriend</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1477124-clan-tzimisce-is-the-least-interesting-clan?p=1477905#post1477905\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Of course it is pedantism, I've clarified time and time again that I meant the mechanics of Thin-blood Alchemy and their Merits and Flaws being a new thing, not TBs <i>per se</i>.</div> </div> </div> </div>It isn't in the sense that none of those mechanics is really new, despite you still claiming they are. None of the themes, either. ToTb had it all, all those mechanics (or equivalent ones just as detailed, but in need of a heavy update, which they got), all those themes. There's nothing new at all about them in V5 except being more common (which was expected).<br /> <br /> That said, though:<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SetiteFriend</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1477124-clan-tzimisce-is-the-least-interesting-clan?p=1477905#post1477905\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, since they've had unique mechanics for 23 years, it makes less sense that their mechanics being expanded means V5 was originally about them?</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree with this and personally I'm not aggravated by them in any way.<br /> <br /> While I do agree completely with the reading that the game is strongly centered on them, their depiction and rules by themselves, especially in the core, do not bother me and I actually liked a lot the idea of eliminating Generation differences among Thin Bloods (making them into kind of baseline, you can't really go lower than that). This last one, by the way, is the single rule on TB that is really new and unique to V5, and I think was a good idea for both lore and game design.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SetiteFriend</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1477124-clan-tzimisce-is-the-least-interesting-clan?p=1477907#post1477907\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But I'm still waiting for the text (or subtext) that somehow supports this &quot;You are intended to play people who are barely vampires, fighting the REAL vampires. You are intended to play someone who barely has any powers, but also barely has a bane and has high humanity, who fights the vampires by exploiting the subtle advantages of having high humanity and barely any bane.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>You'll keep waiting because it is by definition subjective enough that you can't see it if you keep taking direct assertions at face value. It is kind of a reading you don't make and aren't willing to make.<br /> <br /> And that's ok. It just means that our arguments on the matter will keep passing right through each other because we're just not talking the same language here. I at least won't try to further this line of thought, it would take an effort I'm not willing to make or even sure I can.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-04-02T12:48:05-07:00","id":1477918,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1477124-clan-tzimisce-is-the-least-interesting-clan?p=1477912#post1477912\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You'll keep waiting because it is by definition subjective enough that you can't see it if you keep taking direct assertions at face value. It is kind of a reading you don't make and aren't willing to make.</div> </div> </div> </div>Because this is how burden of proof works, you make a random claim and just say the other party just isn't interested in seeing things that way.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1477124-clan-tzimisce-is-the-least-interesting-clan?p=1477912#post1477912\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And that's ok. It just means that our arguments on the matter will keep passing right through each other because we're just not talking the same language here. I at least won't try to further this line of thought, it would take an effort I'm not willing to make or even sure I can.</div> </div> </div> </div>Defending someone else's random and unsubstantiated soapbox about Fifth Edition is indeed a fruitless discussion and there is no point in furthering it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27145-setitefriend","name":"SetiteFriend","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27145_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"255"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-04-02T17:01:11-07:00","id":1477932,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SetiteFriend</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1477124-clan-tzimisce-is-the-least-interesting-clan?p=1477918#post1477918\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Because this is how burden of proof works, you make a random claim and just say the other party just isn't interested in seeing things that way.<br /> <br /> Defending someone else's random and unsubstantiated soapbox about Fifth Edition is indeed a fruitless discussion and there is no point in furthering it.</div> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"color:#FF0000\"><b>Take a warning and leave the thread. If you have an issue with a poster, report them.</b></span><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-04-09T09:28:44-07:00","id":1478376,"title":"","content":"I never found the Tzimsce clan boring at all. Just dam hard to play in a worthy fashion in a game.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-04-09T13:04:52-07:00","id":1478410,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lysander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1477124-clan-tzimisce-is-the-least-interesting-clan?p=1478376#post1478376\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I never found the Tzimsce clan boring at all. Just dam hard to play in a worthy fashion in a game.</div> </div> </div> </div>What do you think hard about them in play?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-04-09T17:11:01-07:00","id":1478445,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1477124-clan-tzimisce-is-the-least-interesting-clan?p=1478410#post1478410\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What do you think hard about them in play?</div> </div> </div> </div>I can't say for them but for me it was being allowed to play them prior to V20 Anarchs Unbound as prior to that I frequently ran into the issue where I couldn't play them as the table would bar Sabbat Clans. Which really only barred the Tzimisce, Blood Brothers, Harbingers of Skull and Salubri Attritubes as everything else had non-Sabbat versions that were allowed. Hell there was one time where I couldn't even play an Old Clan because as far as the ST was concerned, Old Clan Tzimisce were isolationists that stay in Eastern European and would have no reason to be in the USA.<br /> <br /> Thankfully Anarchs Unbound <i>finally</i> undid that silly notion that there wouldn't have been Tzimisce that remained Anarch after the Convention of Thorns and that the mainline Clan isn't some hivemind of fleshcrafting fiends.<br /> <br /> The other issue I have run into is people abusing or going overboard with Fleshcrafting but usually that's also a case of the player running roughshot over a less experienced ST that could also happen with other Clans and Disciplines.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://youtu.be/_yBS2EZFduI?t=2m13s\" target=\"_blank\">Homo sapiens. What an inventive, invincible species. It's only a few million years since they crawled up out of the mud and learned to walk. Puny, defenceless bipeds. They've survived flood, famine and plague. They've survived cosmic wars and holocausts. And now, here they are, out among the stars, waiting to begin a new life. Ready to outsit eternity. They're indomitable. Indomitable.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/420-akatsukileader13","name":"AkatsukiLeader13","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar420_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1637"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-04-10T10:27:35-07:00","id":1478499,"title":"","content":"I found them hard because of how do you portray a clan member that makes an effort to be a alien monster divorced from human concerns","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-04-10T12:20:39-07:00","id":1478505,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lysander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1477124-clan-tzimisce-is-the-least-interesting-clan?p=1478499#post1478499\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I found them hard because of how do you portray a clan member that makes an effort to be a alien monster divorced from human concerns</div> </div> </div> </div>Except not every Tzimisce is an alien monster just like not every Toreador is an art-obsessed fop nor is every Gangrel some mangy loner that would prefer the wilderness to the cities.<br /> <br /> A stereotype does not encompass the entirety of Clan. There are plenty of Tzimisce that aren't vicious monsters or inhuman Metamorphists. Hell look at Dracula. While being an Elder he is less human than younger Kindred, he's not some inhuman monster that lives in a haven made of humans.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://youtu.be/_yBS2EZFduI?t=2m13s\" target=\"_blank\">Homo sapiens. What an inventive, invincible species. It's only a few million years since they crawled up out of the mud and learned to walk. Puny, defenceless bipeds. They've survived flood, famine and plague. They've survived cosmic wars and holocausts. And now, here they are, out among the stars, waiting to begin a new life. Ready to outsit eternity. They're indomitable. Indomitable.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/420-akatsukileader13","name":"AkatsukiLeader13","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar420_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1637"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-04-10T12:44:01-07:00","id":1478508,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lysander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1477124-clan-tzimisce-is-the-least-interesting-clan?p=1478499#post1478499\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I found them hard because of how do you portray a clan member that makes an effort to be a alien monster divorced from human concerns</div> </div> </div> </div>There are two parts to this answer. Firstly, all vampires are, to some extent, divorced from human concerns. They have concerns that are fundamentally inhuman, and there are human concerns that generally do not apply to them. Revenants are the only humans that can come even close to understanding the primal violent rage of a vampire's Beast. They do not need to worry about harm or sickness the way that humans do, because they cannot (themselves) get sick and can heal nearly any trauma that we can imagine so long as they have sufficient vitae. They are extremely resistant to many of the concerns that human beings have regarding the environment, such as hot or cold weather, while also being vulnerable to particular conditions like sunlight that a human would not normally need to be concerned with.<br /> <br /> Plenty of vampires outside of the Tzimisce Clan can adopt habits and practices fundamentally divorced from conventional human experience; this is why Nosferatu can set up warrens down in the sewers when the lack of hygiene would be a severe threat to any human attempting to do the same. Depicting the Tzimisces' aspired divorce from normal human concerns can be achieved by looking at what human concerns simply do not matter to them as vampires, and instead focusing on what concerns that the vampiric condition creates: &quot;food and shelter&quot; mean very different things for a vampire than they do a human.<br /> <br /> However, the other half of this equation is that most vampires cannot separate themselves from conventional human concerns entirely. Part of this has to do with the fact that most vampires hunt their prey by mingling with humans, which means that they generally need to be good at &quot;faking it&quot; even if they don't genuinely need to worry about things. If you dress like it's the middle of summer in the dead of winter simply because the cold cannot really harm you until it's capable of freezing you solid, you are going to stand out like a sore thumb. Similarly, vampires themselves may not need to care about hygiene for their own sake, but they need to consider the impact that it has on their hunting, from the more humourous example of stinking like an open sewer because showering isn't really necessary for your survival, to the more serious concern of becoming a plague-bearer if you pick up some kind of disease that cannot hurt you but can be passed on to your victims if you aren't careful.<br /> <br /> Moreover, I tend to view the Tzimisce opinion that they are fundamentally divorced from their pre-Embrace human condition to be one of their greatest intellectual errors. Given a long enough time period, they can eventually become truly inhuman monsters as old habits and opinions from life are overcome or erased by the habits and opinions that will develop in something with fundamentally different needs. But for the first few centuries of life, habits from your mortal life are likely to maintain an influence on your identity as a member of the undead, especially when some of those habits need to be maintained to keep up your cover while you hunt humans. Eventually you can become a proper Fiend that can stalk humans from the shadows and get the blood you need through the raw power of Disciplines rather than needing to mix and mingle with your human prey, but for a while you're going to need to be able to pretend to be human in order to get close enough to your victims. And even when your old mortal habits fade away, those abandoned mortal habits will still shape how your immortal habits have developed, because growth and change are processes of continuity. The truth is that most Tzimisce simply are not as fundamentally alien to the human condition as they like to imagine themselves, beyond the hoary old Methuselahs that only leave their hidden lairs to drain some unfortunate soul and toss them into a ditch before retiring to their haven to continue pursuing their mysterious goals.<br /> <br /> To depict the inhumanity of a Tzimisce, you don't need to imagine something fundamentally Other. You simply need to imagine how something human-like would develop given a different set of needs and priorities; the Tzimisce simply do this more actively than most other vampires.<br /> <br /> As a final thought, I imagine that the Tzimisce that are likely to become the most fundamentally different from humanity are the ones that are largely indifferent to it, because the ones actively striving to contrast themselves simply for the sake of it are more likely to simply end up a distorted mirror of the thing they are defining themselves against, rather than truly becoming something different.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25886-kharnov","name":"Kharnov","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"683"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-04-10T18:44:16-07:00","id":1478535,"title":"","content":"Ironically, as far as Tzimisce being interested in &quot;trans-vampirism&quot;/transhumanism/so forth, one of the better sources of inspiration I found for that angle ended up being the Ordo Dracul book from first edition Requiem. Its material on alchemical mysticism (both external and internal), embodying mystical archetypes, and finding ways to work around certain inherent vampire weaknesses ended up being the sort of things I had always wanted to see certain branches of the Tzimisce and the Path of Metamorphosis focus on. <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-04-10T18:54:02-07:00","id":1478536,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lysander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1477124-clan-tzimisce-is-the-least-interesting-clan?p=1478499#post1478499\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I found them hard because of how do you portray a clan member that makes an effort to be a alien monster divorced from human concerns</div> </div> </div> </div>The above posts on this are very good, I'll try to simplify it in four strategies:<br /> <br /> 1 - Don't do it. Unless you really want to go for the Necroscope reference in its most extreme depiction in DSotBH, you don't need to do the alien monster stuff to still deal with any or all the other aspects of the clan that you want, including dealing with clan mates that are already there;<br /> <br /> 2 - Overdo it embracing the difficulty, A.K.A. make a poser, someone who isn't nearly there but tries hard to pretend. Bonus points if the character go over-the-top on inhuman behavior to throw others off, and then hides to puke and cry;<br /> <br /> 3 - Go for detachment first and only add to it when you feel like it. Most &quot;alien thought&quot; in fiction is just the character being detached as if others were just artificial, as robots, dolls or something. Chose one metaphor and literally use it as a mental shortcut, every time you want to delve into the detachment stop and picture the other characters as if they were literally that (dolls, robots, imaginary) for yours;<br /> <br /> 4 - Look for inspiration on tales of people that stand off in the way that interests you the most. It may be some mental condition like Autism or OCD, it may be Cultural Shock, it may be the effect of some drug. But for this my best suggestion is to chose carefully and then dive into your chosen inspiration, not just copy a trope, movie or stereotype, but actually reach for the people that go through that and learn about them from them.<br /> <br /> You can also simply read Necroscope to copy the source material, if it is your thing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-04-14T09:08:37-07:00","id":1478845,"title":"","content":"Thanks for some of feedback folks.<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-04-14T20:34:30-07:00","id":1478887,"title":"","content":"I like the posthumanism of Metamorphosis, the mysticism of Auspex, the territorial monstrosity and the mad science, about the only part I don't like is the Bram Stoker inspired mockery of Eastern Europeans and Romani, but that can be side lined far easier from Tzim than from Ravnos, EDIT: Stoker may have meant to be 'fair for his day', that doesn't make it acceptable now.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25011,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25011-taggie","user":"Taggie","date":". 04-15-2022, 02:19 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25011-taggie","name":"Taggie","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1047"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-04-14T20:40:02-07:00","id":1478888,"title":"","content":"I don't really have a problem with the Tzimisce, though I will agree that the eastern-european stuff should be toned down.<br /> <br /> As for Vissicitude, why not make it, Protean, and Serpentis(refluffed depending on user) into a single &quot;branched&quot; discipline Like Quietus or Valeren. Have different bloodlines within the 3 clans develop along whichever of the 3 branches better fits.<br /> <br /> Lore-wise, the Gangrel, Tzimisce, and Settites are hinted at as being interrelated by multiple sources(see the set and osiris thread for examples). So slipping that in wouldn't require more than a few background tweaks.<br /> <br /> Character-wise, as others have pointed out protean fits more thematically with some of the tzimisce characters(and I'd argue serpentis would be perfect for making a Koschei inspired tzimisce). It'll also probably be easier on storytellers to accept Protean or Serpentis Tzimisce characters if they feel Vissicitude is overpowered.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6383-prometheas","name":"Prometheas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1101"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}